{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot","id":873174,"title":"Dragon Rekindled: The Orobori Chronicles (Embers Reboot)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-24T10:41:45-07:00","id":873174,"title":"Dragon Rekindled: The Orobori Chronicles (Embers Reboot)","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>DRAGON REKINDLED:<br /> THE OROBORI CHRONICLES</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">A reboot of the</span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development#post20836\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"> Dragon: The Embers</span></a></span></b></u><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"> Project</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <img src=\"https://s6.postimg.org/4s3vtpgu5/Skull.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Primary Development Thread</span></span></span></b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Released Material</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Current Releases</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">So far, we've only released an incomplete Transitional Ruleset, which is more suited to making changes to the old game. Please use the rules presented in the 2nd Edition of Dragon: The Embers as a baseline for everything here.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><u><b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zh8dFoBLbWksCZd6Bhw3hXOpDaUhBidcFKoGX04fR5Q/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Dragon Rekindled: Transitional Rulebook (rough draft)</span></a></b></u> - A fleshed-out rules-update from <i>Dragon: The Embers - Second Edition</i>.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><u><b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LANnga4YxfyD8uXYBnqV0EuzuNHYlSdTARZJKZgW8VM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Prototype Oroboros Sheet: Document Version</span></a></b></u> - Make a copy on Google Drive and edit it</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><u><b><a href=\"http://s6.postimg.org/bfsoay0e9/Sheet_Prototype.png\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Prototype Oroboros Sheet: Image Version</span></a></b></u> - To be printed as single page with no margins.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><u><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Byul0i9IXo_Pw5aaC9gCfJd7xmF179n_XSGstrVY00I/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">The Order of the Bloody Chalice</span></b></a></u> - Detailed description of a versatile and dangerous group of antagonists who hunt supernatural creatures down for extended life and power, and have the Oroboroi at the top of the list.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=906278#post906278\"><u><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Deep Ones (a quick writeup)</span></b></u></a> - A brief overview of Deep Ones written on the forum as the basis for the upcoming writeup.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Upcoming Releases</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">We're constantly working to develop, write, and release new material for the world of the Oroboroi. These are the next planned releases...</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Purviews and You</span></b> - A writeup on the divine powers which the Oroboroi have access to.</span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Antagonist Writeups</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">The Deep Ones</span></b> - Creatures from the depths of the Dreamtide, with powers that rival the Dragons.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Nightmares</span></b> - A common Antagonist encountered in the shallows of the Dreamtide.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Philosophy of Void: The School of Nihilists</span></b> - Antagonists from within the Oroboroi themselves.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: Part 1</b> - Player's Guide early draft</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Chapter 1: Fire of the Oroboroi</b></span> - Basic lore and concepts</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Chapter 2: The Rise to Power</b></span> - Detailed explanation of Methods and Philosophies</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Chapter 3: Anatomy of a Dragon</b></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> - Detailed Character Creation instructions</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Chapter 4: Playing an Oroboros</b></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> - Special Rules and Systems</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Chapter 5: Secrets of the Oroboroi</b></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> - Detailed lore for fleshing out a character</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Old / Outdates Releases</b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iaCVFntkf67nKB1vRWqKDkmW8dp8s4KsXMqZ6NWVauc\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Dragon Rekindled: A ReIntroduction</span></a></b></u> - A First-Look at Dragon Rekindled.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Thread Contents</span></b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Introduction to Dragon Rekindled (this post)</span></span></b></span></li> <li><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=873176#post873176\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>List of Changes, Currently Accepted Cannon, Frequently Asked Questions</u></span></span></span></a></b></li> <li><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=873177#post873177\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Detailed list of things that need to be done in that general order</u></span></span></span></a></b></li> <li><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=873178#post873178\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Who's Involved and how can you join them</u></span></span></span></a></b></li> <li><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=873179#post873179\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Recommended Reading for Understanding and Inspiration</u></span></span></span></a></b></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: A Re-Introduction</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i>This is a tale which all Orobori know...<br /> <br /> It is a memory imbued upon each and every Heart, by that first Original Sin so many eons ago...<br /> <br /> A memory from time immemorable, from a time when the world was different... A time when mankind were little more than animals...<br /> <br /> Long ago, Man lived as wanderers, beasts among the wilds, hunting and gathering for food, running from predators for survival, taking shelter in trees and caves to sleep. And as man slept, he dreamed...<br /> <br /> He dreamed of great ambitions, monsters, creatures of perfection...<br /> <br /> And from those dreams, in the place where all things imagined eventually flow to, the strongest and boldest answered the call, crawling forth from the Dreamtide, taking their place as the First Gods of Man...<br /> <br /> That primitive man had many words for them...<br /> <br /> Only one is used to today.<br /> <br /> <b>Dragons.</b><br /> <br /> The Dragons were creatures of divine perfection: the height of man\u2019s wildest imaginations. Some were great predators, who made the monsters of old tremble with their presence. Others were great tricksters, upon whom the oldest legends have been built. And some were great rulers, who pulled mankind out of his caves and built the first great civilizations. It is through the power of the Dragons that mankind began on the path that led him to what he is today...<br /> <br /> Strong...<br /> <br /> Dominant...<br /> <br /> Just like the Dragons...<br /> <br /> <br /> But man was a fickle child...<br /> <br /> It was not long before man grew bored, imagining new gods to cast the Dragons aside for, rebelling against and toppling their once proud rulers as the world fell once again into chaos. It was in the great vaults of their Dragon leaders that the rampaging mankind found the most prized, sheltered possessions of the Dragons... Their very Hearts.<br /> <br /> Men were driven mad at the sight of the Hearts, the very essence of Godhood itself before them. Great battles were fought for the hearts, not only through Might, but through Skill, Knowledge, Cunning, and Honor, many died trying to possess the great organs. But, when the battle was over, that was when mankind committed his act of greatest hubris, that great Sin against their First Gods...<br /> <br /> For Mankind wished not only to slay his gods,<br /> <br /> but to become unto them himself.<br /> <br /> It was at that moment that mankind devoured the very Hearts of those who had ruled them benevolently, and it was in that Original Sin that he was cursed: as he had devoured the Heart of a Dragon, so would his heart be devoured one day, in an endless cycle. That was the curse laid upon him by the Dragons, as the last of them died...<br /> <br /> That is the Curse of the Orobori, usurpers doomed to be usurped in an endless cycle, as each generation devours the last.<br /> <br /> The legacy of the Dragons was stolen, Unjust!<br /> <br /> The power of the Orobori was taken, Undeserved!<br /> <br /> The power to rule over mankind immortal...</i></span></span> <div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i>...comes with great weight of responsibility.</i></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><i>What Makes You Worthy?</i></span></span></b></div> <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://openclipart.org/image/300px/svg_to_png/215030/Ouroboros.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Orobori Chronicles</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">This project is a revitalization of <i>Dragon: The Embers</i>, a Dark Pack game based around the idea of the Orobori, humans who acquire the divine power of Dragons through the consumption of their hearts. In it, we will explore the darker side of Dragon, while expanding and refining the rules and lore for the post-GMC era.</span></span><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\">..</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Basic Lore</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The <b>Dragons</b> were creatures from the <b>Dreamtide</b>, a plane of pure imagination where the energy from man's hopes, dreams, and nightmares coalesces. The Dragons heard the dreams of mankind, and crawled out of the Dreamtide to eventually become their <b>First Gods</b>. They were responsible for the dawn of civilization, long before Atlantis. Man turned on them, however, and rose up and slew them, consuming their <b>Hearts</b> in what is known as the <b>Original Sin</b> of the <b>Orobori</b>. For their action, they are afflicted with the <b>Curse of the Orobori</b>, in which all Orobori are doomed to have their hearts devoured and be replaced, the cycle continuing for as long as the hearts exist...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Basic Gameplay</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Orobori power runs on <b>Breath</b>, the raw stuff of potential energy stored and burnt within the <b>Furnace</b> of their <b>Hearts</b>. Breath is gained from consuming sources of <b>Calories</b>, including (but certainly not limited to) food, and can be used for a wide variety of abilities, including the reconstitution of the physical form.<br /> <br /> They have access to numerous draconic traits called <b>Ablutions</b>, which can be manifested and added to their forms nearly at will. Manifesting all Ablutions turns activates <b>True Form</b>, in which they take the full shape of a Dragon, giving them extensive new abilities.<br /> <br /> The most powerful powers the Orobori have Access to are <b>Purviews</b>, manifestations of &quot;divine&quot; power which allows them impose their will directly on reality. This, along with <b>Dream Sorcery</b>, are powers derived directly from the Dreamtide, and often have strict limitations or hefty costs associated with them.<br /> <br /> All Orobori suffer from the effects of <b>Reimagining</b>: an Orobori known to many will quickly find her form affected by the minds of the people who believe in her. This can result in changes to their powers, form, and even their personality. These changes can be for better or for worse, as it is just as easy for the Orobori to lose a useful trait as it is to gain one. Their susceptibility is dependent on their <b>Hubris</b> or <b>Guilt</b>, an integrity scale based on how they handle the powert usurped.<br /> <br /> The Orobori also have to rely on their small numbers to keep hidden, as their form of supernatural veiling is relatively weak: humans who see them in True Form see just that, and are not supernaturally terrified, and will likely be able to recall it later. They also show up clearly on camera. Their only defense is that humans who are completely unaware of the supernatural will begin to question whether it was real or imagined over time, and their surreal appearance makes the camera footage look fake. This is all weak against people who already believe that they could exist, and completely useless against the insane or people who are on drugs, who lack the internal inhibitions which tell them not to believe this.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, the Orobori are an extremely hearty set of creatures: immune to extreme heat and cold, able to walk through burning buildings unscathed, without any real \u201cvital organs\u201d for a would-be assassin... Their only real weaknesses are their Heart and their connection to it. If a Dragon\u2019s heart is eaten or destroyed, they die in short order unless they find a new one.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b>Antagonists</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Orobori are in a bit of an odd situation: unlike other supernatural creatures, they don't have a niche. They do have a strong connection to <b>Dreams</b>, making them effective against <b>Nightmares</b>, and are potentially very hardy in general. They also don't get along nicely with <b>Beasts</b>, <b>Leviathans</b>, or <b>Angels</b>. Anything can be quarry for the Oroboroi however, if they see it as a worthy use of their power, and anything which threatens what they hold dear is a threat worth fighting.<br /> <br /> <b>Slayers</b>, humans who hunt for hearts, can also be a problem for the Orobori, for obvious reasons: all Orobori know this from the fact that they were once Slayers themselves, and are cursed to the fate they brought upon another in an endless cycle.<br /> <br /> Perhaps more terrifying are <b>Heart Eaters</b>, Orobori who've become addicted to the consumption of other's hearts. Orobori who rise to this level of hubris run the risk of becoming out-of-control monsters. Creatures of lesser intellect than humans, who lack an idea of what a Dragon should be, who consume a heart often find themselves consumed by its powers, and are transformed into hideous monstrosities called <b>Chimera</b>. The worst among the Oroboroi, however, are the nihilistic <b>Scholars of Void</b>, who have found no constructive use for their power and so use it to destroy reality for spite and entertainment.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, the Oroboroi must also contend with horrible things left over from the time of the Dragons, such as the reality-bending <b>Deep Ones</b>, who can add concepts to their form at will, and the the <b>Knights of the Bloody Chalice</b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, who use dream sorcery to gain immortality through the blood of both humans and supernatural creatures, and find the Oroboroi particularly potent. The most terrifying of all the threats they face, however,</span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">are </span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">by far</span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> the <b>Old Gods</b>, mysterious beings from before the Dragons who sleep somewhere outside of the reality they know.<br /> <br /> An Orobori Chronicle can go in any direction really, from intrigue, to monster hunting, to delving into forgotten lore, but one theme is central: power. The Oroboroi are all about taking and using power for ends which they believe strongly in, and the things they end up undertaking are epic.</span></span> <div align=\"center\"> <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/j0ghlknwh/Dream_Portal.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 06-24-2017, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:43:21-07:00","id":873176,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Changes from 2nd and 3rd edition</b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Focus and Theme</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Leadership to Power</b> - Oroboroi are no longer bound to the strict take on Leadership. I<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">nstead, Dragon focuses on the broader view of Power and what is done with it: it's a game about going mad with power. </span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Responsibility, Worthiness, and the &quot;Divine Mandate&quot; take on a new tone and meaning here.</span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Dominionists still use the old concept.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Darkness</span></span></span></span></b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - Toning up the darker elements, specifically looking into overuse of power, threats to power, and the constant feeling of never having enough power. Also, the dark-fantasy elements are getting darker.</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Corruption and Usurpation</b> - The rise and fall from power is based on a spiral of corruption.</span></span></span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Backstory Elements</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Old Gods</b> - The deal with the Old Gods is no longer part of the origin story: Dragons were always immortal, and the &quot;Old Gods&quot; are sleeping cosmic horrors.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dragons and Deep Ones</b> - Are fleshed out as ancient beings from the deep Dreamtide.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Divine Mandate</b> - &quot;Divine Mandate&quot; was a concept which applied to the Dragons, and is no longer directly tied to Oroboroi behavior.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Dominionists still use the old concept.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dominion</b> and <b>Collapse</b> are a bit more complex and take in more allusions to story of Eden in Genesis and Paradise Lost. Also Nietzsche.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Reptilian Conspiracies</b> - The Reptilian Conspiracies (name in question) which formed in the centuries after Collapse are a new addition which shed light to Oroboroi behaviors and beliefs over the decades, and how they interact on a global scale.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The <b>Dominionists</b> represent the old concepts of Divine Mandate and Kingship.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Terms and Definitions</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Furnace to Heartstring</b> - \u201cFurnace\u201d is now \u201cHeartstring\u201d, to signify that it is not a property of the Heart itself, but its connection to the Oroboros.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Integrity is Conviction</b> - &quot;Mandate&quot; or &quot;Ethics&quot; is now &quot;Conviction&quot;, to reflect the new focus on Worth rather than a specific view of leadership.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Edicts to Purviews</b> - &quot;Edicts&quot; have been morphed into &quot;Purviews&quot;, which are a manifestation of the Oroboros's highest ideal. Also, &quot;Laws&quot; are now &quot;Impositions&quot;.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Maidens, Hoards, and Provinces</b> - Now represent a different set of mechanics.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Miasma</b> - Now refers to the mist of chaos which is in Pandemonium. The barrier between the Waking and Dreamtide is now called the &quot;<b>Ora</b>&quot;.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>World Elements</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dream Sorcery</b> - Brings Dreamtide powers into the Waking.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Dreamtide</b> - Expanded concept. This has always been another view of the &quot;Astral&quot;, &quot;Dreaming&quot;, or &quot;Primordial Dream&quot;, but now we have the Dragon / Dream Sorceror's perspective. The Dreamtide mimics an actual sea, and has &quot;tides&quot;, &quot;islands&quot;, and &quot;currents&quot;.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Ora</b> - The barrier which creatures going by this logic must cross.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Shoals</b> - .</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Islands</b> - .</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Pandemonium</b> - The bottom of the Dreamtide where things to go die.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Treasury</b> - The &quot;Treasury&quot;, which replaced the Dreamtide in the 3rd Edition, is now on the &quot;far shore&quot; of the Dreamtide, making exploiting it a higher-level affair.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Antagonists</b> - The <b>Knights of the Bloody Chalice,</b> <b>Deep Ones</b>, <b>Nightmares</b>, and <b>Usurpers</b> are being much more thoroughly fleshed out: they will have their own sets of mechanics, character sheets, and advice to Storytellers.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mechanics</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Dreamtide Travel and Manipulation are now part of a merit called &quot;Dream Sorcery&quot;, which can be gained by non-Oroboroi occultists, and require Blood, Breath, Willpower, or Jadeite.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Breath is gained by eating things, like in 2nd edition, but now basic nutritional requirements must also be filled.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The integrity stat is now a sideways system called &quot;Conviction&quot;, and the extremes to fall into are Hubris (the hoarding, rampaging dragon) and Guilt (the human who is no longer worthy of their Heart).</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oroboroi start with 12 Ablutions: 3 from the Method, 3 from the Common, 3 from any Oroboros list, and 3 from the Storyteller's discretion.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ablutions can now be gained and lost as a result of public opinion through a process called \u201cThe Reimagining\u201d.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">There is now an Ablution list with stuff that the Oroboroi only have access to through external means such as the Reimagining.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oroboroi are now completely immune to fire, except in Human Guise, which is burned away to reveal the Dragon beneath.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Heart Creation</b> - We're talking about this: it <i>will</i> be a fleshed out element in the new book.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Pending Changes</b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Slayers, Dragonborn, Pilot Lights, and Deep Ones will have their own sheets and rulesets.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">There's gonna be WAY more stuff to pull with the mysterious and alien Deep Ones, whose connection to the Dragons will be revealed by the end of the book.</span></span></span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Accepted Cannon</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The Dreamtide is basically a place that is created by man's thoughts, and can be crossed over to through dreams. It flows through many realms of imagination, but ends up in a place known as Pandemonium: this is where the Dragons were born from. The Dragons were formed from the dreams of man, came to life, and pulled themselves out of the Dreamtide. After doing that, they assumed various positions of legend and leadership and kick-started civilization as we know it. The Dragons were naturally immortal: as long as their heart remained, they could always reform. Humans eventually got tired of this and turned on them, killed them, and consumed their undying hearts. Doing so transformed them into human-dragon hybrids, and left them with a curse that they would be usurped in the same way. Thus, they are called the Orobori.<br /> <br /> All Orobori are made through this process, in what is known as the First Sin: the act of killing another for access to godlike powers. The Oroboroi become what they are through a process known as the Metamorposis, in which their body is remade in the form of a Dragon based on their ideals, and has access to their old human body, referred to as the Human Guise, which is mostly indistinguishable from the way it used to be. Other than the Human Guise, Dragons only have their unbelievable existence and small numbers to hide their existence from the general population.<br /> <br /> Oroboroi are rare, and seldom see each other, thus, it is hard for them to form cohesive social groups beyond the few others in an area. They do, however, know how to make deals with other supernatural entities, such as Vampires and Werewolves. This is good, because they have many antagonists, such as Nightmares, other Oroboroi, the mysterious Deep Ones, and the Slayers who seek to usurp them. They must also deal with the constant urges for greatness and hubris.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Frequently Asked Questions</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Nothing here yet.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-30-2016, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:43:53-07:00","id":873177,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Detailed list of things that need to be done in that general order</b></span></span></span> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Rebuild 2nd edition</span></span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Take 2nd edition cannon and 3rd edition GMC mechanics, and build a new, transitional book.</span></span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Get sample characters of each archetype to see what people want to do.</span></span></span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Have people write out character concepts without knowing what the complete book has</span></span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Start writing Orobori Chronicles</b></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Start playtesting</span></span></span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Plan and run straightforward campaign</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Make characters based on methods, one of each</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Start with intros</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Run the characters meeting and forming a group</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Do some fights</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mystery: there is a nightmare attacking people. It turns out to be working with a lucid dreamer/dreamwalker in the physical world, he's trying to pull an inception, it's trying to get out.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">More action: bang them up against Werewolves, Vampires, and Changelings</span></span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Try out new concepts in the main campaign</span></span></span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Finish writing Orobori Chronicles</span></span></span></b></li> </ol><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Current Workload</b></span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Antagonist Releases</span></span></span></span></b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"> - Several page writeups on Nightmares, Deep Ones, and Nihilists, written for Chapter 7.<br /> <b>Purviews and You</b> - Information on new Purview rules and a mostly-complete list of them.<br /> <b>Chapter 2: The Rise to Power</b> - A draft of the chapter which has the Methods and Philosophies listed<br /> <b>Dragon Rekindled: Chapters 0 - 5 </b>- A draft of the rest of the chapters of the book needed to create new player characters</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 06-24-2017, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:44:42-07:00","id":873178,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Who's Involved, and </span><span style=\"color:#B22222\">how</span><span style=\"color:#B22222\"> can you join them.</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">We have a large, diverse group working on various parts of the project. We're currently holding at least one meeting a week, based on when the most people can be available, to discuss material being written and push progress. These generally start <b>between 4:00 and 5:00 PM US-Eastern Time</b>, and are non-mandatory. Other than that, we chatter over Skype regularly.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Current Project Members</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Raccoon (RockstarRaccoon)</b> - Project Lead</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=885381#post885381\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Darinas</b></span></a></u> - Writer<br /> <u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=931098#post931098\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Leleil</b></span></a></u> - Writer<br /> <u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=991006#post991006\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Mr Feral</b></span></a></u> - Writer / Editor<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Inactive Members</b></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=874170#post874170\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>CJC (CJC)</b></span></a></u> - Original Artist - Creative Consultant, Art</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=874338#post874338\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>AJF115</b></span></a></u> - Lore Writer<br /> <u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=874568#post874568\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Saulot (SaulottheGentle)</b></span></a></u> - Technical Writer</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=880928#post880928\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Nova (NovaP)</b></span></a></u> - Writer</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Shock</b> - Original Project Head - Creative Consultant, Lore, Writer</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Needed Members</b></span></span></span><br /> Brainstorming members are always welcome, but we're also looking for the following official staff to help with things.<br /> <br /> <b>Writers</b> - We need strong writers, both Fantastical AND Technical, to help build the book.<br /> <br /> <b>Artists</b> - The book should have as much art as possible. If possible, we\u2019d like to have art similar to the Werewolf The Apocalypse 20th Anniversary Edition.<br /> <br /> <b>Playtesters</b> - We need strong forum roleplayers to write up character sheets and eventually go on the official testing campaign, as well as experienced GMs to run their own games and tell us what\u2019s going on with them.<br /> <br /> Note that working on the book has some reading and training / exercise before hand: it may take a week before you end up editing release material.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>How to Join</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Reply to this thread (not in a PM) with the following format</span></span></span> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The bolded phrase \u201c<b>Team Application</b>\u201d at the top of the post, so I can see it.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The <b>specific position</b> you\u2019re applying for, so I know what I'm about to look at.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>A sample of your own work</b>, so I know what I'm bringing in.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Artists</b>: Draw and post a relevant Picture (does not to be colored or complete, jsut a sample of your style: a sketch is fine)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Writers</b>: Write me something about the Orobori</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Playtesters</b>: A 1 paragraph character concept</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">A list of qualifications</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Brief explanation of what you want to be involved in and why.</span></span></li> </ol><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">These will not only be accepted on whether or not you do them, but also on whether or not you're a competent writer. I'm doing it this way because I need people who can 1) make themselves public, 2) follow instructions, and 3) show me that they're not going to write weird gibberish if I give them access to the docs. That being said, <b>you don't HAVE to be good at anything creative to be eligible</b>: we need people to draw the borders and symbols, and we need writers to work on basic mechanics.<br /> <br /> <b>The standard for being accepted is low: simply being able to put forward something competent, even with guidance, is more important than being able to build a masterpiece</b>.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>One last thing...</b></span></span></span><br /> Stop apologizing to me. Goddamn, you people. I have no idea why this is becoming a thing now. I mean, I know I can be blunt and sometimes sound abrasive, but I'm actually never mad or upset about anything. It's really unnecessary...</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 06-24-2017, 12:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T10:45:47-07:00","id":873179,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Suggested Reading for Understanding and Inspiration.</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>For the enrichment of Team Members, prospective Storytellers, and general fans.</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The following media factors heavily into this game's concepts, and you should have an understanding of at least some of these things before you join the team. I don't care if you just read the <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Wikipedia articles, or the Cliff's Notes versions, but these are not only useful from the standpoint of Dragon Rekindled, but will make you a better storycrafter in general.</span> Note that <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">effectively tying some of the more serious ones into any otherwise-competent application is a good way to get it accepted.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Philosophy / Metaphysics</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Philosophy has always played a major role in </span>World of Dark<span style=\"font-family:georgia\">ness, and anything can apply, but these are the big ones here.</span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Socrates and Plato</b> - Pretty much anything by these guys is great material for anything set in the World of Darkness. Stuff like Justice, The Cave, and Platonic Forms are prime examples of content which the whole setting is based on.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Confucius</b> - Shock and CJC have mentioned that his writings factored heavily into 1st and 3rd edition.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Machiavelli's &quot;The Prince&quot;</b> - In which a very intelligent man practically BEGS Lorenzo Di'Medici to violently conquer Italy for it's own good, laying out a cold pragmatism that reshaped politics. If the connection isn't obvious, you need to take a look at the earlier editions of Dragon, and perhaps anything else set in the World of Darkness.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Rene Descartes</b> - Talks about perfection, existence of mind, and the nature of the Christian God's existence. Heavily referenced in the Secret Lore too.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Friedrich Nietzsche</b> - The concepts of Self Actualization and Will to Power, the scathing rebukes of Nihilism, and the fact that the Oroboroi are basically Ubermensch, all factor in really well. Some of this stuff is even directly referenced in the current material.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Alister Crowley</b> - I don't think it's possible to write World of Darkness and not know who this guy is. You don't have to stick a pyramid on your head or anything, just understand his mindset: he was a real-life Occultist, trying to give meaning to what he perceived as supernatural events around him. This mindset, that even the supernatural can be boiled down to the mundane, is essential for writing paranormal fiction and dark fantasy. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ayn Rand</b> - The concepts of the need for Self-Actualization to give life Worth are a large chunk of what the Hubris and Guilt are about. The Randian hero is the epitome of what a determination, a leg-up, and a bit of hubris can get a person. Obviously, Ayn Rand plowed head-on into Hubris, going so far as to condone genocide, so there's that too.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Anton LaVey</b> - The inverse of Rand, who thought that the world was just, therefore man must be brutal, LaVey had the more sobering belief in a brutal and unfair universe. Also, he wrote a bit on Crowley, so there's that.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>David Icke</b> - An Occultist second, a Conspiracy theorist first. Best known for the idea that shapeshifting reptilians from another world control the governments through fake personas, gaining powers through magical means. He also talks about the power of the dream world and the idea that we only see a small part of reality. Sound familiar?</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Science and History</b></span></span></span><br /> A good World Builder can take their fantastical elements and boil them down into the mundane, and can build metaphors from reality. It's good to have a backing.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Richard Dawkin's writings on Evolution and Memes</b> - I am not joking. A HUGE amount of the secret lore requires a basic understanding of these concepts. You will get lost if you do not know them. Make sure you understand how evolution actually works, and the awful realities which people like Dawkins are pointing out, because the process of evolution is a real-life-horror-story that makes Cthulhu seem pass\u00e9. Memes are heavily important to the ideas of a society, and especially creatures based on imagination.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Warring States Period</b> - For 200 years, China was basically a place of constant warfare between the various warlords, who had to band together or be annihilated when outsiders like the Mongols attacked, until the Quin Dynasty conquered everyone. This is how Oroboroi society sometimes functions.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Psychology</b> - Just... Anything. Including the disproven stuff and the Pseudoscience. This is a huge chunk of the Dreamtide.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Mythology / Culture</b></span></span></span><br /> Legends are very important to a game about Living Legends.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>A wide amount of material on Dragons</b> - There's not much specific to be reccomended here, just the understanding that there are vastly different accounts of Dragons, from the Western monsters, to the Asian serpents, to the Coatls described in South American mythology. They're a pretty common concept.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Gilgamesh</b> - The dude was an ass-kicking machine, a king to boot, and was full of Hubris. He was exactly what an Oroboroi can strive to be.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Heracles</b> - The story of a man with godlike powers trying to simply be a good man in the face of strife. Also, Hera is the bitchiest bitch in the universe.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Beowulf</b> - Also an ass-kicking machine, and a Slayer on top of that.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Old Testament / The Torah</b> - Specifically Genesis. The Bible is one of the most widely published but least read books, and it's a HUGE part of our culture. The themes discussed in Genesis were a heavy inspiration for the portrayal of the Dominion and Collapse stories.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>St George</b> - The most iconic Slayer in Western Folklore.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Modern Fiction</b></span></span></span><br /> I'm sure we've all seen far too much of this, so I'll be specific.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Paradise Lost</b> - The story of Genesis... From the perspective of Satan and the people around him. Once again, the story of Eden is a huge influence on how the Dominion and Collapse stuff is portrayed.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Fate Zero: The Meeting of Kings</b> - I'm really not a fan of anime, but this scene blew me away: Gilgamesh, Alexander the Great, and King Arthur all sit around a keg of ale and talk about what a King should be. This is Nasu at his best, and the relevance is obvious.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Gordon R Dickson's &quot;Dragon Knight&quot; Series</b> - It's about a guy from the 1970s who becomes a Mage and gets the power to turn into a Dragon, and get this, he actually stops to give <i>rational explainations</i> for what would otherwise seem fantastical, to the point that the most insane things don't even touch your disbelief. It's an awesome series by a prolific Science-Fantasy author, and if you like the idea of humans becoming Dragons, you should read it.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>David Icke's Reptilian Conspiracy Theory</b> - Ok, so, technically more conspiracy theory than &quot;fiction&quot; per say, (and if you look at Hillary Clinton and Ted Cruz, perhaps even believable), but seriously? The idea that there are lizard-people trying to run the government is <i>dripping</i> with Oroboroi potential.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dragonheart</b> - A movie about leadership, reponsibility, and dragons. This was mentioned in the Embers books, and it needs to be mentioned again here.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dark Kingdom: The Dragon King</b> - Based on a few Norse and German epics, this is the story of a man who kills a dragon, bathes in its blood to gain its powers, and is laid low by greed, treachery, and dark magic. It's exactly what the life-cycle of an Oroboros is about.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Other White Wolf Books</b></span></span></span><br /> Obviously, the more the better, but these stand out the most...</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mage: The Awakening</b> - This is probably the most important book to understand if you want to write things into the World of Darkness. The Mages have the most clear and verifiable understanding of what's actually going on, as well as the physics which REALLY govern what's going on. We're assuming the lore of Mage to be the closest to the reality of what's going on in the World of Darkness.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Vampire: Requiem and/or Masquerade</b> - Tells the story of immortal beings who must eat to survive, and harbor a snarling beast within their chests. <i>Sound familiar?</i></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Werewolf: The Forsaken</b> - They change into monsters. They have access to a realm of symbolism and power that mortals cannot fathom. Who does that sound like?</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Changing Breeds</b> - Always a good second-source on the idea of a shape-shifter.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Scion: Hero, Demigod, God, and everything else</b> - The Scion trilogy is a beautifully crafted set of books, which we are going to take heavy inspiration from for our own formats. The concepts of demigods fighting secret battles among humans in order to prove their worth is perfect fodder for <i>Dragon Rekindled</i>.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Beast: The Primordial </b>- Infamously, this has been heavily compared to Dragon, though it is an entirely different book. There are some similar underlying concepts, which are useful to know, and it's an interesting take on what one can do with Dream-based powers.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse, 20th Anniversary Edition</b> - You don't have to read it, but just LOOK at this thing: this is what a good World of Darkness book SHOULD look like, and it's the standard we're aiming for.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <i> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Notice: Referencing a certain, sub-par, heavily-overrated &quot;roleplaying&quot; &quot;game&quot; which purports to be about dragons living in dungeons is grounds for a kick in the face.</span></span></b></i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 06-27-2017, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T14:36:05-07:00","id":873294,"title":"","content":"Um... Question: Are we keeping Edicts? Because I don't see any mention of them and I personally think that their fluff as the Oroboros calling down the power of the Dreamtide and making a small part of the world essentially a waking dream in which they are the dreamer is both interesting and fitting for the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T22:26:44-07:00","id":873543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=873294#post873294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... Question: Are we keeping Edicts? Because I don't see any mention of them and I personally think that their fluff as the Oroboros calling down the power of the Dreamtide and making a small part of the world essentially a waking dream in which they are the dreamer is both interesting and fitting for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>YES. THAT IS A THING THAT IS STILL IN THERE.<br /> <br /> I forgot to add it here. I'll do that...<br /> <br /> Edit: Done. Though I'm calling it Purviews for now, because I want to try out that term...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 04-25-2016, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T23:55:09-07:00","id":873564,"title":"","content":"Another question: How are we going to be dealing with the interactions of the Astral Realms and the Dreamtide? Are they going to be just different names for the same thing? Are they completely independent planes? Is it only the Dreamtide that exists?<br /> <br /> And it has to be said, I preferred Edicts to Purviews. The word sounds more immediate and forceful. Also, a purview is '<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">the scope of the influence or concerns of something', as opposed to an Edict, which is 'an official order or proclamation issued by a person in authority'. I just think that Edict fits better. You know what they say about fixing things that aren't broken.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-25-2016, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T05:24:45-07:00","id":873678,"title":"","content":"I find it almost funny how the Orobori, despite being possibly the closest Kin that Beasts have apart from other Beasts, have such a bad relationship with them. I can understand why, what with all the terrorising, but it still strikes me as kind of amusing. Although I could see a place for a Nemesis in a Oroboros' Province. Can you say 'chief enforcer'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T05:58:27-07:00","id":873694,"title":"","content":"If it helps for inspiration, the Princess the Hopeful Dreamlands are basically the same as the Mage's Astral Realms, just seen through a different lens. In this case, the lens is the Supernatural Template in use. The best article I can find on this is at the bottom of this wiki page. Maybe Dragon could do something similar to this?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://princesswod.wikia.com/wiki/The_Dreamlands\" target=\"_blank\">http://princesswod.wikia.com/wiki/The_Dreamlands</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T06:18:08-07:00","id":873701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=873678#post873678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it almost funny how the Orobori, despite being possibly the closest Kin that Beasts have apart from other Beasts, have such a bad relationship with them. I can understand why, what with all the terrorising, but it still strikes me as kind of amusing. Although I could see a place for a Nemesis in a Oroboros' Province. Can you say 'chief enforcer'?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not that strange. They're similar because they're equal and opposites.<br /> <br /> Beasts are creatures of the Primordial Dream of the id, dragons the Bright Dream of the superego. The two are just close enough to recognize what the other wants is the exact opposite of the world they thrive in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T09:03:08-07:00","id":873801,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Dragons, Beasts, and Deep Ones are all in the same sort of Clade of sentient Dreamtide creatures. Dragons and Beasts don't get along because Dragons and Nightmares don't get along and what is a Beast but a Nightmare in human form?<br /> <br /> And Yes, the Dreamtide, Astral, Dreamlands, and Primordial Dream are all the same place through different perspectives.<br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If anyone wants to <b>join the project</b>, please say so, and I'll try to have a Skype meeting at some point this week...</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T09:13:13-07:00","id":873815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=873801#post873801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyway...<br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If anyone wants to <b>join the project</b>, please say so, and I'll try to have a Skype meeting at some point this week...</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Did you get the PM I sent you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:29:05-07:00","id":873860,"title":"","content":"uh, no. lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T16:28:46-07:00","id":874098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=873801#post873801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Dragons, Beasts, and Deep Ones are all in the same sort of Clade of sentient Dreamtide creatures. Dragons and Beasts don't get along because Dragons and Nightmares don't get along and what is a Beast but a Nightmare in human form?<br /> <br /> And Yes, the Dreamtide, Astral, Dreamlands, and Primordial Dream are all the same place through different perspectives.<br /> <br /> Anyway...<br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If anyone wants to <b>join the project</b>, please say so, and I'll try to have a Skype meeting at some point this week...</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>PM the time me and I'll see if I will able.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T19:01:56-07:00","id":874170,"title":"","content":"I've prepared nine illustrations thus far, which I thought I'd share to get the creative process rolling.<br /> You can view and download them from a folder in my Google Drive:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B31Gud9WnwZXSzA0SV9DTTR5ZGs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B31Gud9WnwZXSzA0SV9DTTR5ZGs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B31Gud9WnwZXSzA0SV9DTTR5ZGs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B31Gud9WnwZXSzA0SV9DTTR5ZGs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You might notice that most of these are colorized versions of the images present in the third-phase &quot;Christmas in July&quot; document. I felt it would be a good idea to make some artwork available to the project quickly, and this was the best means of doing so. I've restricted coloration to dragon images and I've cut out anything remotely related to humans in the artwork; my style is not conducive to the more realistic human portrayals employed by official Onyx Path documents, and rather than trying to change myself to suit that purpose I've decided to stick to my strengths. While this might seem like it would cause a disjoint in the visual aesthetic of the book (in regards to whosoever draws human images), I feel the sharp break between partial dragon and all dragon is appropriate for the themes of the template.<br /> <br /> I'm going to go into some of the motivation for individual illustrations. Consider skimming past it the cost of using them.<br /> <br /> <b>Cruiser Dragon</b><br /> This illustration was the first crafted of a set intended to emphasize the difference in scale that various Degrees of Divinity represented. The idea of a dragon being roughly the size of a family vehicle lends itself to said dragon LIFTING a family vehicle. I started this illustration as a margin filler but did not finish before the July 25th deadline, so it never made it into the book.<br /> <br /> <b>Dragon Versus Phoenix</b><br /> This image should be familiar; it is one of my micro-doodles (a style of which I am particularly fond) and was intended as an attempt to introduce that style to the book. Had it been well-received more images like this would have followed; the project didn't run long enough to find out, though. Since Raccoon is now deciding what is usable and what is not, I will be supplying more images like this in future to serve as text breaks.<br /> The dragon depicted is the same one present in &quot;Wing Shroud Dragon&quot;, and the Phoenix is intended to be the same as that in &quot;Enraged Phoenix&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Enraged Phoenix</b><br /> This is a brand new illustration, intended to refresh my familiarity with the style of my other Embers work. I also felt it would be a good idea to depict what I was picturing as a major antagonist. In the event the Phoenixi do not make it to the final cut of the game, the illustration might still be used as an Oroboros (since they define their appearance by their own perceptions, it would be easy for one to take the form of a phoenix).<br /> Interestingly enough, I briefly considered making all female dragons Phoenixes, as that is the mythology attached to the Chinese Phoenix. While that would have certainly helped with depicting a clear gender for the images, I decided it wasn't a good fit for this project.<br /> <br /> <b>Fido Chimera</b><br /> Another new illustration, this drawing was more off-the-cuff than Enraged Phoenix and intended to test my capacity to improvise (a good trait to have when producing gobs of artwork). As I progressed I tried to think about how something as sweet as a pet dog could be twisted into a horrible monstrosity by the weight of an Oroboros Heart. I settled on some lobster, cattle, and scorpion influences combined with a serpent. I also threw in the snake's head to emphasize that the Chimera need not preserve a standard vertebrate morphology; future images of similar beasts drawn by me will also likely feature multiple heads.<br /> If Chimera do not make the cut, this image can easily still be utilized either as a Nightmare or as an Oroboros who was too susceptible to outside opinion.<br /> <br /> <b>Hanging Dragon</b><br /> This illustration was part of a bigger image intended to be the cover page splash for the document. I've cropped out the human slayer formerly on the left side of the page and colorized the dragon, resulting in a sort of inquisitive forest meditation scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Prone Dragon</b><br /> Like Cruiser Dragon, this image was first crafted to emphasize scale difference in various Degrees of Divinity. It was not finished before the last phase of the project ended and the head needed improvement. I've since colorized it and I think it'd make a nice intimidating filler.<br /> <br /> <b>Serpent Dragon</b><br /> This image was present in the Third Phase document, though it has been colorized. It was originally intended to be the dragon form of Cameron (from the inter-chapter stories).<br /> <br /> <b>Slayer Orobori</b><br /> Most of this image was in the Third Phase document. It was painfully bad, though; I was trying too hard to relate draconic features to human features so that the creature would resemble its human form, and the result was... hideous. I've since corrected this error, making adjustments to the head and removing the other lingering human features. After finishing the update to this illustration I was certain: I'm going to stick to drawing monsters.<br /> <br /> <b>Wing Shroud Dragon</b><br /> This illustration began life as concept art for a character I had run in an Embers campaign. He was a coal miner who found an Oroboros Heart after a shaft collapse and was forced to consume it to survive. He was a Blood Finder (in 3rd Phase context he'd be a Vizier Delver), and his most memorable moment was when he decided to cure his Black Lung (from working in the mine) by igniting the lingering particles within his bronchial tubes. He also carried his Heart around in his lunch pail, which was amusing.<br /> The drawing itself employed a new experimental technique I was using to illustrate; while it was okay for black-and-white it was incredibly taxing and the pay-off wasn't much better than my old style. I was unhappy with the feet, which is why he ended up being cropped in the Third Phase document.<br /> Raccoon re-drew this image and colorized it. This inspired me to give my drawings another look (and gave me a color scheme to apply, something I hadn't considered for the image). For that contribution I have retained Raccoon's artist mark on the image.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll be preparing more images in this style at my leisure (it's a good way to decompress between other projects) and I'll notify your team when I have uploaded another collection of 8-10 images.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T01:25:42-07:00","id":874338,"title":"","content":"<b>Team Application</b><br /> <br /> <u>Desired position:</u><br /> <br /> I intend to be a writer.<br /> <br /> <u>Sample of Work</u><br /> <br /> What creature looms larger in humanity's imagination than the dragon? They have featured in myths from Asia to the Americas, from Indonesia to England. They have taken every role conceivable, from demon to trickster to mentor to god. They have been by turns worshipped and reviled in almost every civilisation throughout history. From the serpent in Eden to George's dragon to Nidhoggr to the world-devouring Cipactli of the Aztec, dragons are a part of every mythology. Like the serpents they are, they twist their way throughout our tales, legends and dreams, becoming symbols of pride, power and greed. How, then, could such a creature, a being which winds its way through the human consciousness so thoroughly and completely, be nothing more than fantasy? Surely there must be some truth to the tales.<br /> <br /> <u>Qualifications</u><br /> <br /> I have no official qualifications, as I go to an alternative school where grading is handled differently, although I am at present predicted to get an A or A* on the English Language and Literature GCSEs I am working towards. In school, I have been given consistently high grades (that is, A, B+ and A* equivalents) in English and related subjects. I have studied mythology and various forms of narrative. Part of those studies was writing essays on them (some of which I can provide), as well as short stories.<br /> <br /> <u>What I want to be involved in and why</u><br /> <br /> I would like to be involved in the writing of the background and 'fluff' text of this game, as I feel that I would do better at that than dealing with mechanics. Other parts that I am interested in being involved in are the X and Y splats as well as Edicts and the Dreamtide. I would like to be involved in this because I would like to see it brought to the conclusion it deserves. I would like to be involved in bringing it to that conclusion and I intend, if I am accepted, to do the best I can to help it become the best and most enjoyable game it can be. I must admit that I would very much like to play this as a finished game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 04-26-2016, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T08:34:11-07:00","id":874565,"title":"","content":"New addition: Gonna add <b>Slayers</b> to the rules here, and gonna go into detail in the book, because they're both a threat, and what the Orobori were before they got their Hearts...<br /> <br /> ajf&gt; Alright, Application Accepted. Please PM me with your Skype name...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=874170#post874170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Raccoon re-drew this image and colorized it. This inspired me to give my drawings another look (and gave me a color scheme to apply, something I hadn't considered for the image). For that contribution I have retained Raccoon's artist mark on the image.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, I was looking at it like &quot;maybe this is what Jean used to look like&quot;, and went from the aesthetic of a red bull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 04-26-2016, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T08:36:35-07:00","id":874568,"title":"","content":"<b>Team Application<br /> <br /> 1: Specific Position</b><br /> Writing.<br /> <br /> <b>2: Work Sample.</b><br /> In the dawn of Humanity, it was nothing but a world of lust and violence. The newly born children of mud only knew primal emotions of domination, satisfaction and ambition, which dominated the first half of human history. They made only war and chaos onto anything and everything they touched, and yet their higher minds simply desired more. It is said to be from this dreampt up chaos where the first Dragons came from. Born from the dreams and hopes of Humanity, they knew how to organize the chaos that the Humans held. The ruled like gods, teaching mankind the meaning of virtues. But mankind still had those primal urges, and the proof of this was killing their Gods and eating their Hearts. They wrote that dragons were both curators of society and yet a blight on the world that had been wiped out...or so they think. In truth, those who ate the hearts became new dragons themselves, but cursed so that their hearts would be stolen in the turn of a never ending cycle.<br /> <br /> Look at humans today. Nothing has changed. Humanity still has that selfish, primal spark for dominion. They simply learned how to display it through more subtle acts and means. The Ourobori, the people with the cursed hearts, find themselves responsible for this suffering. Some choose to work to lead society back into the right direction, but never can they show their faces. Afterall, those who do not learn from history are doomed to repeat it. The Ourobori, the dragons who are destroyed and hearts eaten by humans bring only new dragons to suffer the same fate.<br /> <br /> <b>3: Qualifications</b><br /> I'll admit, despite English being my first language, I'm actually pretty bad at grammar, which is prolly visible in the above. As well, I've mainly been getting C grades in English. Another weakness I have is that I need to have a clearly lain out goal or guideline to follow. For example, I have to at least have some general idea of an outline for Dragon or what I should put into the writing. However, when I get inspired to do something, I can easily make some rough drafts in the course of a week. That said, I have written up a Princess the Hopeful Supplement &quot;Road of Dawn&quot; (basing majorly off of Kings Raven's ideas for how the Pre-Twilight Courts would be like), and I'm currently the head of the Siren the Surfacing Resurrection and have done most of the writing for it.<br /> <br /> Link to Google Docs with ALL of the Siren Documents to date: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0Bwda1WVb-LLcYVMyYl95MDAxa0U&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/folderview?...0U&amp;usp=sharing</a><br /> Link to Princess the Hopeful site where the Supplement download link is: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/home\" target=\"_blank\">https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/home</a><br /> <br /> <b>4: What I want to be involved in and why</b><br /> Writing of the X and Y Splats. Simply put, the Court of Cups, Wands and Pentacles were the basis of the Road to Dawn Supplement, being Y Splats in Princess. I've also been responsible for writing up the entirety of the X and Y Splats in Siren (which are the Waters and Currents respectively, Currents cover both normal and Abyssal, although Reaper and Yads have helped with/done most/all of the idea making). In other words, most of my prominent writing is the creation of X and Y splats, so it's in writing those up that I feel the most suited for in Dragon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:04:16-07:00","id":874584,"title":"","content":"Ok, Saulotthe, you're right about not being a strong fantasy writer, but I'm sure we could use you for something. Could you try writing something more technical than that? Like, how about a paragraph on a basic game mechanic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:51:31-07:00","id":874623,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar610_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"610\" data-vbnamecard=\"610\">CJC</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While that would have certainly helped with depicting a clear gender for the images, I decided it wasn't a good fit for this project. </div> </div> </div>Why not draw a couple of human form/human-like Dragons using Edicts or something like that?<br /> EDIT: I mean, it's ok to have Dragons in a game of dragons, but maybe having a couple humans would allow players to see themselves as the characters from a easier perspective. And this way you could depict gendered dragons. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":316,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","user":"Jesuncolo","date":". 04-26-2016, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:46:22-07:00","id":874670,"title":"","content":"Alrighties. I'm using these as a basis for the next paragraph.<br /> For how to regain Breath: <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/DragonTheEmbers\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...ragonTheEmbers</a><br /> For a general outline, specifically the Pneuma part (fun fact, Pneuma was named &quot;Breath&quot; before we changed it XD): <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dHPB-rGUo_ObHiCSzSkqhZYovEY56tKBBVwu2_i8eNw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> <b>New Advantage: Breath</b><br /> Breath is more than just a vital sign of human life and a daily excersize to remain alive. To the Ourobori, Breath is what fuels the fire within the Dragon's Heart, that keeps them running faster and better than any human. It's motes of raw energy that Ourobori receive from either luxuriation in signs of their material wealth or consuming food. How much Breath an Ourobori can expend in one turn, as well as how much they can store is determined by their Heart/Furnace (whichever is the appropriate Supernatural Advantage).<br /> <br /> <i>Regaining Breath</i><br /> -Ourobori can sleep with material objects of their wealth to regain Breath. The object must be of enough value to have a Resources cost applied to it, and the Ourobori must receive a full night's rest beside or on the object. Roll the object's Resources + the Ourobori's Furnace/Heart. Each success gives the Ourobori one point of Breath.<br /> -Eating food allows an Ourobori to regain Breath, adding &quot;fuel to the fire&quot; so to speak. For every 500 Calories an Ourobori eats, they regain 1 point of Breath. If the food was highly flammable, such as high proof liquor, then the Ourobori instead gains 1 Breath for every 100 Calories he eats or drinks.<br /> -Eating or drinking flammable but normally non-consumable liquids or solids also grants Breath at a greater rate than eating regular food, but at a price. An Ourobori regains 1 Point of Breath per quart of liquid or every Size 1 object he eats. However, the human body wasn't made to process things labelled &quot;non-consumable&quot;. As such, for each point of Breath regained in this manner, the Ourobori suffers an equivalent penalty to all rolls made in human form.<br /> -Eating a human allows an Ourobori to regain all of their Breath. However, this is considered as a grave sin against Guilt/Hubris.<br /> <br /> <i>Spending and Using Breath</i><br /> <b>Purview Activation: </b>An Ourobori may need to spend Breath to activate Purviews. <br /> <b>Dream Sorcery: </b>An Ourobori may need to spend Breath to make use of Dream Sorcery.<br /> <b>Flame and Frost Immunity: </b>While an Ourobori has Breath, they are still more than human and not subject to the same limitations as Humans have. The Ourobori is considered immune to natural sources of heat and cold, making them unaffected by the Extreme Heat and Extreme Cold Tilts. If they have no Breath however, then they're subject to the full penalties and damages those tilts bring. Supernatural effects or attacks that deal with hot and cold and that target the Ourobori suffer a penalty equal to half the Ourobori's Furnace/Heart, rounded up.<br /> <b>Reflexive Transformation: </b>With the expenditure of one Breath, an Ourobori may transform into his True Form as a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> How does this look? I feel I should've done abit of a smaller thing. <br /> <br /> And if I can say, I can't help but feel like Siren and Dragon have some similar features and yet are mostly opposites. Sirens have Flensers, who are hunters who want to eat Siren's flesh to extend their immortal lives (Eating Siren Flesh allows a person to stop aging for awhile), whereas Dragons have Slayers who hunt Dragons for their hearts. Sirens have Pneuma as a fuel stat (which was once named Breath, heck, Pneuma means &quot;Divine Breath/Breath of Life&quot;) and Dragons have Breath. Dragons have been around since the start of existence to lead humanity like gods, whereas Sirens began existing when the Deluge, the end of existence, happened, and through the power of their progenitor have managed to connect to present day reality to try and stop the Deluge from happening. Sirens being more like Mediators between Civilization and Nature to the Dragon's Ruler. And of course, Sirens are associated with Water whereas Dragons are associated with Fire.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this because either project is doing wrong or is crossing over the other's line, I'm just noting the similarities and liking how they play similar and yet different. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:28:06-07:00","id":874783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jesuncolo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=874623#post874623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not draw a couple of human form/human-like Dragons using Edicts or something like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get ahead of us, lol...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:38:52-07:00","id":874793,"title":"","content":"Ok, Saulotthe, you were a bit rambly there, and I'm seeing some mechanics I don't think are going to look like that in the end, but you're competent enough that we could definitely use you for writing the more technical parts. You said you wanted to work on the Slayer and Brood Bonded templates, right? Those will eventually be a thing.<br /> <br /> Some tips in the future, you might want to try writing off of bulleted outlines, and start with the basic facts before stylizing them. 90% of all aspiring writers benefit from doing that. I'm probably going to have you practice a bit as we get started, and working on the Transitional Edition of Embers and the Playtesting Daft (which can both be sloppy) should help...<br /> <br /> Anyway, please send me your Skype name in a PM and I'll add you to the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 04-26-2016, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:34:25-07:00","id":874834,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10120_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10120\" data-vbnamecard=\"10120\">RockstarRaccoon</a> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=874783#post874783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't get ahead of us, lol...</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if I came off that way. I was only trying to give advice. I know I'm an outsider and I didn't submit, though I looked at what CJC wrote and I thought I could be useful. If you wish so, I'll just stay off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:02:53-07:00","id":874919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=874793#post874793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, Saulotthe, you were a bit rambly there, and I'm seeing some mechanics I don't think are going to look like that in the end, but you're competent enough that we could definitely use you for writing the more technical parts. You said you wanted to work on the Slayer and Brood Bonded templates, right? Those will eventually be a thing.<br /> <br /> Some tips in the future, you might want to try writing off of bulleted outlines, and start with the basic facts before stylizing them. 90% of all aspiring writers benefit from doing that. I'm probably going to have you practice a bit as we get started, and working on the Transitional Edition of Embers and the Playtesting Daft (which can both be sloppy) should help...<br /> <br /> Anyway, please send me your Skype name in a PM and I'll add you to the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties then. And I meant more of the X and Y Splats? As in &quot;What Are You As a Person&quot; (the X/Internal/Birth Splat) and &quot;What Social Group are you in&quot; (the Y/Internal/Social Splat) parts. But I can work on other Templates in game if that's desired. Anyways, the Skype name is sent. If it's wrong, could you tell me so I can try sending another name? :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T18:42:19-07:00","id":875097,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar316_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"316\" data-vbnamecard=\"316\">Jesuncolo</a><br /> Thank you for the input, Jesuncolo.<br /> <br /> A project of this size will require at least a hundred illustrations, and will probably end up at the watermark of a quarter-ton. I won't be the only artist contributing... and because of that I will only be contributing monster illustrations. I hoped by announcing this early it would be clear that the project needs artists to draw human illustrations, as I will not.<br /> <br /> Human illustrations will be more dependent on the game's subsystems, which means it might be better to draw them later in development once those subsystems have had time to set.<br /> <br /> -------<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9750_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9750\" data-vbnamecard=\"9750\">SaulottheGentle</a><br /> You're using the species term incorrectly.<br /> <br /> Oroboros is the singular form. Orobori is the plural. Even though Oroboros is a misspelling of the term Ouroboros it is intentional as the word is a palindrome.<br /> Oroboro &lt;=&gt; oroborO.<br /> &quot;An Oroboros called all her friends together. All those Orobori decided to form a den.&quot;<br /> <br /> Some of those mechanics are dangerous waters; being able to jump to True Form (especially if it retains the potency it did in the second edition) would be extreme. Breath for transformation is more about triggering Ablutions quickly, heating up the parts of the body so that the 'human' facade can be washed away more quickly (that's why the powers are called Ablutions, its a divine cleansing of the body).<br /> How are you at writing conditions and tilts? I feel that eating or drinking something that isn't meant to be a consumable (like a box of tinder or a tank of gasoline) should inflict some lingering negative effect on the character, but damage is too extreme and a roll is too tedious. &quot;Conditions&quot; is a system which was not present when the Second Phase PDF launched and could not be used as a penalty, and is a perfect compromise between damage and a roll to give the gorging system some bite.<br /> <br /> If you're looking to write X/Y splats, I'd recommend starting with the X splats. It appears Raccoon is intending to keep Oroboros induction similar (eat a heart, its old owner begins to fossilize and you become a dragon), so you can look at what's already in the existing material and move from there. As for Y splats, you'd need to wait to see if the direction of the wind is shifting; Philosophies were formerly reactions to the impending extinction (Ash, Bone, Blood, Sweat, Tears) and then were replaced with unrelated calls to ruler-ship (Imperator, Paragon, Savant, Vizier, Caitiff). Until Raccoon decides on the themes he wishes to portray with Philosophies, though, it's best not to waste energy on full write-ups. You could perhaps outline pitches, though, since you're interested in writing those segments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:22:46-07:00","id":875193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875097#post875097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9750_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9750\" data-vbnamecard=\"9750\">SaulottheGentle</a><br /> You're using the species term incorrectly.<br /> <br /> Oroboros is the singular form. Orobori is the plural. Even though Oroboros is a misspelling of the term Ouroboros it is intentional as the word is a palindrome.<br /> Oroboro &lt;=&gt; oroborO.<br /> &quot;An Oroboros called all her friends together. All those Orobori decided to form a den.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't realize that those were the terms. D:<br /> <br /> I should probably admit that I haven't kept tabs on Dragon up until this new thread appeared, so I'm entirely new to the gameline, pdf and all (I wasn't even aware that it HAD a PDF). That said, I'm willing to read up on the Dragon book(s) and get the information I need before writing, if you're willing to let me stay after me saying that. D:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875097#post875097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of those mechanics are dangerous waters; being able to jump to True Form (especially if it retains the potency it did in the second edition) would be extreme. Breath for transformation is more about triggering Ablutions quickly, heating up the parts of the body so that the 'human' facade can be washed away more quickly (that's why the powers are called Ablutions, its a divine cleansing of the body).</div> </div> </div> </div>I never meant for them to be taken as canon on the spot, I know the game is abit too early/WIP to write up what the exact mechanics are. I merely used Breath as a way to write up a mechanic that pertains to the gameline and hopefully to show my writing on them. If nothing else, I do kind of know that loads of wording will change before things are fully done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875097#post875097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are you at writing conditions and tilts? I feel that eating or drinking something that isn't meant to be a consumable (like a box of tinder or a tank of gasoline) should inflict some lingering negative effect on the character, but damage is too extreme and a roll is too tedious. &quot;Conditions&quot; is a system which was not present when the Second Phase PDF launched and could not be used as a penalty, and is a perfect compromise between damage and a roll to give the gorging system some bite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel I'm at least used to how they're supposed to be written out by now. If I could ask for a more specific/clear explanation as to what you mean? &quot;A Condition that can't be used as a penalty and a compromise between damage and a roll&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875097#post875097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're looking to write X/Y splats, I'd recommend starting with the X splats. It appears Raccoon is intending to keep Oroboros induction similar (eat a heart, its old owner begins to fossilize and you become a dragon), so you can look at what's already in the existing material and move from there. As for Y splats, you'd need to wait to see if the direction of the wind is shifting; Philosophies were formerly reactions to the impending extinction (Ash, Bone, Blood, Sweat, Tears) and then were replaced with unrelated calls to ruler-ship (Imperator, Paragon, Savant, Vizier, Caitiff). Until Raccoon decides on the themes he wishes to portray with Philosophies, though, it's best not to waste energy on full write-ups. You could perhaps outline pitches, though, since you're interested in writing those segments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties then. Just the X Splats then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:35:53-07:00","id":875257,"title":"","content":"Relax, I was just clarifying the nomenclature which was in effect when the last PDF was launched. I'm just a consultant; I'm not going to remove members from the team (Besides, your writing is good and you're eager to help; I would be a fool to scare you off over something as petty as terminology).<br /> <br /> As for the Condition, I was trying to explain that the Conditions system wasn't present when Dragon employed a gorging mechanic, so I was forced to choose between inflicting damage on the player or prompting a roll. Both the former and the latter were ineffective, but a Condition would work (something like &quot;Wrong Meal&quot; which would impose a context-sensitive penalty to speed, Willpower, or something... I'm just brainstorming here).<br /> Perhaps separate conditions for different kinds of inedible fuels: solids might risk rupturing the stomach (Eating tinder gives the condition, which advances to a rupture if the player completes reckless criteria A, B, and C) while liquids might induce regurgitation (sensory overload causes spontaneous flaming vomit... not sure what the trigger would be).<br /> <br /> If that's not your forte, don't worry about it. I was trying to be encouraging and I guess I intimidated you, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:55:47-07:00","id":875580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875257#post875257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relax, I was just clarifying the nomenclature which was in effect when the last PDF was launched. I'm just a consultant; I'm not going to remove members from the team (Besides, your writing is good and you're eager to help; I would be a fool to scare you off over something as petty as terminology).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, my apologies. I saw from the pdf and the thread that you were the person in charge. I know you're a consultant now, but I feel the need to at least be as respectful as possible since this is a project you have a huge part in. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875257#post875257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Condition, I was trying to explain that the Conditions system wasn't present when Dragon employed a gorging mechanic, so I was forced to choose between inflicting damage on the player or prompting a roll. Both the former and the latter were ineffective, but a Condition would work (something like &quot;Wrong Meal&quot; which would impose a context-sensitive penalty to speed, Willpower, or something... I'm just brainstorming here).<br /> Perhaps separate conditions for different kinds of inedible fuels: solids might risk rupturing the stomach (Eating tinder gives the condition, which advances to a rupture if the player completes reckless criteria A, B, and C) while liquids might induce regurgitation (sensory overload causes spontaneous flaming vomit... not sure what the trigger would be).</div> </div> </div> </div>Alrighties. I have school in the next 10 minutes, but I'll bring up some ideas. One idea I had was the factor that eating Inedible foods that restore Breath would only give a condition if you were in human form, since the human body wasn't meant to eat inedibles. I was working on the assumption that a Dragon body on the other hand would be able to handle eating things that a human body normally wouldn't be able to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875257#post875257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's not your forte, don't worry about it. I was trying to be encouraging and I guess I intimidated you, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Along with the earlier explanation of feeling the need to give respect to the project heads, I'm at least paranoid when it comes to manners and tend to apologize needlessly. It's more my fault for worrying over nothing really. ^^&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T10:37:35-07:00","id":875752,"title":"","content":"Hello. What's up everybody?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T12:37:16-07:00","id":875862,"title":"","content":"Aside from what's been stated in the first few posts? I dunno...<br /> <br /> Weren't you involved in the old project?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T13:01:13-07:00","id":875890,"title":"","content":"A few questions:<br /> <br /> In the case of the first dragon(s), the ones that crawled from the Dreamtide, was it one great Dragon-goetia which splintered into many shards and became the race of dragons, or was it many dragon-goetia in the first place,all squirming through at around the same time?<br /> <br /> For the X splat, are we making it an inherent quality to the Heart (i.e. the person whose Heart you devoured will have had the same X splat) or is it based on how you acquired the Heart? Personally, I would prefer the inherent quality, but if we're sticking with the Slayers/Finders/etc that's fine with me.<br /> <br /> Are the Y splats going to be social groups, ala Mage's Orders or Vampire's Covenants, or are they going to be more philosophies, ala Promethean's Refinements or Geist's Archetypes? Becuase just looking at the idiosyncratic nature of the Oroboroi, I would lean towards the latter as I can't imagine any dragon willingly submitting to another except through force (although this would make a nice way to combine politics and combat, I think it dilutes them both).<br /> <br /> Could we perhaps make Edicts/Purviews more area-based than in the original Dragon? It's just because, based on their concept, it feels like they would be thematically more suited to wide-area, fairly indiscriminate effects rather than pinpoint ones. That might just be me, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T13:45:54-07:00","id":875939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875890#post875890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of the first dragon(s), the ones that crawled from the Dreamtide, was it one great Dragon-goetia which splintered into many shards and became the race of dragons, or was it many dragon-goetia in the first place,all squirming through at around the same time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the X splat, are we making it an inherent quality to the Heart (i.e. the person whose Heart you devoured will have had the same X splat) or is it based on how you acquired the Heart? Personally, I would prefer the inherent quality, but if we're sticking with the Slayers/Finders/etc that's fine with me. </div> </div> </div>Here's the problem: the Hearts are all mostly the same, and in possession of the memetic code for the baseline of a Dragon. The most important difference between different Orobori is the act by which they came into possession of the heart, as this is a major event which marks the heart with a much more potent meme than anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are the Y splats going to be social groups, ala Mage's Orders or Vampire's Covenants, or are they going to be more philosophies, ala Promethean's Refinements or Geist's Archetypes? Becuase just looking at the idiosyncratic nature of the Oroboroi, I would lean towards the latter as I can't imagine any dragon willingly submitting to another except through force (although this would make a nice way to combine politics and combat, I think it dilutes them both). </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking really hard about this... And I've noticed that the Y splats are generally social groups which various creatures join and swear fealty to. Beyond the matter of pride you mentioned, there's also the matter of availability: there are simply not enough Orobori to do this. The Orobori are in small numbers, meaning it's rare for them to meet more than a couple others in their lifetime, so forming multiple large orders which span the globe would be a massive undertaking, unlike Vampires, who basically infest any city they're present in. The Philosophy thing works for this, but I'm feeling like the Purview thing might work better: it's an expression of the divine power they have, probably an expression of what the Superego desires to invoke in the world. It's how they feel the power they have is best utilized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could we perhaps make Edicts/Purviews more area-based than in the original Dragon? It's just because, based on their concept, it feels like they would be thematically more suited to wide-area, fairly indiscriminate effects rather than pinpoint ones. That might just be me, though. </div> </div> </div>I dunno, PM me your Skype name and we'll talk about it at the meeting next week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T13:53:01-07:00","id":875945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875939#post875939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, one of <i>those </i>is it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875939#post875939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the problem: the Hearts are all mostly the same, and in possession of the memetic code for the baseline of a Dragon. The most important difference between different Orobori is the act by which they came into possession of the heart, as this is a major event which marks the heart with a much more potent meme than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the reasoning there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875939#post875939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking really hard about this... And I've noticed that the Y splats are generally social groups which various creatures join and swear fealty to. Beyond the matter of pride you mentioned, there's also the matter of availability: there are simply not enough Orobori to do this. The Orobori are in small numbers, meaning it's rare for them to meet more than a couple others in their lifetime, so forming multiple large orders which span the globe would be a massive undertaking, unlike Vampires, who basically infest any city they're present in. The Philosophy thing works for this, but I'm feeling like the Purview thing might work better: it's an expression of the divine power they have, probably an expression of what the Superego desires to invoke in the world. It's how they feel the power they have is best utilized.</div> </div> </div> </div>By 'expression of the divine power they have' ,do you mean how they think that their divine power should be applied to the world?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875939#post875939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, PM me your Skype name and we'll talk about it at the meeting next week.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T16:14:28-07:00","id":876092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875945#post875945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\