ong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=875862#post875862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from what's been stated in the first few posts? I dunno...<br /> <br /> Weren't you involved in the old project?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was. I haven't been online much these days cause the only internet connections is the library for about and hour and what data I burn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T15:00:26-07:00","id":880505,"title":"","content":"We're still interested in new people. Writers, artists, and playtesters...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=880356#post880356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was. I haven't been online much these days cause the only internet connections is the library for about and hour and what data I burn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you like to get involved again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=880314#post880314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random question. Even though most of the discussion is on Skype, shouldn't we still post things to this thread to make sure that people interested in reading can still see development and the like?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't have much to post, but alright, I guess I'll post something about what's being done soon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T06:36:18-07:00","id":880928,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Team Application </span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Position: Writer </span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><b>Sample of my work</b></u></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What are the Orobori? They are creatures of dreams who are now formed by the imaginations of the living. They are bound by responsibility, expected to have ethical qualities, lest they be considered dragons of sin. They oppose Nightmares, fighting back Beasts of primordial myth and the Deep Ones that dwell within the deepest seas of the collective dreamscape. They embody the raw power of the times before men, the strength of the mythical dragon. In whatever they do, they learn to excel and function at a level akin to gods. They are fighting extinction, determined to consume massive amounts of calories in order to simply survive day to day. They can work as engines of war, discovery, or even fuel for their own egos. Some dragons are tyrants, and some are benevolent rulers, but all dragons have something they must be responsible for. They are born from the act of eating hearts, an act that seems barbaric in modern times...but was accepted in the ancient days when men were closer to Gods. It is not barbaric, simply a misunderstood ritual that passes the power of the dragon to another. This forms that person into an Orobori, and from there, the heartstrings that guide all dragons sets them on a path to greatness.</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><b>Qualifications</b></u></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(<a href=\"http://www.novasjournal.com/chapters.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.novasjournal.com/chapters.html</a>) [I produced a single issue of my own digital comic with the help of other artists]</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(<a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/threads/souls-lost-on-black-tides-wod.196782/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.rpnation.com/threads/sou...es-wod.196782/</a>) and (<a href=\"https://www.rpnation.com/threads/wod-heart-of-the-mountain.151365/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.rpnation.com/threads/wod...untain.151365/</a>) two PbP I'm working on, both stories involve dragons as key parts of the plot.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I have written a handful of short stories, mostly unpublished. My preferred genre is modern fantasy/supernatural. I have also been GMing for around 3-4 years including having experience in Chronicles of Darkness.</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><b>Why I want to be Involved</b></u></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Raccoon introduced me to Dragon and I loved it. I really didn\u2019t enjoy how the game was unfinished, and like him I liked what 2nd and 3rd Development were trying to do in parts...but it was never complete. I\u2019m a bit hesitant towards working on a big project, but my heart burns with the passion for this game. I want to see it in a completed state that will be easier to read and play. I\u2019m willing to put in my own effort towards that passion. I\u2019m also a big fan of hacking and retooling games in general, along with fantasy and dragons. So to me, working on a modified game seems like something I could do well. </span></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5298-novap","user":"NovaP","date":". 05-03-2016, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5298-novap","name":"NovaP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T11:41:48-07:00","id":881123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=880505#post880505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you like to get involved again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like too. But I'm offline most of the time so I won't be able to get my stuff in on time. Also working on a horror based miniature wargame, switching back and forth isn't that much of a problem. But my internet situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T19:53:23-07:00","id":881431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NovaP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=880928#post880928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u><b>Sample of my work</b></u></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What are the Orobori? They are creatures of dreams who are now formed by the imaginations of the living. They are bound by responsibility, expected to have ethical qualities, lest they be considered dragons of sin. They oppose Nightmares, fighting back Beasts of primordial myth and the Deep Ones that dwell within the deepest seas of the collective dreamscape. They embody the raw power of the times before men, the strength of the mythical dragon. In whatever they do, they learn to excel and function at a level akin to gods. They are fighting extinction, determined to consume massive amounts of calories in order to simply survive day to day. They can work as engines of war, discovery, or even fuel for their own egos. Some dragons are tyrants, and some are benevolent rulers, but all dragons have something they must be responsible for. They are born from the act of eating hearts, an act that seems barbaric in modern times...but was accepted in the ancient days when men were closer to Gods. It is not barbaric, simply a misunderstood ritual that passes the power of the dragon to another. This forms that person into an Orobori, and from there, the heartstrings that guide all dragons sets them on a path to greatness.</span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is very, VERY rambly. Could you write me something that sticks to one topic, and doesn't keep deviating around vague themes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T10:56:55-07:00","id":881982,"title":"","content":"What are Orobori? Predators perfected. Evolution at it's most economical. Gods among monsters! And dying.....<br /> <br /> First draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T11:27:25-07:00","id":882028,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Ok everyone, here's a quick update on what's going on.</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Changes from the 2nd and 3rd editions</b></span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Oroboroi are no longer bound as strictly to the Leadership theme. Instead, they are loosely bound to a broader theme of Responsibility and Worthiness.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Old Gods are no longer part of the basic origin story. They will be mentioned in a later chapter as the \u201cBomb in the Room\u201d, to quote this copy of Idigam Chronicles sitting next to me.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The &quot;Vault&quot; has been shelved for the Dreamtide.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Dreamtide Travel and Manipulation are now part of a merit called &quot;Dream Sorcery&quot;, which can be gained by non-Oroboroi occultists, and require Blood, Breath, Willpower, or Jadeite.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cFurnace\u201d is now \u201cHeartstring\u201d, to signify that it is not a property of the Heart itself, but its connection to the Oroboros.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Breath is gained by eating things, like in 2nd, and we're working on fleshing out just what this may entail. We're thinking of them as being similar to Vitae.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;Mandate&quot; is now &quot;Conviction&quot;, to reflect the new focus on Worth rather than good leadership. It's a sideways system, and the extremes to fall into are Hubris (the hoarding, rampaging dragon) and Guilt (the human who is no longer worthy of their Heart)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Oroboroi start with 12 Ablutions: 3 from the Method, 3 from the Common, 3 from any Oroboros list, and 3 from the Storyteller's discretion.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ablutions can now be gained and lost as a result of public opinion through a process called \u201cThe Reimagining\u201d. Compare this to the Renown-based Gifts in Werewolf</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There is now an Ablution list with stuff that the Oroboroi only have access to through external means.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;School&quot; has been morphed into &quot;Purview&quot;, which is a manifestation of the former-human's highest ideal.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Oroboroi are now completely immune to fire, except in Human Guise, which is burned away to reveal the Dragon beneath.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Slayers, Dragonborn, Pilot Lights, and Deep Ones will have their own sheets and rulesets.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There's gonna be WAY more stuff to pull with the Deep Ones.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Alot of things have been rephrased and retuned for new edition stuff.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>What's been done so far</b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Written out a detailed secret lore, explaining to us what exactly Oroboroi are and what physics are at play here, from which we'll be pulling the mechanics.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Also, Dank Memes.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Finalized some really core decisions on what's going on in this book and where we should take it</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Built a mockup character sheet which has new terms and systems in a bit more detail.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Started work on the Transitional Rulebook.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>What needs to be done by next week</b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Finish and release a Transitional Rulebook.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Have someone look through the new Mage book to figure out what's going on there now.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Get a basic sheet out.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">WE NEED ARTISTS!!</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Moving Forward...</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The current plan is to have a Transitional Rulebook released some time next week. This won't be particularly pretty, nor will it have most of the stuff in it, but it will show exactly where we're taking the game for now. Moving forward from there, we'll be asking for people to try and make characters based on that book, and to give us feedback on the general direction we're moving in. We'll also be looking for Playtesters, and new teammembers in general, ESPECIALLY some artists.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 05-04-2016, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T11:02:45-07:00","id":883028,"title":"","content":"Alright, here's another sample I thought up while trying to focus on Dreams.<br /> <br /> When men dream, the mind wanders aimlessly trying to organize facts and memories into a meaningful mess of images. For the Orobori, who learned to crawl from the Dreamtide, the process is much different. They do not simply wander the dreamscape, they sail through it willingly through powerful sorcery. They walk dreams as simply as a man could walk down the sidewalk. They ride along the tides of imagination like brash sailors. Underneath the waves lurk the unsolved mysteries of the deep darkness. Legends of sea monsters inspired terror in the hearts mortal sailors, and it does much the same for the Orobori who tread in the land of dreams. Unlike mortals, the Orobori take it upon themselves to fight against the Nightmares and become stalwart guardians of the Dreamtide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5298-novap","user":"NovaP","date":". 05-05-2016, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5298-novap","name":"NovaP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T11:18:16-07:00","id":883045,"title":"","content":"<b>Nova&gt; Application Accepted</b><br /> I already have your Skype, so...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T20:15:25-07:00","id":885126,"title":"","content":"So, we're still interested in new members. We're gonna need solid forum-RP writers for the official playtesting group pretty soon...<br /> <br /> Speaking of that: the new playtesting draft is coming out next week! Anyone excited for that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T23:08:50-07:00","id":885194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=885126#post885126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, we're still interested in new members. We're gonna need solid forum-RP writers for the official playtesting group pretty soon...<br /> <br /> Speaking of that: the new playtesting draft is coming out next week! Anyone excited for that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right here, dudes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T08:07:29-07:00","id":885381,"title":"","content":"<b>Team Application<br /> <br /> 1) Specific position:</b> writing<br /> <br /> <b>2) Work Sample:</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Over the course of centuries, dragons have been many things, in many different countries. Mighty gods, to be worshipped and revered. Terrifying beasts, to be slain. Creatures of myth, whose people have been trying to prove the existence. Much like the dreams they originally emerged from, they have changed many times according to how mortals perceived them. To the Orobori, this change is quite literal: the way they are seen by humans can actually cause them to change, altering their appearance and causing them to either lose abilities or gain new ones. Such a phenomenon is known among them as the Reimagining.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>4) Qualifications:</b> I am an aspiring writer, and have already written two books and a half (in french), as well as several stories in english. I also make regular edits on TvTropes (including most of the Dragon the Embers page) and played one New World of Darkness session as a GM. On a downside, I am french, and while I can speak english fluently enough, it still isn't my native language, so I can occasionally do grammatical errors and my writing-style doesn't necessarly translate well.<br /> <br /> Here is a link the most recent fanfic I wrote in english (my other fics can be found from my profile, but they are older and as such don't reflect my current writing very well):<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/11794376/1/An-Odd-Friendship\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1179437...Odd-Friendship</a><br /> <br /> <b>5) </b><b>What I want to be involved in and why:</b> World-building, and the crossover-related parts in particular. The universe is what got me interested in World of Darkness and it fan-made supplements to begin with, and I believe it could be interesting to flesh out the Orobori's interactions with other creatures in the setting, including those from other fan-game if possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 05-08-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T13:13:00-07:00","id":885627,"title":"","content":"<b>Darnias</b>&gt; Ok, this isn't bad, but I'd like for you to go back to the post with the application format, and use that. This is kind of just a single thing, and I'd like to have some background on record before I bring you in. Pay attention to formatting too: we need to keep good formatting in the book, and you seem to have just plopped text down without labels or emphases. Also, the writing you provided could use a bit of touching up, as I see a few grammatical errors, and seems to be just a little bit more fanciful than I'd prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 05-08-2016, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T15:02:46-07:00","id":885728,"title":"","content":"A quote we have to get in at some point: &quot;All that we see or seem is but a dream within a dream.&quot;<br /> <br /> - Edgar Allan Poe","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T15:23:33-07:00","id":885734,"title":"","content":"Hem.... my bad. I did read the application format, but I completely misunderstood how that worked. Just edited the post so it'd match it better. Do not hesitate to tell me if I made another mistake.<br /> <br /> As for the text itself, yes, I do tend to make some grammatical errors, though I usually try to double-check what I write to minimize them. And that sample willingly took a tone like this, I am capable of toning down the fancyness if needed. As for the label/emphasis part... I am afraid I am not sure what you mean. Could you please explain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11745,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","user":"Darinas","date":". 05-08-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T00:43:41-07:00","id":886013,"title":"","content":"Darinas&gt; <b>Application Accepted</b><br /> <br /> Just to make sure you know, this is CHRONICLES of Darkness, not OWoD. There is a very striking difference, namely the amount of mystery and vagueness they put in the books. Keep that in mind from now on, and go look through the list of suggested reading materials on the first page of this thread.<br /> <br /> Please PM me your Skype name so I can get you in the team's chat...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T02:11:09-07:00","id":886037,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I will keep that in mind. And don't worry, I am well-aware of the difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T17:52:42-07:00","id":888704,"title":"","content":"I have a challenge for you. Consider it a stress test of your impending play-test pdf.<br /> <br /> Build Bowser Koopa as a character in the Orobori chronicles. He has a maiden (Princess Peach Toadstool), he turned an entire civilization of people into stone [bricks] (Edict? Dream Sorcery), and he's tormented by a nightmare vying for control of his province (Mario: The PLUMBER!). Their battle--of course--takes place in the Dreamtide.<br /> <br /> Give him stats, write a brief blurb about his motivations, and find a way to anchor it to the material world. Writers, go!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:53:09-07:00","id":889302,"title":"","content":"Well, we don't really have time to build a full sheet, with me pushing for a deadline of Sunday, but lessee..<br /> <b>General</b><br /> Method: Slayer<br /> Philosophy: Materialism<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> Dream Sorcery [4]<br /> Dreamtide Lair [6] (Mushroom Kingdom)<br /> - Note: The Mushroom Kingdom is an Island in the Dreamtide which Bowser and his Cult have taken over<br /> Cult [5] Koopas and Goombas (Note: Dreamtide creatures)<br /> Retainer [3] Kammy Koopa<br /> <br /> <b>Ablutions</b><br /> Scales [5]<br /> Spines [3]<br /> Inferno [3]<br /> Roar [2]<br /> Talons [2]<br /> Colossal [3]<br /> <br /> <b>Purviews (needs work)</b><br /> Money [3] - ? ?<br /> ? [] - ??<br /> <br /> <b>Other Traits</b><br /> Heartstring [5]<br /> Conviction [10] (Full-On Hubris)<br /> Conditions:<br /> - Hunted (Mario &amp; Luigi)<br /> - Madness<br /> - Missing Emotion: Conscience (Traded to Deep One)<br /> - Human-Guise degradation: skin and hair becoming noticeably abnormal, while his hands become increasingly shriveled and claw-like.<br /> <br /> <b>Other</b><br /> Peach would be a 3-dot maiden, but is lost merit dots, seeing as she hates him now.<br /> The Kids would all be well-groomed Pilot Lights, with Baby Bowser the inherritor-apparent.<br /> Mario would be a Hunter with Lucid Dream and Dream Travel.<br /> <br /> <b>Bio</b><br /> Bowser got his Heart a long time ago, but due to the Reimagining, it's no longer important: the man he used to be is long gone. The CEO has been considered a successful businessman with a reputation for ruthlessness and self-importance, but was able to maintain his composure in private. He had a beautiful and kind wife named Peach, his &quot;princess&quot;, who kept his head level at the worst of times (Maiden 3) Their best friends were a pair of brothers (Hunters) who knew his secret and shared the couple's love for Go Karting, and the 4 of them had built their own private island in the Dreamtide. It was the presidential bid where he went too far: by running under the platform of a childish bigot, people began to see him as a rambling egomaniac, and soon, the weight of more than a nation full of people afflicted him with the Reimagining, turning him into a monster.<br /> <br /> Bowser used to be close to Peach, and would call her his &quot;princess&quot;, but she turned on him when his Hubris became to great and his life in the Dreamtide made him increasingly less human. When he traded his Conscience to the Deep Ones, that was the final straw. When she tried to leave, he kidnapped her in a dream, dragging her off into his lair, putting her waking body in a persistent coma. Her mind is now trapped in a prison in the Dreamtide, and she will never wake up unless she can escape.<br /> <br /> Mario is a Hunter with Lucid Dream, Dream Travel, and a few other merits which make him nigh-unkillable in the upper-Dreamtide. He and his brother Luigi (another Hunter with similar stats) are now trying to get Peach back, and reform Bowser from his old ways, but they're starting to realize that he may be too far gone, and Mario is struggling with the fear that he may have to kill his old friend at this point...<br /> <br /> Bowser is currently trying to keep control of the Mushroom Kingdom, while simultaneously attempting to win the US Presidential Election. As it goes on, however, he falls more and more into madness, especially as comedians attempting to satire him continue to invoke the Reimagining: for example, constant satirical comparisons to Hitler have turned him into a Hitler sympathizer. As he changes, their satire gets more extreme, catching him in a never ending feedback loop.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, unbeknownst to them, the ripples of what's going on in the Mushroom Kingdom are slowly making their way across the Dreamtide. Both the Waking and Pandemonium are beginning to be affected by their little private war, but much more troubling to some scholars among the Deep Ones is that the ripples are gaining strength as the battle wages on, and if they were to reach What Lies Beyond, the realm where even the eldest of the Deep Ones do not dare to trespass.... The Deep Ones aren't exactly the kind to just hope that the Old Gods are heavy sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 06-20-2016, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T16:57:47-07:00","id":889467,"title":"","content":"Nice.<br /> <br /> I'm curious; can Maidens be used as open gates to/from the Dreamtide? When I pitched the challenge I too considered that Peach might be comatose, and I was wondering if that might be one of the benefits of the new merit-based form of that advantage. I'm also wondering... did he create the Dreamtide creatures or did he simply mold existing entities into more favorable shapes with his sorcery?<br /> <br /> Modelling prominent media figures like this is a good test of what the system can handle, and you're off to a great start. I'll try to think up another challenge once your test draft is ready (and others can take a shot at this first one once the material is available, if they so desire).<br /> <br /> Cool!<br /> <br /> Cool cool cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T22:36:14-07:00","id":889667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=889467#post889467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious; can Maidens be used as open gates to/from the Dreamtide?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's Dream Sorcery. Maidens are sources of stability. The Maiden merit is currently as follows...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Maiden (Varies)</span></span></b> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A Human Mortal who\u2019s company and opinion is of importance to the Oroboros, and can prevent them from falling too far into Guilt or Hubris with Praise and Admonishment respectively. This Maiden might be a simple one-dot friend who knows something of the character\u2019s exploits, or a several-dot companion who is able to deal with all the crap they go through on a regular basis, perhaps even with some supernatural ability of their own, such as Spirit Sight or Telekinesis. The one requirement is that they ARE a human Mortal: no Supernatural Creatures.</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Because of this Mortality and weakness, Oroboroi tend to be very protective of their \u201cmaidens\u201d, and (especially at high Hubris) may even resort to holding them against their will rather than lose them. Other Oroboroi can see this connection. In fact, they SMELL of Dragon, which tips off most entities with some sense of the supernatural that they are protected. While Oroboroi generally do not screw with each other\u2019s Maidens as a matter of conduct, it is a GAPING weakness that an Oroboros cares about this person, and they MAY be used as leverage by the unscrupulous. Anyone doing so, however, had better bring an army, </span></span></span></b><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">because that sort of behavior tends to piss off a bit more than one Oroboros</span></span></span></b><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">...</span></span></span></b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I pitched the challenge I too considered that Peach might be comatose, and I was wondering if that might be one of the benefits of the new merit-based form of that advantage. </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna be fair here, I'll have to recheck Second Sight on what happens if your dreaming form gets imprisoned in the Dreamtide. This just seemed reasonable... But no, the Dream Sorcery Merit is currently as follows...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Dream Sorcery</span></span></b> <b><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Requirements: Occult (3)OR be an Oroboros</span></span></span></b></b><br /><br /> <b><b><img src=\"https://lh5.googleusercontent.com/sROemjZFA_yUFbHGc1Q61reKDomzHhwc-7pRsM86MRn4JoiJTzRdzch7ZDcBnxVVzE2DhAEGyoGqeydPp8i1c1kttJ8GgYoeq6towFYo0F4JHLlpJg4CRlAJ-uZ65JR8xiyZiIHD\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></b></b><br /><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Dreamtide may be removed from the Waking, but it is not inaccessible, even to mortals. The character who possesses this merit understands the forces at play between this reality and the one beyond the miasma, and is able to affect it with various rituals. Most often, these require what these occultists call\u201cMaterialized Dreamstuff\u201d and \u201cImplements\u201d. Materialized Dreamstuff is a potent material from the Dreamtide which has gained full presence in the Waking, such as the blood of an Oroboros in True Form (1 Lethal), and Implement is something which can directly interact with non-material Dreamstuff, such as an enchanted or Jadeite Daggar.</span></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">1 Dot - Dream Sense</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - for a single point of Willpower, the Sorcerer can activate Dream Sense, allowing them to track down and see dreamstuff and dreamers in the Waking, and allowing them to better navigate the Dreamtide itself.</span></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">2 Dot - Dream Manipulation</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - For Willpower, a caster can hack new elements into a Dream or alter Dreamstuff. Problems that can happen include the dreamer resisting, the dreamer noticing, or the wrong thing being hacked in.</span></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3 Dot - Object Permanence</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - By coating an object taken from the dreamtide with Materialized Dreamstuff, it will become permanent, and will stay in existence even when not in sight or mind.</span></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">4 Dot - Dream Portal</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - The sorcerer knows enough about the Miasma to open portals to the Dreamtide. There are many ways to do this, but the most common two involve a dreamer or materialized dreamstuff. (like the blood of a True Form Oroboros) Either way has it\u2019s own risks associated, as the portal not only allows the sorcerer and their companions to enter and exit the Dreamtide, but anyone and any</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">thing</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> else as well.</span></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> </span></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Entering the Dreamtide requires the enterer to know what they\u2019re doing, either through training or instinct (like the Oroboroi), to suspend all disbelief of what is happening, and to spend a point of willpower to bridge the gap between them and the Dreamtide.</span></span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Through a Dreamer</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - To enter the Dreamtide through a Dreamer, directly into their Dream, only requires the Sorcerer to draw a series of concentric circles around where the Dreamer\u2019s head is using Materialized Dreamstuff. Once everything is in place, anyone who knows how can simply walk in and out of their Dream as if it were a staircase into their head.</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Direct Portal</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - Entering without a Dreamer is more complicated and dangerous. First, a wall of floor must be cleaned of impurities: covering it with good quality paper works. Next, the sorcerer uses Materialized Dreamstuff to draw a flat ovoid with pointed sides and, inside that, a near-perfect circle. Finally, the sorcerer takes their Implement and uses it to carve a line straight down the center of the circle. Entering the Dreamtide is achieved by slipping through the crack.</span></span></span></b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also wondering... did he create the Dreamtide creatures or did he simply mold existing entities into more favorable shapes with his sorcery? </div> </div> </div>I dunno. I'm sure he could do either, but I'd say the Mushroom kingdom was like that when they found it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll try to think up another challenge once your test draft is ready (and others can take a shot at this first one once the material is available, if they so desire). </div> </div> </div>How about you take the first draft and make some characters yourself, or maybe send me your Skype name, and I'll add you to the project...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T22:40:36-07:00","id":889670,"title":"","content":"The challenge should have been to make these guys...<br /> <img src=\"http://www.nelvana.com/content/assets/shows/blazing-dragons/gallery/197/BD001_SA_01_EP001_big.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:10:11-07:00","id":889688,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Now in meme form, because this game is really about who can get the dankest memes.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/6x2w99vy9/Dragon_Expectations.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:24:24-07:00","id":889693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=889670#post889670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The challenge should have been to make these guys...<br /> <img src=\"http://www.nelvana.com/content/assets/shows/blazing-dragons/gallery/197/BD001_SA_01_EP001_big.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Blazing Dragons! I had the Monty Python game based on it (bearing the same name) for the Playstation 1, but I'm familiar with the source material as well.<br /> <br /> I'm not qualified to build characters in Chronicles of Darkness; I never mastered the new rule-set and that's part of the reason the last phase of development fell apart. I don't have a Skype account either, so I'll just watch from here... if you don't mind.<br /> (You're right, your meme there pretty much sums it up. Bonus points!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:47:09-07:00","id":889698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=889693#post889693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not qualified to build characters in Chronicles of Darkness; I never mastered the new rule-set</div> </div> </div> </div>What? They only changed like, 5 things...<br /> Go read the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">GMC Rules Update. (It's free)</a> It'll tell you everything...<br /> <br /> Edit: I only know about Blazing Dragons because I kept seeing pictures of it in searched for &quot;Dragon Knight&quot; stuff...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 05-13-2016, 03:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T17:08:15-07:00","id":890265,"title":"","content":"Very well. I have the GMC update and I read it in its entirety; most of my aversion to character creation was founded in the changes to merits.<br /> <br /> I'll take your challenge and do Blazing Dragons. I'm going to build off of the video game, since it had a more focused story and I'm less familiar with the television show from whence your internet search yielded its quarry. I also don't have access to your document (You didn't share the google docs folder in the thread), so I'm going to wing this. Feel free to correct mechanic misunderstandings or to harvest concepts for new player options.<br /> <br /> <br /> First, some groundwork. Keep in mind I'm embellishing for the purpose of putting the setting into Chronicles of Darkness; the source material isn't nearly this grim:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Camelhot</u></b><br /> Centuries ago (more than a few, less than a bunch) a group of mining serfs working and living in a secluded valley unearthed a vein of buried Orobori Hearts, consumed them, and became dragons. They used their new-found power to overthrow their leaders and drive them out of the valley. The leader of the group took the title of King and a new name: Allfire. He declared that he and the others would found a new nation of gods in that very valley, and only dragons would ever be allowed to dwell there.<br /> As a mockery of (then) popular culture, this new kingdom was named CamelHOT (as a jab against King Arthur Pendragon) and Allfire declared the other dragons would be his Knights of the SQUARE Table (where everyone is equally spaced from each other... unless you happen to be seated at a corner).<br /> <br /> Centuries passed and the little valley of Camelhot remained isolated from the rest of the world. Allfire's knights would incinerate almost every human who wandered into the valley; those who survived the assault were presented before the king and either offered to swear fealty (and given a Heart from the mine) or--if they refused--were roasted like chickens. Eventually the population swelled, the secrets of the mines were obscured, and everyone forgot that they used to be human beings. Only Allfire remembers, and his encroaching senility risks the doom of their entire settlement. To that end, he's begun the pursuit of a successor king, promising his lands and the hand of his daughter Flame in marriage to the most worthy knight in his kingdom.<br /> <br /> The Orobori of Camelhot subsist entirely on coal, to such an extent that they consume nothing else for their sustenance. This has also lead them all to the false belief that they must eat coal to be able to breathe fire. All Camelhot Orobori are green and have six limbs: they are quadrupedal and do not possess wings. They are also deathly afraid of getting wet, and are no longer aware they have human forms. All of these are facets of the reimagining enforced by their constant exposure to their neighbors. Only Allfire remains aware of their real physical characteristics. Whenever a child is born, Allfire has it brought to the castle and feeds it a Heart from the mine; the villagers have come to believe the strange, tailless, pink babies they have appear as such because they have not yet been blessed by the king (and to an extent they are correct). Therefore, every dragon in Camelhot save Allfire and his first knights are Inheritors.<br /> <br /> The vein of Orobori Hearts originally unearthed in the mine is a deep concern for the king; as he aged and researched his new power he became suspicious of the numerous quantity of Hearts--not a natural mineral deposit--buried in the earth of his valley. He has come to believe the mine was originally a mass grave or--more disturbingly--a trophy room for some unknown entity. He frets constantly about what would happen if the latter were true and its owner came back for its prizes. This is of greatest concern because Allfire unearthed a scepter within the mine with the peculiar property of being able to meld machinery with flesh.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> Now, I'll build Flicker (The Inventor; he's the one in the middle of that first picture).<br /> &quot;If Necessity is the mother of invention, then certainly Albert is the father of invention. They're such a great couple... I wonder why they never had any kids.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>General</b><br /> Method: Inheritor<br /> Philosophy: ?<br /> <br /> <b>Merits</b><br /> Dream Sorcery [3] - Restricted: Inventions<br /> Hoard [2] - Random Junk<br /> Virtuous [2] - Humble, Ambitious<br /> Professional Training [2] - Technician<br /> <br /> <b>Ablutions</b><br /> Scales [1]<br /> Inferno [1]<br /> Talons [1]<br /> ?<br /> <br /> <b>Purviews</b><br /> Rigging? [3] - Allows the Oroboros to craft increasingly complex gadgets out of increasingly mundane components (It's the McGyver power). ...This may be covered by the Metal Purview, actually.<br /> <br /> <b>Other Traits</b><br /> Conviction [?] (Inklings of humanity)<br /> Conditions:<br /> - Leveraged (Allfire: serfdom)<br /> - Reimagining (Denizen of Camelhot) - Flicker is green, has six limbs [four legs, two arms] and is wingless, like all other denizens of Camelhot<br /> - Reimagining (Feeble, Brawn over Brains) - As an inventor Flicker is frequently mocked by the other denizens of Camelhot as being feeble and worthless; he suffers -2 to all Physical rolls but gains a beat upon succeeding.<br /> <br /> <b>Bio</b><br /> Flicker, like other denizens of Camelhot, received his Heart directly from Allfire when he was just a baby. As such, he has no awareness of his human guise or his relationship to the world outside of the valley. He's an inventor on retainer in Allfire's castle, but his inventions go largely unnoticed because of the nature of the kingdom and its denizens. He has a knack for putting things together out of mundane components; even having built an automatic steam-powered dishwasher out of tea kettles, a candelabra, a leg warmer, a cup rack, and a mop.<br /> Flicker is secretly infatuated with Allfire's daughter Flame, though he cannot interact with her in an official capacity due to his social standing. He loathes the notion that she will be a prize for one of the Square Table's knights and longs to find a way to spare her from that obligation.<br /> His inventions have recently caught the intention of the court chancellor, who is conspiring with a group of humans beyond the valley to stage a coup and overthrow Allfire's reign.<br /> ---<br /> <br /> There, challenge met. ^_^<br /> (FYI for anybody doing internet searches: the above is a fair use adaptation of intellectual property copywritten by Terry Jones, and is presented here both for the purpose of satire and as a test of content present in the Chronicles of Darknesss fan project <b>The Orobori Chronicles</b> [a fair use adaptation of Onyx Path Publications' intellectual property]. This and Raccoon's previous exploration of Bowser Koopa [again, a fair use adaptation of Nintendo's intellectual property] are purely for demonstration of concept and will not be included in the final document.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T18:50:37-07:00","id":890330,"title":"","content":"Multiple Limbs is an Ablution.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890265#post890265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also don't have access to your document (You didn't share the google docs folder in the thread), so I'm going to wing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>You never wanted to be added. If you sent me your google drive account, I'd add you. I've asked you for your Skype too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 05-13-2016, 09:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T00:17:13-07:00","id":890472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890265#post890265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">most of my aversion to character creation was founded in the changes to merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Merits actually weren't changed much in that book, if you followed the errata...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll take your challenge and do Blazing Dragons. </div> </div> </div>I was joking, but ok.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Centuries ago (more than a few, less than a bunch) a group of mining serfs working and living in a secluded valley unearthed a vein of buried Orobori Hearts, consumed them, and became dragons. </div> </div> </div>I dunno why they'd be there, because a shitload of Dragons or Oroboroi would've had to put them there, and then True-Died but ok...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a mockery of (then) popular culture, this new kingdom was named CamelHOT (as a jab against King Arthur Pendragon) and Allfire declared the other dragons would be his Knights of the SQUARE Table (where everyone is equally spaced from each other... unless you happen to be seated at a corner). </div> </div> </div>This sounds not only like something that could start out silly and become serious, but has a basis in reality: the KKK manual was originally filled with things that were jokes, with absurd names like &quot;Grand Wizard&quot;, and bizarre rituals, but which today are dead serious. And that was only founded 150 years ago: there are people alive today who could have met the founders!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Centuries passed and the little valley of Camelhot remained isolated from the rest of the world. Allfire's knights would incinerate almost every human who wandered into the valley; those who survived the assault were presented before the king and either offered to swear fealty (and given a Heart from the mine) or--if they refused--were roasted like chickens. </div> </div> </div>I sense alot of Hubris Breaking-Points and Conditions, seeing as Oroboroi are still mostly human, at least mentally, and tend to not just murder people lightly unless they've gone off the deep end...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eventually the population swelled, the secrets of the mines were obscured, and everyone forgot that they used to be human beings. </div> </div> </div>Or just, you know, never learned how to assume Human Guise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only Allfire remembers, and his encroaching senility risks the doom of their entire settlement. </div> </div> </div>Solution: Kill him, wait for him to wake up, should fix the age problem, seeing as they re-form to the age they were turned at now, whether they die of being boiled in acid, starvation, or old age...<br /> <br /> Maybe he was Reimagined though...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Orobori of Camelhot subsist entirely on coal, to such an extent that they consume nothing else for their sustenance. </div> </div> </div>Except that won't work, because they still need to sustain their physical form: they spend a breath point per day to keep the Heart from going dormant, and still need to eat for themselves to not starve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All Camelhot Orobori are green and have six limbs: they are quadrupedal and do not possess wings. </div> </div> </div>Ablution: Extra Limbs [2]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are also deathly afraid of getting wet, and are no longer aware they have human forms. </div> </div> </div>They may not be able to take them anymore: if they never tried, they never did, and they may have just been reimagined away...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whenever a child is born, Allfire has it brought to the castle and feeds it a Heart from the mine; the villagers have come to believe the strange, tailless, pink babies they have appear as such because they have not yet been blessed by the king (and to an extent they are correct). Therefore, every dragon in Camelhot save Allfire and his first knights are Inheritors. </div> </div> </div>...Where do the babies come from? I'm not sure yet if Oroboroi can breed with each other... We haven't decided...<br /> <br /> Also, what are all those Hearts doing there? I mean, did some crazy Oroboroi just start collecting them and hoarding them in the ground for a few centuries??<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The vein of Orobori Hearts originally unearthed in the mine is a deep concern for the king; as he aged and researched his new power he became suspicious of the numerous quantity of Hearts--not a natural mineral deposit--buried in the earth of his valley. He has come to believe the mine was originally a mass grave or--more disturbingly--a trophy room for some unknown entity. </div> </div> </div>OH. OK. YEAH, THAT LAMPSHADES IT.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is of greatest concern because Allfire unearthed a scepter within the mine with the peculiar property of being able to meld machinery with flesh. </div> </div> </div>Dreamtide Relic? DREEEAAMTIDE RELIC??<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Philosophy: ? </div> </div> </div>Materialism, Wisdom. or Sweat, because those are for more practical-minded characters...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dream Sorcery [3] - Restricted: Inventions </div> </div> </div>...Restricted? That's a thing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hoard [2] - Random Junk </div> </div> </div>We don't have this merit/mechanic in there right now. They just eat things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ablutions</b> </div> </div> </div>Multiple Limbs [2]<br /> Draconic Intelligence [?]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Purviews</b> </div> </div> </div>Probably Knowledge or Industry....<br /> <br /> Here is the list of primary purviews:<ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ash - Ruin, Agony, Hysteria, Rampage</span></span></b></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Blood - Oath, Justice, Polygraph</span></span></b></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sweat - Industry, Agony, Property</span></span></b></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bone - Hippocratic, Assembly, Polygraph</span></span></b></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tears - Passion, Hysteria, Rampage, Trance</span></span></b></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wisdom - Knowledge, Polygraph, Trance</span></span></b></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Materialism - Currency, Justice, Property</span></span></b></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Nihilism - Void</span></span></b></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Conviction [?] (Inklings of humanity) </div> </div> </div>Conviction is this: What's his self-esteem like? He doesn't liken himself to a god, so it's under 7, and he;s not wallowing in self-loathing, so it's over 3. I'd go with the mildly-wimpy 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There, challenge met. ^_^ </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure, I didn't really think too much about it when I posted, but yeah, I guess that was a challenge...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 05-15-2016, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T21:16:50-07:00","id":891565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890472#post890472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno why they'd be there, because a shitload of Dragons or Oroboroi would've had to put them there, and then True-Died but ok...<br /> <br /> Also, what are all those Hearts doing there? I mean, did some crazy Oroboroi just start collecting them and hoarding them in the ground for a few centuries??<br /> <br /> OH. OK. YEAH, THAT LAMPSHADES IT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhm. Looming dangerous intrigue; who put the hearts there and what happens when they come back and find them missing?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890472#post890472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sense alot of Hubris Breaking-Points and Conditions, seeing as Oroboroi are still mostly human, at least mentally, and tend to not just murder people lightly unless they've gone off the deep end...</div> </div> </div> </div>But they're not murdering willy-nilly. They're roaming around in dragon form and, when seen, would likely be attacked immediately. Most of the deaths are in self-defense, and though failure to swear allegiance resulting in death might seem inhuman it is done in the effort to protect the secrets of the valley.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890472#post890472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or just, you know, never learned how to assume Human Guise.<br /> <br /> They may not be able to take them anymore: if they never tried, they never did, and they may have just been reimagined away...</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't realize that was a thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890472#post890472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solution: Kill him, wait for him to wake up, should fix the age problem, seeing as they re-form to the age they were turned at now, whether they die of being boiled in acid, starvation, or old age...<br /> <br /> Maybe he was Reimagined though...</div> </div> </div> </div>Killing him would resolve the senility if it was a physical ailment, but what if it was psychological? Allfire's senility might come from his fears about the mine or even from the fatigue of centuries and centuries of the burden of leadership. Does death remove mental conditions from an Oroboros?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890472#post890472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that won't work, because they still need to sustain their physical form: they spend a breath point per day to keep the Heart from going dormant, and still need to eat for themselves to not starve.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so they can't sustain their physical bodies with fossil fuels anymore? Bummer, that harpoons the mirrors apocalypse setting for them (Gods of abandoned banks and gas stations). Oh well, you're the boss. Camelhot grows corn (for popcorn) in the game, so maybe the Orobori version sustains themselves on an agricultural diet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890472#post890472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ablution: Extra Limbs [2]</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, so Extra Limbs is making a comeback? I hope you've been able to make it more useful than I did in its previous incarnation.<br /> <br /> If they can't produce biological offspring, then Camelhot becomes even more gruesome as a setting since Allfire would need to kidnap babies for this purpose.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890472#post890472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Where do the babies come from? I'm not sure yet if Oroboroi can breed with each other... We haven't decided...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I was under the impression they could breed but would only produce human offspring (or at best, near-humans with 5-chambered hearts). This was the way they worked in previous incarnations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890472#post890472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Restricted? That's a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. It's just a condition prohibiting the use of an ability if it doesn't meet certain criteria. Bans fall into this category. I've simply applied that concept here, since Flicker is an inventor and his creations are often whimsical (explained as the result of dream sorcery), but he doesn't go about mucking in other peoples' dreams.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890472#post890472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don't have this merit/mechanic in there right now. They just eat things.</div> </div> </div> </div>But... But... Dragons love to sleep on their collectibles! It's one of the greatest depictions of them in western artwork; great beasts snoring atop glittering piles of gold!<br /> Except in this case, the piles would be more flexible than that.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'm sad to see Hoard go as a merit and I hope you reconsider.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=890472#post890472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dreamtide Relic? DREEEAAMTIDE RELIC??</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I was picturing something involving the God Machine~<br /> Err, uh, I mean, SURE! Yeah! Totally a Dreamtide Relic.<br /> <br /> In the video game, Sir George (a human) is vying to take over Camelhot for its jewel mine (In Blazing Dragons the dragons eat jewels instead of food, but George wants them to be rich). He lacks the forces to face the dragons directly, though, as the Knights of the Square Table are very powerful (even if they are lazy) and George's peons are wimpy (You would be too if you were constantly being set on fire).<br /> To get around the military option (which isn't working), Sir George and his court wizard Mervin plot to win the kingdom in Allfire's tournament. However, only dragon knights are permitted to compete. To that end, Mervin sets about building an artificial Black Dragon to compete on George's behalf.<br /> The first Black Dragon is powered by a hamster wheel and George's dog. When that one is destroyed, Camelhot's chancellor (hoping to profit from the coup) learns of Flicker's steam engine and steals the plans, sending them to Mervin to be used in the construction of a Black Dragon 2 (The sequel!). After THAT mechanized dragon fails (but not before thoroughly smashing the tournament grounds), Mervin gets his hands on Allfire's scepter. Sir George demands another Black Dragon from his 'worthless' wizard and--in a fit of rage--Mervin uses the staff to merge Sir George with the broken scraps of the Black Dragon 2.<br /> So that's what I was paying homage to here; a scepter which fuses machinery to flesh. Seems very &quot;God Machine&quot;-esque to me, but I guess it fits the Dreamtide too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ===<br /> In regards to your earlier post, I do not have Skype on my computer, I have not registered with Skype, and I have no intention of using Skype. I can't give you my Skype ID because it does not exist. I don't mean to be harsh in saying such--I've told you twice I didn't have Skype and I think perhaps what I meant was unclear. I didn't mean I didn't have <i>your</i> Skype and therefore could not connect to you (which is what your response implies you interpreted); I meant I do not use that program and therefore have no Skype information to give. Hopefully that's cleared up now.<br /> <br /> As for my statement about lack of access to the document, I had figured you would post a link to your google drive folder with view permissions (not edit permissions) so that everyone who comes to the thread could see what you're working on. If such is not to be the case, oh well; no harm done.<br /> I want to be clear that I'm not interested in having edit privileges on your document. If you are requesting a google account to contact for that purpose I have to decline. If the google account is only to view the documents I'll consider sending one privately; I haven't decided if I want to peek behind the curtain or if I want to wait and experience your work with the rest of the public when it's ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:40:18-07:00","id":892112,"title":"","content":"Well... Speaking of docs, I'm actually on to make an announcement.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">We're going to have a first draft of the Transitional Rulebook up by tonight.</span></span></b><br /> <br /> So there's that...<br /> <br /> Anyone excited to see that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:58:41-07:00","id":892153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=892112#post892112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... Speaking of docs, I'm actually on to make an announcement.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">We're going to have a first draft of the Transitional Rulebook up by tonight.</span></span></b><br /> <br /> So there's that...<br /> <br /> Anyone excited to see that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Very much yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T00:57:38-07:00","id":892371,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I feel bad about this, but I'm a bit of a control freak, and want to read through the book from beginning to end before releasing it...<br /> <br /> ...And right now I'm incredibly sick with something that's making that impossible.<br /> <br /> Sorry guys, you're gonna have to wait another 48 hours <i>at most</i> for this... &gt;!&gt;;;<br /> <br /> <br /> In the mean time, I'll give you something that'll help you get an idea of what you need to change to bring over a character from the old books. I'd appreciate feedback on this, and remember that we're still open to changing things in the next 48 hours.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Major Changes between Embers: 2nd Edition and Rekindled: Transitional Edition.</b></span></span><br /> <b>(AKA, the most important parts of the book)</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>New Focus</b></u></span><br /> Rather than being a game about a specific view of Leadership, Dragon Rekindled is a game about <i><b>POWER</b></i> in general:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Why you want it.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">How you take it.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">What you do with it.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">And the monster (or savior) it turns you into...</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Also, we've added elements like...</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Secret Lore</b> which backs up what's going on and makes the whole thing much deeper and more mysterious.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Philosophy</b> references from people who talked about power, like Nietzsche, Ayn Rand, and Anton LaVey.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Exploration of Fantasy</b> from the meta-perspective of Concept itself: the kind of power the Oroboroi have is based entirely around bringing ideas into reality, both fantasies and hard facts.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">More emphasis on themes like <b>Power</b>, <b>Domination</b>, <b>Corruption</b>, <b>Hubris</b>, <b>Responsibility</b>, <b>Guilt</b>, and <b>The Inevitable Fall</b>.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>New Merits</b></u></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Maiden</b> - A </span><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mortal who knows the Oroboros for who they truly are, and can keep them from swinging too far down one path or another, as well as be a human accomplice in their supernatural dealings.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Cult</b> - A group of Mortals who have some idea of what's going on, and follow the Oroboros as a divine leader.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>PR Campaign</b> - Allows an Oroboros to directly manipulate their Public Image for the Reimagining.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Contingency Plan</b> - How well you've set up for the long haul: investments, identities, conspiracies, etc.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dream Sorcery</b> - 1 to 4 dots (I've posted it already)</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oroboroi get it for free, but Mortals and other Supernaturals can use it as well.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>New Philosophies</b></u></span><br /> Methods are about how you take power, but Philosophies are about WHY you took it in the first place. They embody what is most important to an Oroboros when they first change.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ash</b> - Revolutionaries who thrive on the Destruction of whatever they don't like.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Blood</b> - Honor-hounds who enforce their own morals.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Coin</b> (new) - Materialists who believe that wealth and resources are the most important things in the world. This can mean many things, from a Banking Executive who hoards wealth, to the Communist revolutionary attempting to overthrow him, to the Charity Worker desperately trying to acquire the funds to keep the shelters running. All of them are accountants who see that wealth is what moves the world.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Sweat</b> - Work Ethic, Industry, Inspiration, and Pride.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Bone</b> - Symbols of stability, who are experts in holding things together.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Tears</b> - Believe that emotions are really what matters.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Book</b> (new) - Believe that knowledge is the greatest power, and that all problems can be solved with fact. They are occultists, scientists, thinkers, and teachers, and their signature Purview, Knowledge, deals with gaining, spreading, and secluding information.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Nihilism</b> - Power without reason: they believe that there is nothing of worth in the universe, and have no reason to use their powers for anything but subversion of meaning itself. Not all of them are neccesarily bad, but among the highest leaders of the great organizations, they are considered a threat to everything an Oroboros should stand for.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Note that schools of the 5 Evils have been shuffled back into the others, and the True Heart Schools are no longer relevant. (for now, at least...)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>Ablutions</b></u></span><br /> They haven't really changed much. The &quot;odd-even&quot; ones are now just boosts to both skills, and the new starting points are a little different:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3 Points from the <b>Common</b> list</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3 Points from the <b>Method</b> list</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3 Points from any <b>Oroboros</b> list</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3 Points from the <b>Storyteller</b> due to Public Image</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">New Ablutions are mainly following the rule that every list has...</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>A Type of Breath</b>: Common is Fire, Slayers get Ice, Finders get a mist of Perception, Tricksters get &quot;sleeping sand&quot;, and the other two haven't been fleshed out enough.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>An Attribute-Booster</b> which takes breath to boost the Method-Attribute for a scene.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ablutions which are both positive and negative</b>, because there was too much emphasis on Inherritors being good and Tricksters being bad. Now they all have potential for both.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>Changing Edicts to Purviews</b></u></span><br /> Functionally the same, and 90% unchanged, only more streamlined towards both positive and negative ends, and built to better reflect the Philosophies. &quot;Due Process&quot; is now &quot;Justice&quot; which allows an Oroboros to not simply hide a crime, but reveal it as well.<br /> <br /> Each Philosophy starts with a dot of its own specific purviews (as opposed to a single Edict you had to take) and one from any they chose.<br /> <br /> The signature Purviews for each Philosophy are currently...</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ash</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - Ruin, Agony, Hysteria, Rampage</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Blood</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - Oath, Justice, Polygraph</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sweat</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - Industry, Agony, Property</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bone </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">- Hippocratic, Assembly, Polygraph</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Tears</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - Passion, Hysteria, Rampage, Trance</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Wisdom</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - Knowledge, Polygraph, Trance</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Materialism</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - Currency, Justice, Property</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Nihilism</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> - Void</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><u>Heartstring replaces Furnace</u></b></span><br /> Power Stats represent the strength of the source of a character's supernatural powers, but an Oroboros's Heart doesn't actually change with them. The thing that does is how well they're connected to it: their Heartstring.<br /> <br /> Higher Heartstring means...</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Larger breath pool, more breath per turn.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Stats can go above 5 once Heartstring does.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Greater Distance from the Heart</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Early on, you can maybe cross town.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Later, you might be able to leave it on the other side of the county.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">At 10, you can go to the other side of the planet... assuming you don't <i>leave</i> the planet.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">More potent Reimagining</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">At 1 and 2, Ablution dots are on the table.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">3, 4, and 5 add other physical characteristics to the chopping block.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">6, 7, and 8 add skills, merits, personality quirks, and mannerisms. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">at 9 and 10, the very attributes and personality of an Oroboros can be altered.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>Oroboros Integrity: Conviction</b></u></span><br /> <b>Conviction</b> represents how the Oroboros feels about themselves, from the over-inflated extreme of Hubris, to the self-loathing Guilt. A Conviction of 5 represents an Oroboros who isn't going off the deep end of either extreme, however, each extremes have their own utility.<br /> <br /> <b>Hubris</b> has the benefit of strong Self-Image, which allows them to add every point above 5 against the Reimagining, but are prone to Hoarding, Rage, and other forms of Hubris. At the extremes of 9 and 10, an Oroboros has such a high image of herself, that she'll find it hard to resist the proposals of Challengers. Breaking points for this include anything that </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">reinforc</span></span></span></b><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">es the idea that an Oroboros is a god</span></span></span></b><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, either through her own action or a reaction to her actions</span></span></span></b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">.<br /> <br /> <b>Guilt</b> has the benefit of desperation, and the Oroboros gains a free point of Willpower once per scene for any action which would trigger a breaking point towards Hubris (assuming she's drop below 4), but the drawback is the Reimagining becoming more potent as she spirals towards someone who may not even want to protect her own identity. At the extremes of 1 and 0, an Oroboros will begin seeking a new, better owner for her Heart, and will start looking for an Inherritor. Breaking points for this include any time an Oroboros fails to live up to the power she has willfully usurped from another.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">New Traits</span></b></u></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Nutrition</b> - Oroboroi need to eat enough to nutritionally sustain themselves before they can garner breath. This becomes more potent as Divinity rises.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Eating for Calories</b> - The &quot;refueling&quot; roll is only required if an Oroboros consumes a non-food item for fuel, but not for broccoli.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Temperature</b> - Oroboroi are now immune to extreme temperatures and fire, but can still be frozen solid.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Toxicity</b> - Oroboroi blood is technically boiled every minute (that's how fast human blood circulates), meaning they're immune to anything that can't survive being supernaturally boiled, like most poisons and illnesses. That's just biology.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Heart Removal</b> - Is no longer as big of an issue: an Oroboros can take it out to hide it somewhere for a day, or eat it again to keep it in their chest, but there's no huge emphasis on how &quot;only a fool would take their one weakness and not put it somewhere where they can't keep an eye on it.&quot; An Oroboros can only travel a short distance from her Heart, depending on her Heartstring.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Immortality</b> - Oroboroi are immortal. Period. They age relatively slowly, but always resurrect at the age they became an Oroboros at, As long as the form can be rebuilt by the Heart, they can resurrect at any time.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Weaknesses</b> - Oroboroi are extremely susceptible to &quot;Dark Magic&quot; and Jade.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">And of course, the big new thing everyone seems to be asking about is...<br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>The Reimagining</b></u></span><br /> This is about the idea that others will always have some control how to use power, for better or for worse. Democracy, Public Opinion, Morale, Oversight... No man is an island, no matter how badly those with the most Hubris tell themselves.<br /> <br /> Here's how that works...</span></span> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Whenever an Oroboros feeds a point of Breath to keep the Heart beating, the Storyteller overlooks what their current &quot;Public Image&quot; is, to see what the potential changes are. Merits like Maiden, Cult, and PR Campaign can keep this in line.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The roll is based on a combination (through addition) of 3 things: how many people believe this new image, how strongly they believe it, and how tangible it is (for instance, simply saying &quot;I can imagine him as a pilot&quot; and &quot;I literally believe he has wings&quot; are a 1 and a 5 respectively)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">The Oroboros resists based on Resolve + Composure + however far above 5 their conviction is. (So, Tyrannical Dragons tend to be better at resisting)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">If the Reimagining Roll - the Resistance Roll is more than 0, the Oroboros gets a 1-dot change to whatever was on the table. If it's an exceptional success, it's 2 dots.</span></span></li> </ol><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Note that it becomes more potent at higher Heartstring, with low levels being ablutions, and higher levels being things like personality traits, HOWEVER, the Heart itself and things that are direct manifestations of the Heart (like the simple fact that they are an Oroboros) are permanent and cannot be affected by the Reimagining.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Aaaand</span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> that's it for now. Expect a rough draft of the Transitional Rulebook in the next 48 hours...<br /> - Racc0!0n</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 05-17-2016, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T00:21:24-07:00","id":893882,"title":"","content":"Running through it... Releasing it reeeeal soon....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T03:06:26-07:00","id":893927,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Alright, here it is, the current draft of the Transitional Rulebook, with (almost) everything you'd need to move an Oroboros over from <i>Dragon: The Embers - Second Edition</i>. I'm not entirely happy with it, but we're not going to sit on it any longer. Expect some obvious holes in the draft now, including (at the worst parts) references to 2nd edition, and some patches in the coming weeks as we move onto the full, 10-chapter, rulebook, which will probably take a few months. We're open to any questions or comments on this right now, but please remember <b>that this is neither a complete nor finalized set of rules</b>, just a document containing a solid idea of the direction we're heading in. We also don't have a character sheet up yet, but I'll have something usable up soon, and I'll be working with Mr Gone to develop a high quality one.<br /> <br /> That being said, have some Dragon stuff!</span></span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zh8dFoBLbWksCZd6Bhw3hXOpDaUhBidcFKoGX04fR5Q\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Dragon Rekindled: Transitional Edition</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#696969\">A set of rules for creating and playing an Oroboros in the post-God-Machine era...</span></span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zh8dFoBLbWksCZd6Bhw3hXOpDaUhBidcFKoGX04fR5Q\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">(This is a link to a Google Doc. Click it!)</span></span></a></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">In this book, we've put together a new set of rules for a new direction in the Dragon line, which will be refined and continued upon in the months leading up to the full version of Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><u>Chapters</u></b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Introduction</b> - Containing all the things they normally do.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Chapter 1: Lore</b> - Contains all the information a starting-level Oroboros would be privy to.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Chapter 2: Character Creation</b> - New character rules, new Method stuff, new Philosophies, and new Ablution and Purview lists.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Chapter 3: Playing <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">an Oroboros</span></b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"> - A detailed set of rules on how to use the character sheets in play.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Appendex 1: The Dreamtide</b> - A brief overview of the Dreamtide and the things that are found there.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Appendex 2: Crossover Rules</b> - A brief discussion of how an Oroboros might interact with the other Supernatural creatures.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>What's left to do here</b></u></span><br /> This is really an incomplete draft, as much as it has everything you'd need for most of it. There are a few things that need work...</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Clean up the Writing</b> - Some of it came out... Strange...</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Get the Ablution and Purview lists fleshed out</b> - Because they're obviously incomplete and unbalanced.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Spend some time fleshing out some of the mechanics better</b> - They're kind of incomplete or vague in places they shouldn't be.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>The Team which put this together</b></u></span><br /> Note that everyone here was in a Skype chat, regularly meeting and discussing new mechanics and decisions.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Raccoon</b> - Project Head</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Shock</b> - Creative Counsel</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>AJF</b> - Primary Lore Writer</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Saulot</b> - Primary Mechanical Writer</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Nova</b> - Writer</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Darinas</b> - Also a Writer</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">And, of course, we lifted a large chunk of this from <i>Dragon: The Embers - Second Edition</i>, so they get credit here too...</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 05-19-2016, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T05:05:57-07:00","id":893949,"title":"","content":"I would just like to say that the project's existence and state is entirely due to Raccoon's excellent management. Caps off to you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T15:31:39-07:00","id":895708,"title":"","content":"So... We've been talking internally, and I've noticed there hasn't been alot of feedback on this...<br /> <br /> What are people's feelings on the changes? With this release, we were focusing alot on what could be new or different, but with the full release, we're talking about putting more stuff from Embers back in...<br /> <br /> Feedback please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T05:58:27-07:00","id":896034,"title":"","content":"It looks good so far but I do have a few problems 1. In the crossover rules you don't talk about many downsides with them working together aside from hunters. Even Princess the game designed to play white hat talks about how werewolves don't see murder like humans.<br /> And it's not like their isn't places for conflict a dragons blood may lead to a stable relationship but it can also lead to the vampire trying to kidnap the dragon and drain him for the rest of eternity.<br /> 2. In the previous embers games two dragons that kept their hearts in their bodies could have a dragon child. I liked it because it put part of the blame for their extinction on their own heads. If they weren't so greedy and self centered they may have been able to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1685-looker","name":"Looker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T00:24:58-07:00","id":896605,"title":"","content":"Like I said, I think the drawback of this version is that we're focusing on what can be different or new, and not on what makes the game complete. So yeah, there are gonna be holes like this.<br /> <br /> Anywhere there's a gap in these rules, refer to 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Looker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=896034#post896034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. In the crossover rules you don't talk about many downsides with them working together aside from hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Embers 2nd Edition, it talks all about what makes them fight. I wanted to talk about the possibilities of cooperation, because I like to see them work together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. In the previous embers games two dragons that kept their hearts in their bodies could have a dragon child. I liked it because it put part of the blame for their extinction on their own heads. If they weren't so greedy and self centered they may have been able to survive. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, we're toying with this one alot right now. In the end, we cut the references to it from this version so we'd have time to decide on where exactly we want to go with this...<br /> <br /> The full release will have an appendix devoted to this stuff, along with distinct character sheets with an array of powers, like Ghouls and Wolf-Blooded in their respective 2nd edition books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 05-23-2016, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T12:06:51-07:00","id":897045,"title":"","content":"I kind of think &quot;Create More Hearts&quot; (beyond making eggs) should be mostly a plot hook with some rules guidelines. It should come off as similar to a Mage's quest to unseat the Exarchs-ultimately impossible on a global scale (for Awakened, it's because the Exarchs are more idea than entity, for Dragons it's because it's way, way too easy to destroy a Heart permanently as opposed to creating another), but not a pointless one-it's quite possible to force the Seers into retreat and improve the lives of a city, so it should come off as being known to Ourobouri that they have found ways of cloning/summoning virgin Hearts into being, it just isn't easy and making a new one seems to be unique to each new Heart. Thus, draconic extinction is pushed a generation or so back, and they live to rule another day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T23:50:40-07:00","id":897614,"title":"","content":"One again, need to stress: this is a book about the core lore and mechanics of the game so far. Think of it as the Quickstart, or Playtesting Draft. The full book, which will take a few months, is going to have about 12 chapters filled with all sorts of extra lore, unanswered questions, antagonists, world-building, expanded mechanics, and pretty much all the story-fodder you'd need to run a Chronicle following a group of Usurpers from first discovering their Hearts all the way to the point where they retake the Dragon's former positions as Apex Predator of Pandemonium. (Much to the chagrin of any Deep Ones they don't happen to be on good terms with) I'm really happy you guys are excited about this stuff, but I'd be even happier to hear what you don't like about the core of what we've done.<br /> <br /> That being said...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Looker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=896034#post896034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. In the crossover rules you don't talk about many downsides with them working together aside from hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>To elaborate on what I said, expect the full book to have full mechanics and lore on their interactions, including fighting, friendship, and simple exchanges. For instance, we're looking into the idea that Purviews could be seen as some type of Arcana and Impositions are like Rotes, except the Oroboroi don't have to worry about Paradox or Disbelief, which would make interaction with Mages very interesting, whether through Purview-vs-Arcana combat or Cooperative-Spellcasting.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. In the previous embers games two dragons that kept their hearts in their bodies could have a dragon child. I liked it because it put part of the blame for their extinction on their own heads. </div> </div> </div>I liked that too, but whenever I play one, I just can't see them pulling their Hearts out unless they're being stupid or desperate: WHY would you EVER let the ONE THING THAT CAN KILL YOU out of your sight for a single moment? If you're an 8 ft tall walking Panzer Tank, what hiding spot could possibly be safer than inside of you? Yeah, it's still a thing, but the emphasis on how it's considered the only reasonable decision is gone for now...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=897045#post897045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of think &quot;Create More Hearts&quot; (beyond making eggs) should be mostly a plot hook with some rules guidelines. It should come off as similar to a Mage's quest to unseat the Exarchs-ultimately impossible on a global scale (for Awakened, it's because the Exarchs are more idea than entity, for Dragons it's because it's way, way too easy to destroy a Heart permanently as opposed to creating another), but not a pointless one-it's quite possible to force the Seers into retreat and improve the lives of a city, so it should come off as being known to Ourobouri that they have found ways of cloning/summoning virgin Hearts into being, it just isn't easy and making a new one seems to be unique to each new Heart. Thus, draconic extinction is pushed a generation or so back, and they live to rule another day.</div> </div> </div> </div>We've been talking about the possibility that Pilot Lights (which happen because two Oroboroi with their Hearts still intact can breed someone with a 1-chambered proto-Heart) might be grown into Oroboroi through multiple methods, such as feeding them the Hearts of 8 other Pilot Lights, or keeping them alive for long enough that you can grow that one chamber into 9.<br /> <br /> We've also been talking about the possibility of making Dragons the same way you'd make any other Dreamtide Creature: imagining them into being. Obviously, this needs both powerful Dreamtide Sorcery and a through understanding on what makes a Heart what it is, which poses a problem: what if, in learning such vast forbidden knowledge, the Oroboroi suddenly find a reason to not make the Hearts at all? What if they realize some horrifying truth about the Occult matters they're dealing with? What sort of deals might one have to make with the Deep Ones for the things they know about the Hearts and the Dreamtide? What if, in searching to fulfill this undertaking, they are somehow broken and left without purpose?<br /> <br /> Ever wonder where the Nihilists come from? ...Or what the Deep Ones REALLY are?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm really enjoying writing this stuff about Imagined Dragons looking for the Dankest Memes to try and become more Uber, even after we realized that World of Darkness is really just a more complicated version of Snakes and Ladders...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T00:52:48-07:00","id":901854,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Just so everyone knows, <b>we are currently looking for playtesters</b>. Anyone who wants to be in the official playtest while we work on the book, please submit an application now. We need 5 players: 1 for each method. You must be good at text roleplay, grammar, and character-based storytelling.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Also, have a Character Sheet</span></b></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LANnga4YxfyD8uXYBnqV0EuzuNHYlSdTARZJKZgW8VM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LANnga4YxfyD8uXYBnqV0EuzuNHYlSdTARZJKZgW8VM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LANnga4YxfyD8uXYBnqV0EuzuNHYlSdTARZJKZgW8VM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LANnga4YxfyD8uXYBnqV0EuzuNHYlSdTARZJKZgW8VM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And to remind you what this game is about...<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Sp1mVNOB5tg\" data-code=\"Sp1mVNOB5tg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Sp1mVNOB5tg/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T00:42:09-07:00","id":905449,"title":"","content":"So... Does anyone have any feedback or suggestions?<br /> <br /> You guys want us to tell you about anything in the new book? I could give you stats for a Deep One or something...<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/905458-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-official-playtest-ooc#post905458\">I made a thread for the official playtest!</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 06-02-2016, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:57:12-07:00","id":906057,"title":"","content":"Actually stats on a deep one sound cool. I am wondering how a dragon dark era would look plus what happens if a Beast visits a Dragon in their dreams and the horror is a Dragon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T22:58:01-07:00","id":906229,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, I noticed that the sheets I put out print differently depending on what's up, so I made a PNG version and doodled on it.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><a href=\"http://s6.postimg.org/bfsoay0e9/Sheet_Prototype.png\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Better Oroboros Sheet - Image Version</span></span></a></span></b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=906057#post906057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually stats on a deep one sound cool. I am wondering how a dragon dark era would look plus what happens if a Beast visits a Dragon in their dreams and the horror is a Dragon?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is like, 3 things, but ok, gimme a bit on them and I'll get them up eventually...<ul><li>Deep Ones we have copious notes on...</li> <li>Do you mean like, Oroboroi in the Dark Ages? 'cause we haven't gotten to that yet.</li> <li>I don't know enough about Beast yet to answer this. Ask Nova and Darinas...</li> </ul><br /> Anyone else want something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 06-04-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T01:13:49-07:00","id":906278,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\"><span style=\"color:#000080\"><b><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">D\u0339\u0356\u034eE\u032b\u031d\u0333\u0329\u0318\u032cE\u0339\u0345\u031d\u032eP\u031f\u0325 \u0323\u031f\u0347O\u032d\u0317\u0323\u0359\u0316\u0325N\u0320\u0317\u0319E\u0332 -\u0354\u0348 \u033a\u0331\u031d\u0333T\u034d\u0354\u0331h\u0339e\u0356\u032a\u0348\u034d \u032dDro\u032b\u033c\u0339\u0316\u0323w\u031e\u034d\u0348\u0323n\u032e\u031ei\u0333\u0325\u033bn\u035a\u0324\u0353\u0348g\u033b\u0325 \u0354\u031dH\u031d\u032a\u0319\u0355\u0324\u0329\u0330os\u0323\u0329\u0323\u033b\u0331\u0329\u0359t\u032d\u0320\u035a</span></b></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">The Deep Ones are dark and mysterious creatures from Pandemonium, the place where all things eventually come to rest at the bottom of the Dreamtide. They are creatures of pure potential, who can weave new concepts into their own forms at will, but cannot travel in the waking without a Host...</span></span></b></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#000080\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Deep One Sheet Creation</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>There is currently no Deep One sheet, and won't be until they're better fleshed out. They are simple creatures, though. For now, you only need to know a few things.</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Attributes</b> - Deep Ones do not have differentiated fields for Attributes, only Power, Finesse, and Resistance. Start with 0 points in each and spread 9 as desired. Remember that they have an effective Heartstring of 9, and thus, a stat maximum of 9.<br /> <b>Skills</b> - Deep Ones have 22 Skill Points to spend, but they do not differentiate between fields, so just spread them as needed. Once again, maximum is 9.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Merits</b> - Deep Ones do not have Merits, as these embody concepts which do not apply to them.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Ablutions</b> - Deep Ones always keep around 50 Dots of ablutions attached to their form, but can add and remove them at will. Once again, Maximum is 9.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Purviews</b> - The Deep Ones cannot harness the Will To Power, and thus, do not have Purviews.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Health</b> - 1 for every Point of Ablutions the Deep One has Manifested, meaning 50 is typical. Note that damaging a Deep One also damages the manifestation of targeted Ablution.<br /> <b>Willpower</b> - Deep Ones do not have Willpower, as they simply do not operate that way.<br /> <b>Breath</b> - The deep ones run on something equivilant to the Oroboroi's &quot;Breath&quot;, but can have up to 50 points at a time, and can get it from breaking down anything: they just use different stats, like size, structure, of health, to determine what's there.<br /> <b>Machination</b> - What this Deep One is currently attempting to accomplish, and how are they planning on going about it, similar to an Oroboros's Undertaking. Make a clear and actionable goal, and divide it into a 3 to 5 step checklist. When the Deep One has achieved all the steps, they have achieved their goal and can move onto the next.<br /> <b>Other Traits</b> - Deep Ones are immune to Heat, Toxins, and lack of Oxygen, and downgrade any damage that is not caused by one of their weaknesses. This applies to Fire, which they do not have special immunity to. They share the Oroboroi's weakness to Jade and Dark Magic. A creature of the Waking who actively tries to will against their actions rolls Resolve + Composure, and subtracts their successes from the Deep One's.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Note that Deep Ones do not have a Supernatural Power or Integrity stat, nor do they have Conditions or Experience.</b></span></span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#000080\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Common Deep One Ablutions</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>A Deep One might have anything as an Ablution. Remember that they are able to remove the forms of things they encounter and add them to themselves, giving the ability to manifest that and causing that object to crumble into raw matter, which can be consumed for Breath. A Deep One who consumes an object can gain breath equal to its size, and they have no concept or care for whether it is considered food. In fact, it is common for them to consume things which they want new Ablutions from. Lifting a concept from an object is a 10-die roll against that object's structure. In the case of a living thing, pick the highest resistance stat.<br /> <br /> Deep Ones do NOT have access to any sort of &quot;divinity levels&quot;, and are always considered to be in &quot;True Form&quot;. This means they don't get any other changes for manifesting or dispelling their Ablutions, but it also means that they never lose their elemental resistances.<br /> <br /> The following are common examples of Ablutions which the Deep Ones have easy access to.</b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Buff:Mastery</b> - When Manifesting this, the Deep One gains this number of dots in any Merit they want, chosen at the time of each Manifestation. If these dots represented resources, they disappear afterwards. This cannot be used to create new people, but CAN be used to temporarily alter existing ones.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Breath:Miasma</b> - The Deep One spends a point of breath to create a room-sized cloud of Miasma, which looks, tastes, and sounds like white noise, and induces extreme confusion in anything caught in it. All creatures nearby who are not resistant to the effects of Pandemonium are caught in a space of unmeaning which lasts a number of turns equal to the number of dots in this, meaning that the number of dots the Deep One has in this are subtracted directly from their <i>successes</i> on every roll they make.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Weaponry:Unmaking</b> - The Deep One has an attack in which they can simply focus on a single target and deal Lethal damage directly. This bypasses all defenses, both mundane and supernatural.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Tentacles</b> - Creates an tentacle-like appendage, which is usually long and blunted, but can have various traits. For every point in a single Tentacle ablution, the Deep One adds 2 Meters to its length. This appendage functions like an arm with a hand, but with a -3 penalty to anything more complicated than wrapping and slapping. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">This Ablution can be purchased an unlimited number of times for a virtually unlimited number of tentacles.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Extra Eyes</b> - For every point manifest, the Deep One gains another eye wherever they want it. Each eye adds 4 more dice to rolls to see things, and means they cannot be snuck up on from the angle it is pointing in.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Darklight</b> - The Deep One creates a cloud of immaterial, pitch black darkness around themselves, in a spherical area with a diameter of 5 Meters times the number of dots in the ablution. This costs 1 breath and lasts for a scene.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>[Creature] Carapace</b> - The Deep One takes the form of the specified creature, with the number of dots in this being the number of successes needed to perceive that there is something very very wrong, assuming the Deep One is hiding it and not simply using it as a cowl to wrap around their true form, which is effectively just a writhing, formless mass with eyes and small tentacles.</span></span></span></li> <li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Host / Human Guise</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"> - A Human who has been added as part of their form. (see &quot;Drowning Host&quot;)</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#000080\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Using the Deep One</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>I say &quot;Using&quot; because you're not giving this to a player. Deep Ones are Tier 3 reality warpers who defy human understanding: their thought process is totally relatable to humans, but their experiences, emotions, and desires are completely alien. Deep Ones come to the surface in the course of some sort of otherworldly machination, usually either looking for fresh concepts to add to themselves, or to alter the Waking to directly effect something in the Dreamtide.<br /> <br /> Deep Ones are not inherently hostile to anyone, but their machinations may require them to kill someone, possible an Oroboroi. Machinations typically involve some greater undertaking which is of use in Pandemonium, and the Deep Ones only venture far from there when they need to get or do something for that purpose. Deep Ones are completely immortal, and aren't susceptible to the curse of the Oroboroi, so they can be extremely patient with a machination, which may take decades, or centuries to come to fruition.<br /> <br /> Examples of Machinations include...</b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Removing a facet of Human Civilization which is negatively affecting the Dreamtide.</b></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Adding a facet to Human Culture which will make the Dreamtide more pleasant.</b></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Collecting useful Ablutions, knowledge which has not reached the Dreamtide, or new emotions to experience.</b></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Killing someone from the Waking who has been or may be a threat to another Machination.</b></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Killing a large number of humans to lessen their influence on the Dreamtide.</b></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Killing Dragons in revenge for Humanity's initial climb. Note that Deep Ones do not differentiate between Oroboroi and the Dragons whose Hearts they now have.</b></span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>The Deep Ones often act very sedate, but are absolutely resolute in whatever they do. They do not have remorse or conscience, and usually see most other creatures as tools at best and obstacles at worst. They may show some respect to an Oroboros, Beast, Leviathan, or another Deep One, as they see them as kindred, but this empathy does not translate into remorse. When they express emotions, they are not on a gradient: one who is angry will be furious, one who is pleased will be delighted, one who is sad may simply go dormant and float back down to Pandemonium.<br /> <br /> The Deep Ones were around when humans were still living in caves, and they can remember a large amount of history (both real and fictional) and science (mostly disproven theories), and are treasure-troves of Occult knowledge. After all, they've been watching our dreams for a very long time. Because of this, they have a strong enough understanding of the Ora to cross it at will: they must simply roll against the Ora's length at that time and place, and upon success, slip across.<br /> <br /> In short, they are resolute, calculative, extremely volatile, and extremely well learned.</b></span></span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#000080\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>The Drowning Host</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>A Deep One cannot travel for long in the Waking without a Host, as they need to spend a point of Breath every scene to prevent themselves from going Dormant, which dispels all Ablutions and leaves them unconscious in the form of a small, blue and gray colored, bulbous blob, though they will be sucked back into the Dreamtide when nighttime falls. Even without this, the Deep Ones do not have the ability to effectively imitate Humans, and therefore, need Humans to interact with human society for them. This leads to a very macabre deal...</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>The Deal</b> - In order to gain unhindered access to the Waking, the Deep Ones make deals with a Mortal Human: in exchange for her body and her life, the Human gains access to the powers of the Deep One to accomplish some goal. The Deep Ones may or may not care for what this goal is themselves, the important thing is that they have a body to take them around in the Waking. Examples of a goal a Deep One may assist with are...</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Revenge against an enemy who has taken everything, possibly an Oroboros</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Altering the Waking in some significant way</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Going on a journey to compete some sort of &quot;bucket-list&quot; before dying of a terminal illness.</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>The Union</b> - In order to complete the deal, the human must willingly allow the core of the Deep One to consume her. This is usually done through a process where one of the two envelops the other, the human lets go of all will to remain a physical entity, and the Deep One concentrates upon breaking her down into every concept which makes up her form. The Deep One consumes the Human and when she wakes up, she has become its Host.<br /> <br /> <b>The Symbiosis</b> - The Human retains everything from her sheet in this new state, with the added bonus of gaining everything the Deep One's True Form has at all times. This includes resistances, the ability to manifest and dispel the Deep One's ablutions, and the power to use Breath to heal and power ablutions. The Deep One must share direct control of the body for as long as the union is going, but only needs to spend a point of Breath every day to prevent dormancy, now that it has a Host from the Waking.<br /> <br /> Note that the Deep One treats the host as a 9-dot Ablution, and that less than 9 dots would mean an incomplete form. The Deep Ones don't always <i>need</i> the form to be &quot;complete&quot;, however...<br /> <br /> <b>Length of Tenure</b> - Depending on the goal of both the Deep One and the Host, and how well the union fits into the Deep One's machinations, the union may last for a very short or very long time. Deep Ones have been known to keep a host for mere days, while others have kept a host for Centuries, taking them back to Pandemonium when not engaged in a Machination. No matter how long the symbiosis lasts, however, the end is always the same: once the Deep One no longer has reason to keep the Host, they will discard them.<br /> <br /> <b>The Drowning</b> - Once a human has become a Host there is no turning back: they are no longer able to maintain their material being in the waking world without the Deep One, which now has control of their very form. If the Deep One doesn't like something about their form, they have the power to change it. Deep Ones which find the usefulness of their Host waning will begin to alter their form to make it more useful, remove parts to make it easier to maintain, or remove it all together. The Host can resist this, but cannot fight back, so eventually, the Deep One will get its way.<br /> <br /> A Host without a Deep One loses any Ablutions and Breath they didn't manage to hold onto, and loses a box of health for every scene in which they are without the Deep One,</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"> as their conceptual function begins to melt away, leaving only a husk of non-descript matter</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">. The only way for them to survive without such an entity sustaining them is to cross the Ora into the Dreamtide, where they can replenish their Health and Breath, but this is extremely perilous. A Savvy host might look for another Deep One, but this is temporary. There is only one permanent solution to being an entity without a stable Waking form, and that is to obtain an item which can sustain the forms of the Dreamtide in the Waking...</span></span></span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Like the Heart of a Dragon.</span></span></span></span></b></span></div> <hr /><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">m\u035c\u0354\u0330\u0356\u0348\u032aY\u0334\u0316\u0348\u031d\u0323 \u035f\u0348\u032b\u033c\u031e\u0326\u0323\u0323k\u0361\u0315\u0321\u0319\u0345\u0347\u00a1\u0341\u0336\u0330\u0331\u033an\u031d\u0325\u0333\u0345\u0331\u0353\u032c\u0329D\u0327\u031b\u0356\u031c\u0320\u0345\u0317 \u0321\u035f\u0329\u032dh\u0345\u0353\u032e\u0317\u0348@\u035f\u0356\u0339\u0319\u033c\u0318\u032a\u0356\u0324t\u0337\u0345\u0316\u034d\u0348\u0319\u0324H\u0337\u0359\u0359\u0353 \u0327\u0340\u0334\u031c\u0320\u031cl\u0358\u0337\u0348\u034ea\u0328\u035f\u0326\u0345\u032d\u031f\u035a\u0317$\u031b\u032e\u0359\u0317\u0326\u031c\u031f\u0318t\u0360\u0358\u035c\u031f\u0332\u032fe\u0326\u0324\u032c\u033b\u031f\u0319D\u0334\u0339 \u035c\u033b\u0330\u034d\u031c\u0330\u032cm\u0321\u032c\u032e\u032a\u035a\u031f\u031c\u0319A\u031cn\u035e\u0318\u0347\u0331\u031f\u0349\u031c\u034dy\u0335\u0315\u0338\u0355\u0349\u0332\u0318\u0347\u0359\u031c \u032fa\u0335\u0336\u0325n\u035d\u0333\u032f\u031f \u0489\u033b\u031fE\u0327\u0320\u0349\u0348\u0318\u0339\u033c\u03490\u0360\u0322\u0489\u031fn\u0340\u0345\u0348\u0353\u0326\u0353,\u0327\u032c\u0339 \u0338\u0319\u0355\u0316\u0323\u033a</span></span></b></span> <div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">a\u0337\u032c\u032cn\u0338\u0358\u035a\u033b\u031f\u032f\u0326d\u031b\u0359\u033c\u034e\u0318\u035a\u0359\u0331\u0345 \u0335\u035f\u032c\u0332\u0330\u034e\u033c\u032d\u0353w\u0328\u035f\u034d\u0345\u034d\u031d\u0319\u0332\u0320E\u0324\u033b\u0355\u031e\u031c \u0328\u0355\u031e\u033a\u0347\u031c\u0359s\u031b\u0345\u0317h\u0327\u0315\u0334\u0323\u0316a\u0362\u0335\u0324\u0329\u0355\u0320\u0339\u0316\u0320\u033bL\u035e\u0333\u032b\u031e\u0339\u0354\u031c\u0332\u0353L\u035d\u035c\u0321\u0359\u0331\u0323\u0355\u031e\u0318\u0324\u0333 \u032e \u0358\u035c\u0348\u0345\u0349\u032c\u031d\u0324\u0355\u032d\u03230\u0489\u034f\u0341\u032e\u0347\u0355\u032b\u0359u\u0360\u035c\u0348\u032a\u0349\u0333\u032fT\u035d\u0489\u032e\u0354\u0320\u032f\u0348\u0331\u032cl\u0322\u0361\u0335\u0353\u033a\u032fa\u0315\u035d\u0336\u032b \u0325\u0331s\u035e\u0328\u033a\u033aT\u0358\u0347\u035a\u032c\u0331\u0318\u033a\u033a\u0329 \u0358\u0327\u0338\u0325\u032b\u0331\u0324\u0355\u0316e\u0335\u0335\u0331\u0356\u0319\u031c\u032b\u0319v\u0326\u0318\u0329\u031d\u0325\u0331e\u0347\u033a\u034e\u034d\u0353N\u0361\u0316\u032f\u032c\u0317\u0330\u0318\u032d\u0323 \u0319\u033c\u032e\u0323\u0325\u032by\u035f\u033c\u0332\u031dO\u0361\u031f\u0330\u033a\u0354\u031c\u0320u\u0341\u033b\u031c\u031f,\u0362\u0340\u032c\u0353\u0319\u0316 \u034f\u0358\u0330\u0333\u032dd\u031b\u0327\u033a\u0318\u0325\u033c\u031fR\u0340\u0358\u0355a\u0362\u0316\u0317G\u034f\u0355\u0348o\u031f\u034d\u0323\u033c\u0325\u0348\u0359\u032an\u0338\u0322\u0361\u033c\u0347\u032a\u0325.\u0362\u0324\u033b\u0319\u0356\u032d\u035a \u033a \u0327\u031b\u0356\u033a</span></span></b></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><span style=\"color:#000080\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">w\u0336\u0337\u0331\u0349\u031c\u0319\u0332\u032f\u0320H\u0340\u0329\u033a\u031e\u0316\u033ca\u0335\u0361\u0355\u0356\u0356\u0331\u033c\u0349\u031fT\u0315\u0356\u0359 \u035d\u0327\u0324\u033b\u0354\u0324\u0330\u032d\u0355\u0316y\u0338\u0489\u0316\u0359\u032bO\u0361\u0340\u0328\u032a\u0316\u0355\u0324u\u031b\u035c\u032f\u033a\u0329\u031cR\u0341\u0337\u0316\u032f\u033c\u0319\u032d \u0340\u0354\u032f\u034d\u031d\u0356\u0355\u0318i\u0358\u0336\u0317\u0323\u0319n\u0334\u035c\u0356\u0316\u032c\u033a\u035a\u0353T\u0322\u0339\u032d\u0325e\u0338\u0329\u032cn\u0360\u031b\u0336\u033a\u0326T\u035e\u031c\u0317i\u0330\u034d\u0325\u0317\u0347o\u0334 \u0328\u034d\u034en\u0360\u0349s\u0321\u032a\u031e\u0319\u031d\u0359\u034d\u0332\u0347 \u035d\u0325\u031d\u034e\u0329\u0339M\u0328\u035f\u033a\u0323\u032e\u0354a\u035f\u031d\u0319\u031c\u033a\u0318\u0355\u032cy\u032c\u0339\u032d\u032c\u033c\u032b \u0358\u0321\u0