ng To the Strongest, etc. I can see Dragon or Orobori lurking in the Time where the gauntlet has not fallen and the border marches still allow God spirits of all kinds to cross. I can see them having a active presence in the East.<br /> <br /> I still ponder the interaction of Orobori vs. The rest of the world of darkness entities both Canon and fanon. Leviathan being God beast as well could be a interesting conflict. Which God monster came first and are they willing to work together against Humanities New Gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T11:44:48-07:00","id":906596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Freederp92</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=906582#post906582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting I must say, Deep Ones interactions with Mastigos mages sound like a hell of a time!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a different &quot;Pandemonium&quot;. World of Darkness has similar names for different places like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can they only host out of mortals and how do other super naturals see them? </div> </div> </div>Only some who could become an Oroboros. Other Supernaturals probably don't know about them unless they encounter them, as they are rarer in the Waking and the Dream than the Oroboroi. When they do encounter them, they'll try to make deals to replace some of the supernatural creature's innate supernatural powers with Ablutions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah I was referring to Dark Eras, the supplement describing different Eras of play including To the Strongest, etc. I can see Dragon or Orobori lurking in the Time where the gauntlet has not fallen and the border marches still allow God spirits of all kinds to cross. I can see them having a active presence in the East. </div> </div> </div>Oh, back then? Well, first you have Dominion, then you have Collapse, then the Oroboroi try to become the new gods and get slain, then they go into hiding. It's not clear when the Gauntlet / Ora / Void was imposed to separate this world from the others in this timeline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I still ponder the interaction of Orobori vs. The rest of the world of darkness entities both Canon and fanon. </div> </div> </div>Go look at the Antagonists section of Second and Third edition of Embers, and the Appendix at the end of the Transitional book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Leviathan being God beast as well could be a interesting conflict. Which God monster came first and are they willing to work together against Humanities New Gods? </div> </div> </div>We've talked about this. The Leviathans (stop me if I'm wrong) are children of the Old Gods, who came before the Dragons, and the Orobroi who know enough about them know to be terrified of. The Beasts look like Nightmares in Human form, and are rare enough that an Oroboros won't meet too many: what the Oroboros thinks of a Beast is going to depend on how they act. The Oroboroi aren't the First Gods, they don't have a feud with the New Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T12:48:45-07:00","id":906646,"title":"","content":"I figured they would be different realms but still a Mastigos mage could be addicted to the mystery it represented and since they can often deal with goetics it might interest them.<br /> <br /> Also that explanation makes sense. <br /> <br /> Also yeah Leviathans are primordial things whose Wake can be scary spawning cults and ahabs. Beast kinda fill the role of teaching through fear. Their Heroes are Slayer's of Horrors and can't handle sharing the kill with others.<br /> <br /> This project is interesting and I hope to see more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11808-freederp92","name":"Freederp92","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T01:48:18-07:00","id":907529,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">- NEWS UPDATE -</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Current inner workings</span></span></b></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Reviewing Reference Material</b> - </span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">So that everyone can better unders<span style=\"font-family:georgia\">tand the concepts at play, we're having readings and discussions related to real-world material which makes a good reference</span>.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Working on Writing Skills</b> - </span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In order to work on the editing of the Transitional Edition we put out, and to bu<span style=\"font-family:georgia\">ild quality for the final release, we're going over concepts and strategies to better write new things</span>.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>New Ablution List</b> - <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">We're working</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> on a list of ablutions which will <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">fit the new edition, complete with updated versions of the old ones and more fleshed out versions of the new ones</span>. <span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Expect to see something on this in the next couple weeks.</span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Chapter 2</b> - As this seems to be the easiest and most fleshed-out chapter to write, we're working on putting it out as a better example of what the final book will look like</span></span><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">.</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Current Issues</span></span></span></b></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>WE NEED PEOPLE!</b> - So far, 2 of the 6 members have left due to not having enough time, mainly because of school-related workloads. Anyone who's interested in writing, drawing, playtesting, or just helping to brainstorm should apply to join!</span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Other than that, things feel like they're going well on this end...</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Final Notes</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If anyone wants to know about the current status of any mechanic, please ask.<br /> If anyone wants to give feedback about something already released, fire away.<br /> Other than that, we hope you all stay excited, and we'll show you more completed work soon enough.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T15:07:37-07:00","id":912467,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sitting in the weekly meeting here, and just wanted to tell everyone what we're talking about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> <b>In Dragon Rekindled, the Oroboroi face</b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">FULL LIFE CONSEQUENCES!</span></span></b></span><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">STAY TUNED FOR MORE!</span></span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T08:15:10-07:00","id":914837,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I got work related work loads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T13:34:46-07:00","id":915040,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#696969\"><b>Coming next week...</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#cc0066\"><b>The Knights of the Bloody Chalice</b></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">They are few in number, and their members are quite secretive, but to those who know of this ancient cabal of Blood Bathing Occultists, they are a menace which must be stamped out...</span></b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">How did this secretive and dangerous group form in the time before written history?</span></b></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">What sort of dark rituals do they use to drain the blood of others and keep themselves in their prime?</span></b></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">What sort of powers and tactics do they employ to lead others into the charge against the Oroboroi?</span></b></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Why would they resort to these barbaric means, especially when immortality is only a Heart away?</span></b></span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Keep watching to find out...</b></span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T16:42:03-07:00","id":917622,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I want to clarify something, because people have asked:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Just because something hasn't been touched on yet, doesn't mean it's been removed.</b></span></span><br /> Like the <i><b>Knights of the Bloody Chalice</b></i>, there are alot of things we haven't had time to go through yet. We want to keep everything that made the 2nd and 3rd editions of Embers what they were, but we want to add more flavor, structure, and darker elements to them, while expanding the possibilities of what Dragon can be.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Transitional Rulebook&quot; was just that: a set of new ideas and mechanics which would carry over Dragon into 2nd Edition. It's neither the full book, nor really a finalized game. It's more like the GMC Rules Update which White Wolf released a few years ago: it's there so you can adapt old material for new games. It doesn't have all the content because that sort of thing is an entirely different Dragon. The version of the book we are working on <i>right now</i>, <b><i>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles</i></b> is the one which will have all the content.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Examples of things which we are NOT taking out, but haven't gotten around to yet</span></b></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>The Treasury</b>, which is being placed on the Far Shore of the Dreamtide</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>More Antecedents for more Heartstring</b>, going back to the original Dragon at Heartstring 10</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dynasties</b>, which are being written as conspiracies / occult-groups</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Provinces, Maidens, and Hoards</b>, which are in there now, but will see more refinement.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Dreams, Nightmares, Dream Worlds</b>, and all the other Dreamtide stuff, because the Appendix only touched on them briefly (Nightmares are actually our next planned &quot;glimpse&quot;, after the Knights)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Heart Removal</b> and all the things that come with it, including methods of keeping the Heart and how far you can go from it.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Pilot Lights and Brood Bonded</b>. To those out there who have lamented their removal, you have <i>no idea</i> how much work is going into the <i>entire chapter on them</i>. We want them to have their own Character Sheets and everything, just like the &quot;Wolf Blooded&quot; in <i>Werewolf 2nd Edition</i>.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Unlisted Edicts</b>, which we're going to rebuild into it.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Examples of the very few things which ARE being removed</span></span></b></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Einherjar</b>: they're interesting, but they didn't really relate to anything else in the book.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Grafts</b>: once again, they're cool, and we like them, but they just don't fit in with anything else.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ominous Drums</b>: we like it, but it needs to be rewritten, and I've got a different idea for what the story should look like...</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Note also that just because we're removing something now, doesn't mean you can't use it, nor does it mean we won't change our minds.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">A(nother) Plea for People</span></span></b><br /> If you want to give input on something, <b>join the project</b>: we're really not being picky about anyone who wants to brainstorm and develop ideas with us, just with people who want to directly add the final content. Darinas, for example, is playing a huge part in fleshing out the <i>Knights of the Bloody Chalice</i> (expect the release on that by Thursday night: we're excited!), because it was one of his favorite things in the Embers books.<br /> <br /> Once again, joining is as simple as applying, so if anyone's interested, apply ASAP!</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 06-25-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T00:31:34-07:00","id":917851,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Fun stuff out of the Bloody Chalice discussions...</span></span></b><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">One of the disadvantages of being one is listed as &quot;The ritual is damn crazy&quot;</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">From the viewpoint of Nietsche (&quot;Raccoon is obsessed with Nietsche&quot;), these guys are written as the <i>Will to Live</i> overtaking the <i>Will To Power</i>.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Ironically, they lose parts of their humanity simply by <i><b>murdering</b> innocent people to <b>bathe</b> in their goddamn <b>blood</b></i>.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Their leader is supposedly a noble of some sort from around the time of the collapse, who has balls-out magic powers.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;The reason why they don't just eat the hearts is they are crazy and stupid.&quot; &quot;No, that's dumb.&quot; &quot;Let's make them Dream Sorcerers!&quot;</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Yeah, they can go to the Dreamtide, work Dark Magic, carry plenty of Jade.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Also, they have Breath</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">They have 5 ranks, with Prospects, who want to become Squires, who want to be knights, who rise to become lords, who are in awe of their supposedly 10,000+ year old King.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">There's an example in there of one of them faking a group of The Long Night into thinking they're a priest, then convincing them to kill a den of Oroboroi with the &quot;blessings&quot; (Breath imbument) and &quot;holy implements&quot; (jade) they've provided as the group's &quot;old and frail mentor&quot;.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">&quot;There are always two Sith, the Master and the Apprentice... So which one was that, and where's the other one?&quot; &quot;Sith?&quot; &quot;Knights. I mean Knights.&quot;</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">They don't fuck with Deep Ones. They want to live forever, and dying would defeat the purpose.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I_izvAbhExY\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is their theme song</span></a></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Anyway, it's pretty well fleshed out, and we're increasingly proud of our newest 3-page antagonist, so I've decided to give us that Thursday night deadline, assuming we don't complete it by or right after Wednesday's meeting. Next two releases planned are Nightmares and Pilot Lights, then probably Chapter 2: Methods and Philosophies (and Dynasties).<br /> <br /> Who else is excited? (And who wants to join?)</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 06-20-2016, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T16:35:03-07:00","id":921219,"title":"","content":"Man, I feel dumb, I self-imposed that Thursday deadline, then a bunch of stuff happened...<br /> <br /> Anyway, expect the Knights soon. Also going to release a new list of Purviews soon (we're digging into that right now), so watch for that...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T21:10:36-07:00","id":922438,"title":"","content":"...You know what?<br /> The sudden lack of response from the community is making me feel like there's something I don't know about or that the interest comes in waves and I need to wait for the next one. I'm not gonna worry about releasing anything else until someone else comments on this thread.<br /> <br /> We're working on the Purviews and Ablutions, and the Knights stuff is pretty much ready for the first draft of the full book...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T12:07:06-07:00","id":922768,"title":"","content":"Let's see if I can help you.<br /> <br /> With no particular order:<br /> <br /> 1- Rules.<br /> The first edition rules were overly complicated, subsystems stacked over other subsystems.<br /> This edition simplify some, it's need to simplify all of it.<br /> <br /> 2 - Inflated<br /> This is the sins of all the books of CroD, is you write something with a paragraph that can be written with one phrase, do it in one phrase, this help alot with the above one.<br /> Also if the rule set it's not written in character, don't mix crunch and fluff.<br /> <br /> 3 - reimagining<br /> <br /> It's a good concept, but it's not for everyone; Made it so or made it an optional rule.<br /> I say it because there's a lot of people that feel very violent if someone touch their character sheet, also backstabbing between the players and the gamemaster, a tabletop rpg isn't a competition!<br /> <br /> 4 - make true form important, also, make the game about dragons.<br /> <br /> True form looks like very anecdotic, it's so anecdotic that's very infuriating. <br /> I mean, is this a game about dragons or about conspiracy lovers politicians? or backstabbing vampires? or empresarial espionage?<br /> that's was the reason Dragon the Inheritance born in the beginning, hell! I'm even write my own. <br /> Also, even this fangame was before, now there's Beast the Primordial and Demon the Descent, and that's a problem.<br /> Leviathan can coexist with Beast because the theme and mood are very different, but Ember and Beast looks and feel very similar and overlaps in one another in certain places, the same with Demon but in a lesser extent.<br /> Make it different, make it it's own game, and above all, make it a game about dragons, which now it isn't.<br /> <br /> I hope that list can help you with something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nosolorol.com/nuevo/images/Fostern.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1192-aura","name":"Aura","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T17:22:48-07:00","id":922935,"title":"","content":".... I personally don't really understand how the current version we did isn't about Dragons, or even how it's similar to either Beast or Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T18:22:30-07:00","id":924208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=922768#post922768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1- Rules.<br /> The first edition rules were overly complicated, subsystems stacked over other subsystems.<br /> This edition simplify some, it's need to simplify all of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been a focus on some level, but keep in mind that it's hard to write good mechanics, especially for a highly supernatural character design which is supposed to be as customizable as Dragon, without having some complicated rules come up. Moreover, the subsystems you're mentioning actually <i>simplify</i> what the other books would just leave as vague rules reused by 3 or 4 abilities. A large chunk of Embers' appeal was the wide variety of hacks and mechanics it presented, which gave Storytellers and other Fan Projects a huge amount of fodder.<br /> <br /> That said, taking old mechanics and rewriting them is a major part of what we're doing, and using variations on the ones added in GMC is going to be a HUGE help: the Tilts are <i>great</i> for replacing alot of the old rules, the Clue and Doors systems will <i>really</i> help with the Purviews which deal with investigation and persuasion, respectively, (actually, one of the Knowledge Impositions is specifically geared towards slipping behind the doors and changing a belief while leaving them still shut tight for the next guy, and the new mechanic is making that alot easier to write.) and the Item Concealment rules which were clarified recently have outright REPLACED what used to be a relatively complex system for Ablution Tells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2 - Inflated<br /> This is the sins of all the books of CroD, is you write something with a paragraph that can be written with one phrase, do it in one phrase, this help alot with the above one.<br /> Also if the rule set it's not written in character, don't mix crunch and fluff. </div> </div> </div>This is a problem with the writing staff that I'm currently trying to reign in: fantasy writers, especially ones with lots of passion but little experience with technical writing, tend to embellish WAY too much. That's why I didn't start by trying to release the full book right away: I needed to see them write a book that, while I think it's good enough to use (discounting the things that we're still editing in), has some very serious problems. Those problems are now being addressed. The first draft is never the best, and a large chunk of the focus right now is on making the next one better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3 - reimagining<br /> It's a good concept, but it's not for everyone; Made it so or made it an optional rule.<br /> I say it because there's a lot of people that feel very violent if someone touch their character sheet, also backstabbing between the players and the gamemaster, a tabletop rpg isn't a competition! </div> </div> </div>Well, <b>we <i>are</i> trying to reign in how much it actually does</b>: we don't intend it to actually come up with characters who haven't gotten sloppy with power, nor do we intend for it to be rolled more than once every few sessions, if at all. There are also late game mechanics which outright negate it that we haven't finished and released yet. For example, Dynasties, where the Dragons of St George are made to pretty much WALLOW in Guilt without consequence, while the Delvers simply know what the Reimagining is on a deeper level than the others do, so they just will it not to happen. It only really comes up if you rise in power way too quickly, which is part of the point of the mechanic, thematically, or if you have characters who are really old.<br /> <br /> On the other claw though, if you have such a bad group that you see a mechanic with potential as potential for infighting, then that's not really our problem: we're going to have advice on running a group in the book, but if your group just infights then you can't expect us to hold back mechanics intended for groups who don't to save your group for another session or two. You don't HAVE to use it if you REALLY don't like it, but we're writing a small chunk of the book's concept around it, and it's fitting nicely so far, so we haven't seen a need to write it out.<br /> <br /> Then again, we might write it out in the next month. We don't know. Once again, it's not a well-fleshed-out concept yet, and we haven't gotten around to releasing much on it: it's not an important mechanic to us right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4 - make true form important, also, make the game about dragons.<br /> True form looks like very anecdotic, it's so anecdotic that's very infuriating.<br /> I mean, is this a game about dragons or about conspiracy lovers politicians? or backstabbing vampires? or empresarial espionage? </div> </div> </div>...Have you read any of the notes I've made about this? Because while, no, the game isn't <i>entirely</i> focused on Dragons. The dragon powers are Metaphor for Power in general here, the Dragons themselves are an ancient horror, and the Oroboroi have powers and weaknesses based on their origin as a fantasy. To make the idea more broad and dragonny, the political stuff has been minimized for other elements. Meanwhile, we've been writing the Dragon form as a default at this point, because we do intend for them to be in it whenever they don't need to keep up that masquerade.<br /> <br /> There is a chunk of this that can't be helped though. This is not Harry Potter, where someone bursting into Dragon Form in the middle of Diagon Alley is going to get disapproving looks from all the other wizards, this is World of Darkness, where supernatural creatures are <i>terrified</i> of what might happen if they're found out. Yeah, we want them in Dragon Form more often than Uratha stay in Garou, but it's impossible to write a creature which can interact with humanity while in the form of a mythological creature.<br /> <br /> Also, it really doesn't do well to make it up as you go. Reality, even through the lens of the World of Darkness, has established rules and considerations. These books take research and thought: we're pulling from Plato, Decarte, Nietzsche, Rand, LaVey, and Dawkins here, as well as more Dragon mythology than I can begin to name here. Also the 3 Embers books. We can't just write things in because they sound cool, we have to think carefully about them. If you're looking at this and saying &quot;they didn't make this a game about being a rampaging dragon like you can play in D&amp;D&quot;, then that's our job done right: we want it to feel like it fits into a Chronicle of Darkness as well as Vampire or Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> that's was the reason Dragon the Inheritance born in the beginning, hell! I'm even write my own. </div> </div> </div>If you have a problem with Dragon, which is a pretty well established book that's been in development for almost 10 years, why not talk about it before running off to make your own? Maybe there's something you're missing, or something we actually want to change? There are alot of fan projects out there, and we're splitting limited resources by resorting to infighting. We actually have a set of notes on how we might reconcile Inheritance and Rekindled in the same universe if that project ever sees prominence again, and I've tried to reach out to the heads of several other projects, but realize that there are already multiple projects based on this concept, all of them taking it in different directions, and all of them are spread thin. If you have a problem with something we're doing, we'd prefer you talk it out with us, or at least one of the other Dragon projects, not split resources even more by starting another 10-chapter book...<br /> <br /> Granted, as project head, I have to juggle the demands of several large groups, and despite appearances, I don't have the power to make broad-sweeping decisions on a whim. I keep Shock around to make sure we don't miss anything important about the old material, because there's only so much I'm willing to change, and there are some things which just won't work as well as others. (Shock was happy that we removed the 5 Evils, because that gave us more room to write the Purviews) We're not going to be able to write a game to make everyone happy, so we're writing the game that will make Embers fans happy, and the big changes are meant to be refinements and expansions on the capabilities of the old material. With a philosophy like that, I dunno how much we can give you, but there's a real lack of dialogue here when you decide walking in that you're going to go make your own when this project is actively seeking involvement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, even this fangame was before, now there's Beast the Primordial and Demon the Descent, and that's a problem. </div> </div> </div>I don't see how that's a problem. Yeah, Beast <i>coincidentally</i> has a large amount of material which, on the surface, looks similar to things discussed in Embers, Inheritance, Leviathan, and Princess, but most of that is actually based in existing mythos and mechanics: the four games are functionally and thematically <i>very</i> different. Beast is about spreading wisdom through fear, embracing your own monstrosity, and generally being emo. (the Emo thing is leading to a lack of popularity with some crowds, but it's actually a very nice book from what I've been shown: no book can please everyone, that doesn't make it bad) Dragon is about the drive, struggle, usage, and inevitable fall from Power. Also you can turn into a Dragon, so there's that. There isn't as much overlap when you get past the surface issues, because while they're both World of Darkness books about monsters of Dreamtide origin, they're completely different takes. Even still, there's a huge amount of overlap with EVERY book, because that's just what happens when you have multiple things written from the same basic rules in the same setting. I'm going to note that Purviews are effectively Mini-Arcana, that True Form is a different shade of Garou, The Knights of the Bloody Chalice were probably written by someone who read Chapter 1 of Immortals, Vampires already used the idea of &quot;immortality at a price&quot; with 25 years of time to flesh it out, Changeling (I'm told) has some sort of Dream Magic, Princesses use Jade to fight Dreamtide monsters, and, going back to mages, there is a whole set of books dedicated to the Astral Plane. Nobody brings <i>that</i> overlap up when talking about Fan-Projects, but our meetings are <i>filled</i> with references to existing books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Leviathan can coexist with Beast because the theme and mood are very different </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like how Dragon copied some of the same existing mythology / occult stuff in a vaguely similar way, but had a completely different outcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Make it different </div> </div> </div>It is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> make it it's own game </div> </div> </div>It is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> make it a game about dragons </div> </div> </div>It is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> which now it isn't. </div> </div> </div>As has been explained, the argument doesn't hold up. If you don't agree with that, then please elaborate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hope that list can help you with something. </div> </div> </div>It helps to get some level of feedback, even if we just end up disagreeing with it, because this does tell me that mechanics and releases might need to be clarified. It at least gave a reason to clarify and organize thoughts here. If you want to stick around and talk, I'd be happy to, but I dunno if I can make another long-form response: this is a 10 chapter book, and it all needs to be carefully crafted..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T19:00:24-07:00","id":925164,"title":"","content":"I drew a new skull. <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://s6.postimg.org/i90uckr5t/Skull.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-02-2016, 10:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T10:56:47-07:00","id":925409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=924208#post924208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how that's a problem. Yeah, Beast <i>coincidentally</i> has a large amount of material which, on the surface, looks similar to things discussed in Embers, Inheritance, Leviathan, and Princess, but most of that is actually based in existing mythos and mechanics: the four games are functionally and thematically <i>very</i> different. Beast is about spreading wisdom through fear, embracing your own monstrosity, and generally being emo. (the Emo thing is leading to a lack of popularity with some crowds, but it's actually a very nice book from what I've been shown: no book can please everyone, that doesn't make it bad) Dragon is about the drive, struggle, usage, and inevitable fall from Power. Also you can turn into a Dragon, so there's that. There isn't as much overlap when you get past the surface issues, because while they're both World of Darkness books about monsters of Dreamtide origin, they're completely different takes. Even still, there's a huge amount of overlap with EVERY book, because that's just what happens when you have multiple things written from the same basic rules in the same setting. I'm going to note that Purviews are effectively Mini-Arcana, that True Form is a different shade of Garou, The Knights of the Bloody Chalice were probably written by someone who read Chapter 1 of Immortals, Vampires already used the idea of &quot;immortality at a price&quot; with 25 years of time to flesh it out, Changeling (I'm told) has some sort of Dream Magic, Princesses use Jade to fight Dreamtide monsters, and, going back to mages, there is a whole set of books dedicated to the Astral Plane. Nobody brings <i>that</i> overlap up when talking about Fan-Projects, but our meetings are <i>filled</i> with references to existing books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, Beast: the Primordial basically <i>is</i> a take on dragons as PCs. The Horrors aren't necessarily reptilian monsters, but the whole game is built around the scene in fantasy stories where the hero descends into a great monster's lair to kill it, told from the monster's viewpoint; and dragons are probably the most common kind of monster in that scene. It isn't just the Lair trait and system - lots of the Atavisms are based on classic draconic powers.<br /> <br /> If I'm reading it correctly, the biggest difference between Beast and Oroboroi is that the latter get to play <i>both</i> roles in the iconic scene, at different times in their lives: an Oroboros begins as the dragon slayer, claims its power by eating its heart, then returns home to rule, becoming dragon-like; eventually he grows so monstrous that he has to be slain, becoming the dragon whose power will be claimed by his murderers.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, why isn't it possible for his Heart to be divided among several people when an Oroboros is killed? Does the game really need the number of dragons to be slowly dwindling with no possibility of recovering? In Mummy the decay of the Arisen from an original state of glory is part of the theme - but do dragons need the theme of a lost paradise? I suspect the PC origin (you ate a monster's heart to steal its power!) already does enough along those lines - Oroboroi chose to exile themselves from humanity, their lives before eating the Heart are an age of innocence that they deliberately abandoned and can never return to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T16:07:16-07:00","id":925544,"title":"","content":"Ok, so, last night I got a chance to read through someone's copy of Beast... And the more I read the more it seems like a completely different game. Like, yeah, there's nightmares and monsters and the Dream stuff, but it's just not the same book at all.<br /> <br /> I'm also starting to feel a bit disheartened by the fact that we're taking all this time to rewrite a good fan book and make it even better, and everyone keeps focusing on these minor similarities to a book which came out long after this project began. We could be here all month trying to argue over it, but it's not productive, and there really isn't as strong of an argument as you people think. :/<br /> <br /> After this, I don't think I'm going to bother talking too much about Beast, because I really just don't see the argument that it's the same book and I'm not even sure it's relevant here. If a vague similarity to Beast is the biggest problem you have with Dragon, then Dragon must be an excellent book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=925409#post925409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, Beast: the Primordial basically <i>is</i> a take on dragons as PCs. The Horrors aren't necessarily reptilian monsters, but the whole game is built around the scene in fantasy stories where the hero descends into a great monster's lair to kill it, told from the monster's viewpoint; and dragons are probably the most common kind of monster in that scene. It isn't just the Lair trait and system - lots of the Atavisms are based on classic draconic powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's such a different take on it. Beasts aren't supposed to be &quot;real dragons&quot;, they're supposed to be avatars of Humanity's fear, and the Dragon thing is incidental / metaphorical. The Orobroroi are real Dragons, period, even if they're different from the initial thought, and when they're not Dragons, they're Ubermencsch / Gods. Go try and make that criticism of the similarities between Beast and Werewolf or Vampire: they're all scary, and Beasts can be made like Werewolves or Vampires, because Beast is supposed to be a versatile book like that. That doesn't make the one book eliminate the merit of the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I'm reading it correctly, the biggest difference between Beast and Oroboroi is that the latter get to play <i>both</i> roles in the iconic scene, at different times in their lives: an Oroboros begins as the dragon slayer, claims its power by eating its heart, then returns home to rule, becoming dragon-like; eventually he grows so monstrous that he has to be slain, becoming the dragon whose power will be claimed by his murderers. </div> </div> </div>There are several other major differences though.<br /> <br /> The Oroboroi have transformation powers, which Beast has nothing like, that mean that they end up with this really powerful Dragon Form to use in this very hands-on visceral manner. Beasts don't have anything like that, instead they have their Lair and their Atavisms, which aren't as immediately powerful or visceral as the Oroboroi.<br /> <br /> The tone is entirely different: whereas Dragon takes this very power-centric theme and uses alot of dark-fantasy elements, Beast takes on this very dark/goth theme that uses elements of traditionalism. Beast takes all this time to bemoan the lack of fear in our civilization, that we believe we've risen above the harsh realities, and need a horror to teach us an important lesson about what we SHOULD fear. Dragon is about punching the Beast's viewpoint in the face, grabbing a shitload of power, and carrying out some sort of godlike undertaking.<br /> <br /> They are literally night and day as both good guys and bad guys: Beasts are like Batman, Dragons are like Superman. I can see a Dragon punching meteors in the face, or fighting interplanetary horrors, or attempting to solve some global political crisis, but I don't see the reclusive Beast doing that. Meanwhile, I can much more easily see a Beast lurking in the shadows, waiting for criminals to strike, then dealing out some good old fashioned justice, either by terrifying them, or by just beating them senseless. On the flipside, a Dragon gone bad hoards power and resources to dominates humanity as a whole. A Beast gone bad becomes an obligate sadist, preying on people at random on an individual level. Their scope, power type, and interest are completely different.<br /> <br /> As a book, Beast doesn't have the same volume of potential as Dragon. Don't get me wrong, it's a good book, but there's only one character I can see myself interested in, there's only one plot I can think of running, and there's only one real undertaking presented. Hell, the only major antagonist I see in Beast is the Hero, where as we're making up random things to throw into any campaign. Don't get me wrong, I think that the idea of Beast is great and I can totally see myself playing it... But only once. Like Promethian, it's creating this very well crafted and detailed view on what is essentially a single kind of story, and it's great at what it does, but it's not what Dragon is. Dragon has a much broader scope and usage, with material that can bleed over into any other setting, and that's one of the things that's so great about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, why isn't it possible for his Heart to be divided among several people when an Oroboros is killed? </div> </div> </div>The Heart is a single entity: all parts have to be there to function. Think about it this way, if I were to give you a new component for your computer, like a new motherboard, would you be able to run the computer without a complete motherboard? When doctors do Heart Transplants, they can't just divide a single Heart up between multiple patients, because each chamber has a function. In this case, you need the power of a full Heart to become an Oroboroi. We've been getting into this with our discussions of Pilot Lights, who are going to grow Hearts one chamber at a time, but like I said, we haven't gotten to the point of writing a release on stuff like that yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the game really need the number of dragons to be slowly dwindling with no possibility of recovering? </div> </div> </div>Well, that was a theme that was played up in the original, with the idea that there may be a way out. We're not seeing a need right now to play it up. I will say though, there aren't any other books with that theme as far as I know, and it does add a bit of melancholy and tension to it all...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> do dragons need the theme of a lost paradise? </div> </div> </div>It was in the original Embers, and we're trying to be true to that. It's working for us so far too, so we haven't felt a need to change that. The Knights of the Chalice have their origin in it, and we're actually basing a chunk of the Dynasty stuff on that once we get there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suspect the PC origin (you ate a monster's heart to steal its power!) already does enough along those lines - Oroboroi chose to exile themselves from humanity, their lives before eating the Heart are an age of innocence that they deliberately abandoned and can never return to. </div> </div> </div>True, the whole &quot;First Sin&quot; thing is used in two different ways. Like I said though, I think what you just said should show you why I'm saying the games are completely different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T17:07:09-07:00","id":925568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=925544#post925544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it's such a different take on it. Beasts aren't supposed to be <b>&quot;real dragons&quot;</b>-*snip*.</div> </div> </div> </div>Look. I by and large make a point to ignore fan projects, and I'm only here because of a mis-click. I don't care much care for how you proceed on this game. Do what thou wilt.<br /> <br /> But much like &quot;Descent doesn't have real demons&quot;, I would kindly encourage you to take this mentality that the dragons of Beast aren't real dragons and toss it into a fire. Yes, they are embodiments of humanity's dark and primal self. They are also fucking dragons. They steal your gold, your sheep, your women, store them in their mountain, burn your fields, devour the pride king's wear on their brows and tear down any knights who come after them. They have armor like tenfold shields, teeth like swords, claws like spears, tails that strike like thunderbolts, wings like hurricanes, breath like death, and don't give a flaming shit if you disagree with them when they come to claim all you hold dear. When you are dragged by your hair into their Lair, you don't see a figment, an illusion-you see a fucking dragon about to have lunch.<br /> <br /> Kindly toss your &quot;They're not real dragons&quot; into a fire. That they are different kind of dragon does not stop them from being motherfucking dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-03-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T20:27:37-07:00","id":925663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=925568#post925568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kindly toss your &quot;They're not real dragons&quot; into a fire. That they are different kind of dragon does not stop them from being motherfucking dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>*sigh*<br /> <br /> Figured something like this would happen.<br /> <br /> What Arts says is true and honestly, a factor of all WoD games. The Kindred don't hold a monopoly on the concept of Vampire in WoD (The book Wicked Dead shows just how many blood suckers vary) and the same in Forsaken Chronicler's Guide with the Cursed. So on and so forth. Orobroroi and Beast occupy the same symbolism as True Fae, The Dragons of Mage, along with various others. Dividing them as one or the other in a purity test isn't going to help anyone.<br /> <br /> Now, if we can continue with the project without pissing off any more freelancers, that would be great.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll start adding the fluff to the philosophies section over the next several days, The draft has a good outline and time to start adding meat to bone to the next section.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T23:18:01-07:00","id":925749,"title":"","content":"Well... I don't think ArcaneArts read the rest of the argument. As he said, he wasn't actually paying attention.<br /> <br /> The argument wasn't that Beast can't be about Dragons, the argument is that the Oroboroi aren't the same thing, and I still stand by what I said, even if he misinterpreted the way I said it. Once again, I actually like Beast: it's a bit small-scope for me, but what's there is very well done.<br /> <br /> You're right though, Shock, it's getting a little absurd that we're suddenly on the defensive about a vague similarity to a completely different book. If it were the same book, we wouldn't be bothering with this one, so yeah, it's probably not productive to get into it anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> Moving on... Darinas wanted to alter the Knights, so we're doing that. Like I said, once I see people who like the project showing interest again, I'll start releasing stuff like that for them...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-04-2016, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:26:32-07:00","id":926086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=925749#post925749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Like I said, once I see people who like the project showing interest again, I'll start releasing stuff like that for them...</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't have anything to contribute, but I'd like to see stuff. Also, for the purposes of understanding how the game has changed, were would I find the most recent previous edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T16:13:29-07:00","id":926130,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Hi there, I'm glad you asked!</b><br /> The first few posts of this thread have information about the current project itself, including links to some releases. There's also these links:<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development#post20836\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is the last thread for the Embers project</span></a></b><br /> We're using material from all 3 editions, that thread, and the design notes, but mainly we're focusing on expanding the material from 2nd edition. The links to all of them are in that first post.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=892371#post892371\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">An outdated list I made a while back of the changes we were making at the time.</span></a></b><br /> I need to update the list on the first page of this thread. I guess I'll do that before Wednesday's meeting.<br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=906278#post906278\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Early release draft for the Deep Ones</span></a></b><br /> A chunk of this is probably going to look different soon: I'm making Docs for each of these antagonists so we have a more finalized release...</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T05:14:19-07:00","id":926995,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">NEW RELEASE THING!</span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Byul0i9IXo_Pw5aaC9gCfJd7xmF179n_XSGstrVY00I/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">The Order of the Bloody Chalice</span></a></b></u><br /> Here we present an ancient and secretive order of Blood Bathers, whose prime targets are the Oroboroi. In this document, you'll find what the Oroboroi have managed to learn about their history, culture, structure, rituals, powers, and tactics. The Knights are intended as a terrifying and relatively rare villain to throw at a group of experienced supernaturals or hunters, and can quickly throw them out of their element.<br /> <br /> We're really happy with this document, and we hope you all enjoy it as much as we enjoyed writing it!</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-06-2016, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T17:45:56-07:00","id":931098,"title":"","content":"<b>Team Application:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Position</b>: Fluff and Fiction Writer, Focusing On Antagonists<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Writing: </b>In-Character Philosophy of Ash Overview<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Philosophy of Ash-Destruction<br /> <br /> {Warlord Is Another Term For Hero}<br /> <br /> (Nicknames: Generals, Renewers, Despoilers)<br /> <br /> <i>First; let me welcome you to the world of the winged. Second; took you long enough. My troops were really starting to lobby for me to just kill that bastard myself and give you the Heart. But, you stuck through it, with only a little help from me,</i><br /> <br /> <i>Oh don't act so surprised. Surely you didn't think it wasn't a</i> little<i> unlikely that you discovered that old bastard was a dragon-and by eating his heart, you could become one-by a random pdf search, did you? Don't bother answering-I can tell by that look in your eye you're relieved that you finally get the full big picture. That's good, even if you don't join the practical chapter of our little clubhouses. But I think you will,because there's a reason you chose to eat the Heart and not rid the world of its baleful legacy forever. Before you ask, I'm not a mind reader-just very good at reading potential enemies and hesitant allies, which is to say I'm good at reading people who actually interact with me. Useful quality when knowing your opponent is the difference between a victory and a devastating rout.<br /> <br /> But I digress. Back to you-I read your blog, which is how you came to my attention. You were always unafraid to admit there were things in the world that weren't right, and you knew there were more things to wrong than just racism, class divide, or greed. But you didn't fall into the trap of assuming that everything bad was a single force-you're more of a conspiracy realist than a theorist, knowing that the hidden masters of the world are just a fractious, fallible, and occasionally noble as their subjects. Probably a little nastier on average, but no more so than politicians. Which is why, when you found a hidden master, obvious signs of magic, soft power and all, you didn't rant about it on that paranoid con man's show, or plaster his true nature across the media in all caps, or even make a note on your public blog-you followed him, studied him, tried to understand what made him tick. Even when you realized he was a far stranger being than any humanoid lizard from outer space, you studied further-you realized it was more a question of who he was, not what he was. And what you found horrified you. Paying off police, inciting riots, threatening politicians-it wasn't even the conspiracy, it was what the conspiracy was meant to do. Hurt people-sure, he thought it was about criminals, but you guessed he told criminals apart from the normal law-abiding populace by skin color. Barbarians, after all, are part of a different culture, which means they do actually look different-of course, we by definition are all barbarians. None of us speak Greek.<br /> <br /> But you didn't want just to stop him. You knew that if someone could be that petty, and awful, and cold, then other secret masters could be worse. More ambitious perhaps, but perhaps even worse, even more small-minded. And more importantly, you knew that hidden masters don't run everything-prejudice just happened for no good reason. You wanted to change things, but changing things without power is futile at best, uncontrollable at worst. And so you tore your predecessor down, broke his world to pieces-and you used his remains to draw up the blueprints to a better one.<br /> <br /> Well, the bad news is, there is a hidden master-just one that was born of racism rather than the other way around. A spirit, a parasite grown fat on unthinking privilege and the rage that comes from forcing others to confront their own benefits from hidden evil. almost a god of inbred purity, now. The good news is, you were right on all other counts-and dragons were the embodiments of the biggest enemy of God in the West.<br /> <br /> So I come to you with an offer of apprenticeship, one Devil to another-wanna make a Hell of Heaven?</i></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Qualifications: I'm the main and only writer behind the GURPS Monsters thread, and spent a significant portion of my life on a setting called<a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?640556-necro-nWoD-Infinite-Macarbre-Darkness-of-the-Endless-Space\" target=\"_blank\"> Darkness of the Endless Space</a>, which seemed to be popular before I got burnt out on it. I'm still fairly new as a writer, but I seem to be fairly popular and liked-I'm very good at writing antagonists and passable at short fiction in established settings, I've found.<br /> <br /> Interests: Again, antagonists and world-building, with some fiction if need be. Mostly fluff, but I can help brainstorm some more abstract Conditions and Tilts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T13:56:07-07:00","id":931557,"title":"","content":"Application for Leleil accepted... Lemme just add you to the list...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T12:30:05-07:00","id":932998,"title":"","content":"<b>Team Application:</b><br /> <br /> <b>Position-</b> writer, both fluff and crunch<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Writing- Musing about the Deep Ones</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">At the lowest depth of the Dreamtide, they lurk quietly. They live in cities of broken ideas and alien concepts, shaped from the madness of the pit called Pandemonium. There, they made thousands of new religions, laws and societies as they enslave the lower denizens of the nightmare realm- social structures both elegant and alien to the mind of both Man and Dragon. Their knowledge of the Dreamtide and its shaping are greater than almost any other race, allowing them to shape the forms of the mind as if it were clay. Some of them are willing to teach their secrets to those who come from the higher levels of the Dreamtide, shaping their dream-flesh as they wish if they are willing to pay the price, which changed from one monster to another- but is always alien and twisted. While the journey to the depths of the dream is dangerous, some among the Orobori are willing to go great lengths in order to achieve greater power. However, those touched by the Deep Ones are never the same as they used too- their touch gives freedom of form, yet it leave the mark of the pit upon them. Each time they twist the form, a part of their very beings is carried back to the wake world with the subject- and as the dragon takes her true form and rise in power, the resonance echos back to the pit, strengthening the primordial madness. Through the Orobori's awe, the Deep One's fear leaks, creeping into the minds of loyal subjects and shows them the greatness of Pandemonium. Slowly, the corruption spreads, and madness grows around the dragon. The more the Orobori seek the pit's freedom, the greater is the fear she spreads- until eventually, she becomes the embodiment of that madness, becoming from a divine king into a demonic tyrant.<br /> <br /> It is not to say one should stay away from the pit- after all, even the greatest among kings were touched by madness. But when you do, do it wisely- for all know that once the king lose his divine right to role, his subjects are allowed to claim his head. And Heart.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Qualifications-</b> well, I did wrote a lot of homebrew of all kinds through the years- mostly for Hunter, but also a couple of other projects including an attempt at a fan made game, a Shard, new splats for different games and more. For specific information, you could look at my signature.<br /> <br /> <b>Interests-</b> Dragon was my favorite fan-made game, and I was really sad to see it die out. Although I'm not sure I would have enough time to help as regular, I'll be happy to help as much as I can with whatever you need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T14:44:17-07:00","id":933069,"title":"","content":"<b> Application accepted </b><br /> The writing was a bit rambly, but we can work on that. Accept my Skype invitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T20:03:57-07:00","id":954163,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m in your attic, haunting your stuff.<br /> <br /> I read what you have so far. Your setting elements are great and consistent. However, some of the mechanics of the second edition don\u2019t fit the feel of your reboot. I have a few suggestions you may take or leave as you please.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> First, I\u2019ve drawn new dragon images for the five methods.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Link to Google Folder<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B31Gud9WnwZXRUZHVUhSc1hkTWs\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/drive/folde...UZHVUhSc1hkTWs</a></div>Please use these instead of those pictures from the first edition. When a player turns to the method section they\u2019ll want to see a cool image, and the clumsy art of my past does not make a good impression (Ironically you used an image I intended to replace the Slayer method image with in the Conviction section).<br /> As a good rule of thumb, if it has cursive initials instead of the initial grin it\u2019s from when I was a teenager and it shouldn\u2019t be used. It\u2019s too painful to look at! ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Second, I feel ablutions will need to be simplified to better correspond to the thematic elements of your new chronicles. Here are my recommendations: if you use these, do so as a replacer for the current ablutions instead of an addition. You said you were working on them in the shadows, though, so all of this might be redundant or contradicted already.<br /> <br /> Anyway, here\u2019s my pass on the ablutions.<br /> <br /> ======<br /> <br /> Weaponry<br /> Deadly weaponry built into the dragon\u2019s anatomy.<br /> Every two points of Weaponry manifest across the board increases the damage of the spawned weapons by 1.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> The weapon grows out of the dragon\u2019s flesh.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Weaponry: Damage (Common)<br /> Increases the raw damage of the weapon by one per point manifest.<br /> Additionally gives the dragon the option to upgrade the damage type associated with the attack: brawl can become lethal and weaponry can become aggravated.<br /> <br /> Weaponry: Cleave (Slayer)<br /> Increases the number of targets a single attack can strike by the points manifest. For attacks against multiple targets, use the highest armor rating and lowest defense rating and make one roll.<br /> <br /> Weaponry: Pierce (Finder)<br /> Allows the weapon to ignore an amount of armor equal to the points manifest.<br /> Ignores both worn and biological armor. Worn armor is shredded by the weapon\u2019s attack, reducing its rating by one per successful attack until it is destroyed. Supernatural gear is only temporarily damaged by this type of attack.<br /> <br /> Weaponry: Trauma (Trickster)<br /> Causes the attack to inflict the Trauma condition at a rating equal to the points manifest. Trauma doesn\u2019t stack from similar sources; only the highest Trauma from Ablutions counts.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">___<br /> Trauma &lt;X&gt; [Condition]<br /> Severe internal injury makes every action taxingly painful. The afflicted may only function at half physical capacity (halve physical skills and attributes for the purpose of forming dice pools, halve speed) or risk acquiring the Agonizing Pain tilt for the remainder of the scene. Trauma may only inflict this tilt once per scene.<br /> Trauma resolves when all wounds have been cleared from the afflicted. Resolving Trauma gives a beat.<br /> <br /> Agonizing Pain &lt;X&gt; [Tilt]<br /> Physical trauma is strained by overexertion and floors the afflicted with pain. The afflicted must suffer an amount equal to the triggering Trauma condition: this suffering can take the form of a penalty to all actions for the rest of the scene or the form of aggravated damage immediately. This is a sliding option: for instance a Trauma 4 trigger of the Agonizing Pain tilt could inflict 3 aggravated wounds and a -1 penalty at the afflicted\u2019s discretion. Choosing to take the aggravated damage grants one beat per wound suffered.<br /> ___</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Weaponry: Grapple (Challenger)<br /> The weapon may be used to initiate a grapple. Rolls to grapple and perform maneuvers receive +1 for each point manifest, and the dragon may attach a damage maneuver onto any other maneuver as a free action. The weapon cannot be removed from the struggle with the disarm maneuver but can be controlled by the grappled victim if they gain control of the struggle.<br /> <br /> Weaponry: Reliable (Inheritor)<br /> For each point manifest you may recycle one failed die back into the combat pool.</div>Physique<br /> Draconic ablution which enhances physical attributes.<br /> Every two points of Physique manifest across the board increases the dragon\u2019s size by 1, with all associated benefits of such growth.<br /> Health gained from these ablutions and the change in size is Heroic; track it on the bottom health bar and mark wounds there first. These wounds are ERASED when those health levels disappear from disbanding the ablution.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Increase in size and muscularity<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Physique: Strength (Slayer)<br /> Increases Strength by one per point manifest.<br /> Also multiplies throwing distance by its manifest rating and multiplies effective lifting strength by its manifest rating.<br /> <br /> Physique: Dexterity (Trickster)<br /> Increases Dexterity by one per point manifest.<br /> Additionally, the dragon may move through spaces as if her size is one rating smaller per point manifest, to a minimum size of 1.<br /> <br /> Physique: Stamina (Finder)<br /> Increases Stamina by one per point manifest.<br /> Additionally, the dragon may multiply her effective stamina rating by its manifest rating for the purpose of holding her breath.<br /> <br /> Physique: Armor (Inheritor)<br /> Increases Armor by +1/+1 per point manifest. This armor is considered biological and is counted in addition to any worn armor.<br /> <br /> Physique: Regeneration (Challenger)<br /> When the dragon would recover 1 point of health, she instead recovers a number of points of health equal to this ablution\u2019s manifest rating. This includes health regained through natural healing, health from reforging with breath, and health recovered by medical attention.</div>Stature<br /> Draconic ablution which enhances social impact.<br /> Every two points of Stature manifest across the board render the dragon\u2019s features more striking and memorable, increasing social rolls by one.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Increasingly sharp and statuesque facial structure<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Stature: Presence (Inheritor)<br /> Increases Presence by one per point manifest.<br /> Additionally, all parties will respect the dragon as if she held status in their organization equal to the points manifest in this Ablution.<br /> <br /> Stature: Manipulation (Trickster)<br /> Increases Manipulation by one per point manifest.<br /> When rolling to open doors while this ablution is manifest, the roll applies to a number of doors equal to the points manifest (instead of just one). This is true if attempting to persuade a single target (punching through many doors simultaneously) or when working with a group (simultaneously opening single doors of multiple targets in a single roll).<br /> <br /> Stature: Composure (Finder)<br /> Increases Composure by one per point manifest.<br /> Additionally, when opponents are trying to persuade the dragon they must overcome an additional number of doors equal to the points manifest in this ablution.<br /> <br /> Stature: Predator Glare (Slayer)<br /> The dragon may stare down a target, forcing them to do nothing but flee for a number of turns equal to the points manifest in this ablution. The first such stare in a scene is free, but subsequent stares require a point of Willpower.<br /> The target of a Predator Glare loses an amount of Willpower equal to the points manifest in this ablution. If that reduction would render them completely depleted, they will flee <i>without regard to their own safety</i>, potentially leaping through windows out of skyscrapers to escape.<br /> Mortals have no defense against this ability, but supernatural beings initiate a clash of wills: Presence + Heartstring against Composure + Resistance.<br /> <br /> Stature: Word of the Crown (Challenger)<br /> The dragon may issue a command (for 1 Breath) with a number of steps equal to the points manifest in this ablution. Someone who hears the command must obey.<br /> Mortals have no defense against this ability, but may roll Resolve \u2013 Stature: Word of the Crown if the command places them in immediate danger or at risk of a breaking point. Supernatural beings initiate a clash of wills: Manipulation + Heartstring against Composure + Resistance. Additionally, like mortals they get an opportunity to break free of the command (if subjugated) when placed in immediate danger or at risk of a breaking point.<br /> Only one person must follow the orders for each command; the dragon may decide WHO exactly is subject to the power by spending 1 Willpower; otherwise the storyteller decides. The mortal performing the steps of the command receives a bonus to all rolls related to that command, equal to the points manifest in this ablution.</div>Acuity<br /> Draconic ablution which enhances mental capacity.<br /> Every two points of Acuity manifest across the board increases the dragon\u2019s perception by one.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Increasingly complex and numerous sigils form across the body, colored in the same tone the dragon\u2019s scales will eventually take.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Acuity: Intelligence (Finder)<br /> Increases Intelligence by one per point manifest.<br /> Additionally, each scene the dragon may receive a number of storyteller hints (or clues towards a discovery) equal to the points manifest.<br /> <br /> Acuity: Wits (Slayer)<br /> Increases Wits by one per point manifest.<br /> Additionally, Acuity: Wits is added to the dragon\u2019s defense, even if she has sacrificed it this turn.<br /> <br /> Acuity: Resolve (Challenger)<br /> Increases Composure by one per point manifest.<br /> Additionally, when Willpower is spent or lost, roll a number of chance dice equal to the points manifest in this ablution. If any show 10, the Willpower is recovered.<br /> <br /> Acuity: Keen Senses (Trickster)<br /> Grants +1 to Perception rolls per point manifest.<br /> Additionally, the dragon may make a perception roll to detect extrasensory phenomenon, such as electrical energy in the air, infrared and ultraviolet light, dreamstuff, and subsonic and hypersonic vibration. This ability also allows them to detect supernatural power, potentially revealing other dragons or supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> Acuity: Eye of Value (Inheritor)<br /> Once per scene, the dragon may conduct research rolls on an object in 3 second intervals rather than the usual extended action periods. The number of such accelerated rolls possible each scene is equal to the points manifest in Acuity: Eye of Value, but successes accumulated may be applied later to traditional duration extended action rolls.</div>Respiration<br /> Draconic ablution which unleashes concentrated Dreamtide energy from the Heart.<br /> Breath weapons have a 10 yard cone by default (working like explosives, but with the firearms skill), but every two points of Respiration manifest doubles that range.<br /> 10 \u00e0 20 \u00e0 20 \u00e0 40 \u00e0 40 \u00e0 80 \u00e0 80 \u00e0 160 (\u201cClose\u201d ranges)<br /> A point of Willpower may be spent to exclude specific targets from the effects of a Respiration.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Increasingly bright and warm glow in the chest over the Heart, eventually resembling a patch of lava.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Respiration: Inferno (Common)<br /> By spending one point of breath, the dragon lets loose a blast of flames, which inflicts aggravated damage as fire equal to the points manifest, and applies the \u201cOn Fire\u201d tilt.<br /> <br /> Respiration: Acid (Common)<br /> By spending one point of breath, the dragon expels a surge of corrosive acid, which dissolves an amount of structure on impacted objects equal to the points manifest, regardless of the durability. Supernatural objects are not permanently destroyed by this attack but if it reduces their structure to 0 they lose one dot of their rating.<br /> The acid destroys clothes as well but will not inflict harm on living things.<br /> <br /> Respiration: Blizzard (Slayer)<br /> By spending one point of breath, the dragon emits a wave of freezing cold, which pierces an amount of armor equal to the points manifest, inflicts lethal damage, and applies the \u201cHypothermia\u201d tilt.<br /> <br /> Respiration: Hypnotic Dust (Trickster)<br /> By spending one point of breath, the dragon exhumes a cloud of hypnotic particles. Anyone who inhales these particles suffers the Hypnotic Dust condition, at a rating equal to the points manifest in this ablution.<br /> Subsequent exhalations clog the air, causing a choking fit and bashing damage to all who inhale the dust.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">___<br /> Hypnotic Dust &lt;X&gt; [Condition]<br /> Dreamstuff-charged particles induce the mind of the afflicted to open the Ora and embrace sleep. If the rating of this condition exceeds the afflicted\u2019s stamina he becomes listless, lowers himself to the ground, and sleeps immediately. Otherwise each turn spent in the dust increases the rating of this condition by one unless the afflicted holds his breath.<br /> Supernatural beings add their Resistance to their Stamina for the purpose of determining if and when the embrace of sleep occurs.<br /> This sleep is normal and triggers the normal benefit of sleep, but the afflicted cannot be roused until the scene ends or they suffer physical harm.<br /> The condition is resolved when the subject is removed from the dust or when the scene ends, and rewards a beat unless the afflicted was friendly to the dragon.<br /> ___</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Respiration: Inspiring Light (Inheritor)<br /> By spending one point of breath, the dragon exhumes a burst of warm light. Anyone touched by this light receives a pool of bonus dice equal to the points manifest in this ablution. These dice can be spent as the targets please for the remainder of the scene. Unspent dice are lost at scene\u2019s end.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Respiration: X-Ray (Finder)<br /> By spending one point of breath, the dragon exhumes a beam of radiation which allows her to see though objects. For the rest of the scene, the dragon receives a bonus to perception rolls equal to the points manifest in this ablution. Additionally, all objects held by targets in the area of the beam are revealed to everyone who saw the ray; searching them for weapons or hidden materials automatically succeeds.<br /> Finally, if the dragon is researching for a discovery, she immediately unveils a number of clues equal to the points manifest in this ablution.<br /> <br /> Respiration: Tempest Roar (Challenger)<br /> By spending one point of breath, the dragon roars with terrible fury. For the rest of the scene, anyone caught in this roar suffers the \u201cCower before God\u201d condition at a level equal to the points manifest in this ablution.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">___<br /> Cower before God &lt;X&gt; [Condition]<br /> The terrifying power of the Tempest Roar leaves the afflicted shaking in their boots. Any action they would take which could go against the roaring Oroboros suffers a penalty equal to the rating of this condition.<br /> The afflicted may voluntarily suffer a dramatic failure against the Oroboros to end the condition. Otherwise, it ends at the end of the scene. This condition awards a beat when resolved.<br /> ___</span></div>Anatomy<br /> Draconic ablution which modifies the body for metamorphic advantage.<br /> Every two points of Anatomy manifest increases the species speed factors by one.<br /> <b>Tell:</b> Larger and larger patches of scales, feathers, or fur across the body, with a general drift towards an animalistic appearance.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Anatomy: Chameleon (Common)<br /> The dragon may blend with her surroundings, allowing her to attempt to move undetected without cover, effectively becoming invisible. A point of breath is required to hide equipment and clothes in this same manner.<br /> Anyone attempting to perceive the dragon suffers a penalty to such attempt equal to the points manifest in this ablution, plus the dragon\u2019s Heartstring. Using infrared goggles or an equivalent will halve this penalty.<br /> For one point of Willpower, Anatomy: Chameleon negates an amount of supernatural-sourced perception equal to its points manifest (That is, Anatomy: Chameleon 3 can block 3-dot supernatural powers which perceive hidden things).</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Anatomy: Scale of Fortune (Common)<br /> By inflicting one lethal wound to rip off scales, the dragon may gain a temporary Resources rating equal to the points manifest in this Ablution. Once removed, the scales take the form of gold coins; generally they are plain but for one point of Willpower they can be made to look like officially minted currency.<br /> <br /> Anatomy: Toxic Blood (Common)<br /> By spending one point of breath, the dragon\u2019s blood becomes dangerously toxic. When the dragon suffers lethal damage, she bleeds this terrible substance on everyone within melee reach. Targets contacted by the blood suffer the Corrosion Spray tilt, at a rating equal to the points manifest in this ablution.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">___<br /> Corrosion Spray &lt;X&gt; [Tilt]<br /> The afflicted suffers a number of bashing wounds equal to the rating of this tilt. They will continue to suffer this damage each turn until they remove the clothing covered by the toxic blood or rinse it away with pure water.<br /> ___</span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Anatomy: Burrow (Common)<br /> By spending one point of Willpower, the dragon can dig through a number of feet of solid matter equal to the points manifest in this ablution. During the turn of the dig, the dragon\u2019s defense is increased by the distance travelled. Soft and loose materials like soil triple the distance the dragon can dig in a single use of Burrow.<br /> <b>[This ablution could be perceived as a weaker version of Flight, and may need to be pruned. It also diminishes the impact of Physique: Dexterity which is used for bypassing security systems]</b></span></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Anatomy: Preemptive Focus (Common)<br /> The dragon is able to take aim on activities in which the concept should not normally be possible. For instance, the dragon may aim a repair on an automobile to gain a bonus to her rolls when she begins. The number of time intervals which can be spent aiming with preemptive focus and likewise the maximum bonus attainable is equal to the points manifest in this ablution.<br /> Aiming for a task takes the same amount of time as a single interval of work on the task. For instance, 30 minute repair intervals requires 30 minutes of preemptive focus to gain a +1 aiming bonus, while a one-turn baseball bat swing takes one turn of preemptive focus to gain a +1 aiming bonus.<br /> The bonuses gained from aiming with preemptive focus persist as long as the dragon remains intent on her task. So as long as she is repairing the vehicle, every roll of the extended action receives the aim bonus. Likewise as long as she is wielding the bat in combat the aim bonus applies to all attacks made with the bat (instead of just the first). Firearms can be aimed with preemptive focus as well; aim bonuses persist across multiple turns of shots when used with this ablution.<br /> <b>[This ablution\u2019s mechanic is fairly complex to describe; the trait may need to be pruned or redirected into an imposition]</b></span></div>Excellence<br /> Draconic ablution which taps into otherworldly power.<br /> Every two points of Excellence manifest increases Willpower by one.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Excellence: Skill of the Gods (Common)<br /> For a point of breath, 3s, 2s, and 1s on a roll may be treated as 8s, 9s, and 10s (respectively). Additionally, you may reroll a number of dice from the pool equal to the points manifest in this ablution.<br /> If the breath is not paid before the dice are rolled, it may be paid by also suffering a single aggravated wound.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Excellence: Flight (Common)<br /> For a point of breath this scene the dragon may take to the air and fly.<br /> Flight speed is (Stamina + Strength + Species Flight Factor) x Flight Ablution manifest. Dragons have a Species Flight Factor of 18. Birds have a Species Flight Factor of 54 to 84.<br /> Flight\u2019s manifest points are added to defense while airborne. Additionally, while airborne dodge actions are twice as effective and also count against ranged and firearm attacks.<br /> <br /> Excellence: Impassioned Effort (Common)<br /> The dragon\u2019s Willpower expenditures receive a bonus equal to the points manifest. For instance, using a Willpower ability with Excellence: Impassioned Effort 4 gives the corresponding roll a +4. Spending Willpower to boost a regular action with Excellence: Impassioned Effort 3 gives +6 instead of +3. Using Willpower to raise resistance with Excellence: Impassioned Effort 5 grants +7 instead of +2 to the resistance attribute.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\">Excellence: Speed of Information (Common)<br /> For one point of Willpower per roll, the dragon may divide the duration of an extended action\u2019s interval by the points manifest in this ablution +1. For instance, a 30 minute repair interval subjected to Excellence: Speed of Information 4 would instead take 6 minutes per roll.<br /> <b>[This ablution might need to be cut, since it conflicts with Acuity: Eye of Value. It has a wider range of application but is less accelerated.]</b></span><br /> <br /> Excellence: Fangs of the Beast (Reimagining)<br /> For one point of Willpower, the dragon may utilize another supernatural being\u2019s means of gathering energy to generate breath. The amount of breath the dragon can generate is equal to the points manifest in this ablution. For instance, a dragon might drink vitae from a human, but would only be able to accumulate up to 4 breath in that manner while manifesting Excellence: Fangs of the Beast 4.<br /> The type of supernatural the dragon can mimic with this ablution depends on which one triggered the ablution\u2019s acquisition with the reimagining. That is, a dragon can\u2019t draw energy like a changeling if she\u2019s hanging out with werewolves.<br /> <br /> Excellence: Barrier (Reimagining)<br /> For one point of breath per scene, the dragon may generate a forcefield around herself. This field stops objects from approaching her person and functions as full cover with a durability rating equal to the points manifest. As it is a field of energy it has no structure and any damage it suffers to durability is repaired at the start of the turn.<br /> The field acts as cover only against objects to which the dragon is perceived invulnerable.</div>======<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve tried to keep the spirit of the ablutions you chose to keep as well as facilitate your new Reimagining mechanic: instead of removing ablutions the storyteller can shift dots into another ablution of that category, or into the man-forged category.<br /> I also tried to combine some of the traits which had overlap, cleaving to the clearly dominant power.<br /> <br /> The categories each contain at least five Ablutions, which can be purchased separately. I\u2019ve made an effort to put them into methods I thought would be appropriate. I\u2019ve also doubled down on the power of this stuff; playing a dragon with these Ablutions should feel awesome, which is appropriate considering the drawbacks worked into the narrative portion of the game.<br /> <br /> Tells are intended to follow the rule you established in your draft\u2014that is every point manifest in a particular ablution requires a size &lt;x&gt; item to conceal it. Since ablutions are in categories, stacking the same type of ablution can result in traits very difficult to conceal. For example, getting Physique 12 from Physique: Stamina 5, Physique: Armor 3, and Physique: Strength 4 would require a size 12 object to hide the supernatural features (that is, it would require hiding behind a small family vehicle). Also, by putting the tells by category they can be rendered more general in their approach, giving the player more freedom to make the dragon look the way they want. When each separate ablution has a unique tell, eventually you run out of things to display on the body (as you saw in the second edition with the completely random and unrelated tells!).<br /> <br /> Ablutions need to be complex enough to warrant their experience cost, but simple enough to be tallied quickly when used. I\u2019ve tried to attain that balance with this pass here, and I hope that my efforts were successful. Again, certain ablutions have been eliminated because of overlap (Mesmerizing Gaze was just a weaker form of the Word of the Crown; Spines was an ineffective overlap of Corrosive Blood; Sing oh Muse and Master and Student were better implementations of Skill of the Gods; there may have been others but those were the big ones). What\u2019s left should be diverse enough to be interesting but condensed enough so as to not overwhelm prospective players. I couldn\u2019t come up with much for the reimagining ablutions, but perhaps that\u2019s a good thing. Reimagined ablutions might work better as conditions instead of actual ablutions the dragon can turn on and off.<br /> Still, you said you were analyzing the mechanical side of that idea and I\u2019m sure you have some good notes on where you\u2019re going.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t had a chance to pass the Deep One ablutions with scrutiny yet, but from my first read they should fit into these categories fairly easily. At worst they can have their own category, but you get what I\u2019m going for, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Third is Divinity. This mechanic was originally implemented to give dragons a general \u2018monster\u2019 vibe if their tells didn\u2019t do it for them. That being said, the way it\u2019s written is too restrictive for the feel I believe you\u2019re aiming at in your revival. I\u2019ve been toying with some ideas and I think I\u2019ve got something that could work.<br /> <br /> ======<br /> Divinity<br /> <br /> For every ten points manifest in an ablution, you attain your next degree of divinity. Divinity increases your size by its current rating and doubles the effectiveness of an ablution category\u2019s bonus. You should pick which categories are affiliated with which divinity levels the first time you attain them, and mark those categories on your sheet.<br /> <br /> Example<br /> Divinity 1 Weaponry (Your biological weapon does 1 additional damage per point of Weaponry Ablutions manifest)<br /> Divinity 2 Weaponry (Your biological weapon does 2 additional damage per point of Weaponry Ablutions manifest)<br /> Divinity 3 Physique (Size increased by 1 for every point of Physique Ablutions manifest)<br /> Divinity 4 Physique (Size increased by 2 for every point of Physique Ablutions manifest)<br /> Divinity 5 Physique (Size increased by 4 for every point of Physique Ablutions manifest) [Yep, Kaiju it up here]<br /> Divinity 6 Respiration [Dreamtide only] (Range of breath attacks doubled for every point of Respiration Ablutions manifest)<br /> Divinity 7 Respiration [Dreamtide only] (Range of breath attacks quadrupled for every point of Respiration Ablutions manifest)<br /> Divinity 8 Anatomy [Dreamtide only] (Species speed factor increased by 1 for every point of Anatomy Ablutions manifest) [At such a big size, the low speed is a detriment]<br /> Divinity 9 Anatomy [Dreamtide only] (Species speed factor increased by 2 for every point of Anatomy Ablutions manifest) [Gotta speed up]<br /> Divinity 10 Anatomy [Dreamtide only] (Species speed factor increased by 4 for every point of Anatomy Ablutions manifest) [to be the Jormungandr world destroyer of your dreams!]<br /> <br /> I know multiplicative mechanics fly out of reasonable scope relatively quickly, but we agreed that doubling down on the power was the right idea. Also, this kind of prowess might be needed in the depths of the Dreamtide, the only place attaining the last levels of divinity is possible.<br /> <br /> ======<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fourth, I was looking at your three new philosophies and I think they should have names related to bodily humours (in line with the others).<br /> <br /> ======<br /> <br /> Instead of <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Materialism</span></b>, I think <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Sinew</b></span> would work well (as it emphasizes the connections between various body parts), or possibly Claw (the hand which distributes). <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Wisdom</b></span> could be <b><span style=\"color:#008000\">Nerves</span></b> (taking the brain literally) or Anima (taking the brain as a house for the soul). <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Nihilism</b></span> could be <span style=\"color:#006400\"><b>Bile</b></span> (representing their reprehensible view of the universe and their pursuit of wretched [heh, wretch] activities) or Flesh (representing the hedonism which sometimes accompanies nihilism). Alternatively, <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Greenhorn</b></span> might work as the <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>\u201cFolly of Flesh\u201d</b></span> (instead of a Philosophy) since their connection to the Oroboros condition is as fleeting as the skin flaking off the body\u2019s surface.<br /> <br /> Naming the social splats after humours has several functions: first it relates them to an obsolete ideology of medicine, drawing parallel to their own obsolete nature in the world, and second it enhances the body horror, emphasizing gruesome terminology consistently throughout the book.<br /> ======<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, the Purviews. If the first edition and its [Power] Philosophies taught us anything, it is that specific mechanical ordering does not create engaging gameplay. Impositions need to have a clear and easily understood function which can be blended with others in the purview. Some that are in your test draft are not achieving this, such as Ruin\u2019s abilities which are leaning too heavily on mechanics. Perhaps the impositions should instead take a more narrative approach to power instead of tweaking mechanics.<br /> Still, it sounds like you\u2019re on top of that. I had planned to do a pass on Purviews to give you, but I\u2019ll wait since you\u2019ve said they\u2019re in flux.<br /> <br /> <br /> Great work so far!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":". 10-27-2016, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:32:00-07:00","id":954544,"title":"","content":"CJC, are you sure you don't want to join the Skype chat? You seem like you'd be a good addition to the main team...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:44:36-07:00","id":954555,"title":"","content":"I have social anxiety with regards to video chat, which in my mind is a more stressful form of telephone chat (which I find very difficult). When I have the opportunity to respond with a letter, I can custom tailor what I want to say, proofread it, and remove portions which are unclear or potentially inflammatory (thereby preventing a miscommunication which could result in hurt feelings or broken friendships). I also lack the personality to interrupt someone which prevents me from getting a word in edgewise.<br /> <br /> To that end, I would be unable to contribute to a video chat conversation. Without the ability to collaborate in any meaningful way, scheduling around my presence would be a waste of everyone's time.<br /> <br /> Besides, you've got Shock. Dragon is his brainchild; I'm just the au pair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:51:22-07:00","id":954627,"title":"","content":"The Skype chat is mostly text between meetings, which we've had people text through. I also don't foresee there being a problem if you DID try to talk: we're pretty good about stopping and saying &quot;what does everyone think?&quot; at key decision points. At the very least, it'd be nice to have a more direct method of talking to you about things...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T16:53:14-07:00","id":954685,"title":"","content":"<b>EDIT:</b> I'm a self-loathing narcissist. I am frequently beset with fits of self-importance followed by pits of self-hatred.<br /> The original contents of this post were an example of the former.<br /> <br /> Normally I'm against a revisionist approach to the internet. It's not right for me or anyone to edit away blemishes or character flaws. In this case, though, I feel the act is necessary to avoid damaging the reputation of this project.<br /> <br /> I'm a mess. The Orobori Chronicles is not. Do not let my fleeting association with the project cast aspersions of gloom on what is shaping up to be a truly remarkable fan work.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>TL, DR:</b> IGNORE ME!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":". 09-24-2016, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T12:45:18-07:00","id":975653,"title":"","content":"I should probably post something here so you all know that this is still going and we're still accepting new applicants...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T23:27:13-07:00","id":978887,"title":"","content":"By the way, how is this going so far? Whereabouts are you in the process?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T13:56:41-07:00","id":980420,"title":"","content":"We're about a quarter of the way through the first draft of the final book. We're planning on releasing papers for the Deep Ones, Nightmares, and Nihilists soon, like with the Bloody Chalice, as well as Chapters 1, 2, and 3 soon enough, hopefully throughout October. I'd like to pull together some people from the other projects for the storytelling chapter, as it'd be nice to throw down advice that none of the other books offer.<br /> <br /> We're still looking for artists and editors, because we could use new people to push progress with us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T10:07:51-07:00","id":991006,"title":"","content":"<b>Team Application</b><br /> <br /> <b>Position-</b> Editor, though I would also be happy to add to necessary fluff/crunch writing<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Writing- Knight of the Hunt</b> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> As soon as the prey starts running I realize I have put this off for too long. My breath runs ragged and the blades on each hip rattle with each step. Sloppy and disgraceful, but not so much that it will get away. I've been at this too many years to not have learned how to recover from a mistake. Not a decade ago and I would have had the prey captured and drained before it ever saw me, yet here I am chasing it like a fledgling neonate. The prey thinking like an animal, running downwind in the hopes that I will lose its scent. Perhaps it is one of the wolven kind whose blood gives one such intolerable aggression before the transition is done. The prey tries to wend its way through alleyways, thinking I will lose its trail, but I have learnt these streets too well for such a trick. Wend...the word is going out of fashion, is it not? I must be careful to avoid such anachronisms. The languages change slowly but one can quickly be left behind without close attention. Nothing signals a potential target so much as slipping into dead speech before closing in. But these distractions do not become me. I have let it get ahead of me again. Experience only serves so well when the body fails you. For a moment I am caught under a streetlamp, rare in an area as crime-ridden and deserted as this, and glimpse my hand. Its lined features warn I have been careless. By my estimation I have aged ten years in as many minutes. Should the chase persist I will not last through the night. But I have no need of fear. The prey it out of options, and at the end of an alleyway it cowers in its exhaustion. I draw close and in a silent movement wrest my weapon from its sheath. Wrest. Another term to be discarded from a bygone age. But what is the nature of this prey? Young. Ten to twelve, by my estimation, and female as its slender frame reveals. But I must be cautious; these appearances can deceive and destroy. More than once has an heir to hell hidden its true terror until a careless squire saw his end. I shall not be as they. I shall endure. I shall survive. I will outlast them all and cleanse this world in blood. </div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <b>Qualifications-</b> I am currently a RPG and board game reviewer on GamingTrend.com, where I just today published an interview with Richard Thomas. I have also written a number of much more boring law-related articles for the American Bar Association. Those are unrelated to homebrewing except in that they give me more practice writing and editing.<br /> <br /> <b>Interests-</b> I have been enamored with Dragon since I first read it, and I am incredibly happy that it is continuing to get refined and updated over time. It has dark themes of power and paranoia that even the World of Darkness has yet to rival.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T17:03:54-07:00","id":991179,"title":"","content":"I have an antagonist idea that is connected with the Old Gods if you want to hear it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-22-2016, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:12:37-07:00","id":993093,"title":"","content":"Sorry this took so long. We've been slow and I've been overwhelmed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=991006#post991006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Position-</b> Editor, though I would also be happy to add to necessary fluff/crunch writing</div> </div> </div> </div>We're understaffed and undermotivated as is, so yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Sample Writing- Knight of the Hunt</b> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty competent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Qualifications-</b> I am currently a RPG and board game reviewer on GamingTrend.com, where I just today published an interview with Richard Thomas. I have also written a number of much more boring law-related articles for the American Bar Association. Those are unrelated to homebrewing except in that they give me more practice writing and editing. </div> </div> </div>Oh good, another high-level writer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Interests-</b> I have been enamored with Dragon since I first read it, and I am incredibly happy that it is continuing to get refined and updated over time. It has dark themes of power and paranoia that even the World of Darkness has yet to rival. </div> </div> </div>Right, you sound motivated, and excitement is what the team is lacking.<br /> <br /> <b>Application Accepted</b><br /> Please PM me your Skype name and I'll get you on the docs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:13:31-07:00","id":993096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=991179#post991179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an antagonist idea that is connected with the Old Gods if you want to hear it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um.... Yes?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T20:10:22-07:00","id":993273,"title":"","content":"My basic idea is an Old God cult that is posing as a self- help group called Sunstone Counselling. They are led by a former televangelist named Bill Cottonwood, but rumor has it Bill answers to a council that is made out of powerful dream sorcerers and elders of the cult.<br /> <br /> The cult's real name is The Sons of the Void but they decided to hide behind their current cover because of the Orobori.<br /> <br /> I will go into more detail later. Also, if the Old Gods aren't possible I could use the Scholars of Void","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-25-2016, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T12:37:51-07:00","id":993636,"title":"","content":"Sorry for double posting but I have a question. Are the Old God's a possible candidate for worship by cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T13:55:44-07:00","id":993683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=993636#post993636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for double posting but I have a question. Are the Old God's a possible candidate for worship by cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the Old Gods are essentially Dream Cthulhu. They aren't really awake or aware and if they were they would probably drive humanity mad or dominate us from their lairs in the deep Dreamtide. Cults might certainly worship them and get 'visions' from the sleeping god's dreams, but they're not the kind of thing that you meet on the street. Even the elder dragons and the Deep Ones fear their waking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:15:34-07:00","id":993696,"title":"","content":"Ok thanks for telling me. I wanted to know because my antagonists pretty much worship the Old God's and I wanted to know if it was possible","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:17:55-07:00","id":993698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=993696#post993696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok thanks for telling me. I wanted to know because my antagonists pretty much worship the Old God's and I wanted to know if it was possible</div> </div> </div> </div>Worshipping an Old God, yes, being able to see/summon/become an Old God, not so much.<br /> <br /> Mind you, this is all going off of when I was a part of the project. Which was over 3 months ago now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:57:46-07:00","id":993718,"title":"","content":"I already knew they could not be summoned, due to them being asleep and all. I was also planning on them worshipping two old gods instead of one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:34:52-07:00","id":993741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=993718#post993718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already knew they could not be summoned, due to them being asleep and all. I was also planning on them worshipping two old gods instead of one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like as good an idea as any. Out of curiosity, what kind of gods are they? Are they gods of anything in particular or just divine immensities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:09:08-07:00","id":993758,"title":"","content":"They say their Gods are brother and sister and worship them together.. They believe the sister represents pleasure while the brother represents death and nightmares.<br /> <br /> Also, does the self-help group concept sound good to you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-26-2016, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T12:58:01-07:00","id":994170,"title":"","content":"I could try to post a small snippet of information about the cult's cover. Also, sorry for the double post","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-27-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:56:57-07:00","id":995397,"title":"","content":"Everything AJF said is accurate. The old gods COULD have a cult, but they're like Cthulhu: they're asleep and there are forces working to prevent them from waking. Now, that DOESN'T mean a plot to wake them couldn't come up in a campaign, because a sufficient disturbance in Pandemonium might actually do that, nor does it mean that they aren't dangerous. I'd make this &quot;Bill Cottonwood&quot; a high level Dragon of Void, because that'd give him the ability to travel down to where they are and potentially commune with them...<br /> <br /> It sounds like you have a fine idea for a campaign there.<br /> <br /> Edit: I should note, we haven't bothered to flesh out the Old Gods yet. They're not a part of the core game or lore, or even a major part of the setting we've built.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 10-29-2016, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T16:28:29-07:00","id":995420,"title":"","content":"Alright Bill Cottonwood will be a dragon of void. The cult's front, Sunstone Counselling, will be one of those self-help companies that harp on about their success and how wonderful their 12 step program is. Their clients would be lured in not only by the idea of ditching what is holding them back, but by Cottonwood himself. Before becoming a dragon, Bill was a well-known and respected televangelist and his good reputation would draw in clients. But what no one knows is that the program is being used to recruit out potential members of the cult. Sunstone's headquarters are in Austin, Texas but the campaign will start in Seattle, Washington.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T16:39:27-07:00","id":995426,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000080\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">HELLO<br /> <br /> WE ARE HERE IN THE<br /> <br /> WEEKLY<br /> MEETING<br /> <br /> <br /> CURRENTLY WORKING ON....</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s6.postimg.org/j2p96b43l/Deep_One_Skul.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T16:42:04-07:00","id":995428,"title":"","content":"What is that? Also, when you picture Sunstone's cultists just picture men in matching suits and with creepy smiles on their faces","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T08:33:08-07:00","id":995650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=995428#post995428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't you like to know...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, when you picture Sunstone's cultists just picture men in matching suits and with creepy smiles on their faces </div> </div> </div>Clich\u00e9. Whatever happened to the perfectly normal cults, where the only way you know that there's anything up other than being overly friendly and polite is when you realize they're wearing magic underwear? I'd like to see that.<br /> <br /> There. That's the cult of the Old Gods. They wear magic underwear that protects them from the Oroboroi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 10-30-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T09:59:14-07:00","id":995688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=995650#post995650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't you like to know...<br /> <br /> <br /> Clich\u00e9. Whatever happened to the perfectly normal cults, where the only way you know that there's anything up other than being overly friendly and polite is when you realize they're wearing magic underwear? I'd like to see that.<br /> <br /> There. That's the cult of the Old Gods. They wear magic underwear that protects them from the Oroboroi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those smiling men are just the cult's recruiters or as Sunstone calls them, &quot; Seekers&quot;. The highest ranked cultist the Orobori would see would be the counselors, the men and women who teach the doctrine of the Sunstone and by extension, the cult's. Also, Bill was taught the doctrine while on a mission trip to Nepal by the leader of a order of monks who also worshipped the Old Gods. Shortly after converting to the monks religion, Orobori showed up and destroyed the whole monestary. Somehow Bill managed to escape, but not before killing one of the Orobori and stealing it's heart.<br /> <br /> After days of roaming the mountains of Nepal, Bill decided to eat the heart to stave off starvation, not knowing what will happen when he did. After eating the heart, he became one of the same monsters that tried to kill him.He then spent the next thirty years in the mountains slowly building up his power. In 2000, he finally came home to America and started Sunstone Counselling, a self-help company he claimed would help people ditch the things that held them back. The doctrine that he and his future counselors taught was a abridged version that the monks taught Bill. Within ten years, Sunstone grew into a multi-national corporation with other 10,000 clients.<br /> <br /> Although almost everyone knows about Sunstone and most of their doctrine, no one knows the sinister intentions of the company. Sunstone's goal is to awaken the sleeping Old Gods and they won't heisitate to kill anyone, even their own clients, to accomplish this end. Sunstone's Board of Directors, who are led by Mr. Cottonwood, are made out of some of the Old God's most devoted worshippers and a fellow dragon by the name of Ronald Calipe. Both Bill and Robert are Void dragons, with Bill being the oldest and most powerful.<br /> <br /> Also, those smiles the recruiters have are fake. They won't be smiling when they try to gun you down with a SMG. That is actually a scene in my chronicle.<br /> <br /> I just realized something. The chronicle will basically be Dragons Vs. The Cult of Cthulu except if the cult was a actually a corporation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 10-30-2016, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T15:13:01-07:00","id":997396,"title":"","content":"If you want me to post a team-member application just ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:09:51-07:00","id":998361,"title":"","content":"...why do you need me to ask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:26:40-07:00","id":998377,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to know if you wanted me on board. Also, what did you think of the cult's backstory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T20:33:57-07:00","id":998589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=998377#post998377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what did you think of the cult's backstory?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was kind of scattered with cliche, and I'm not really seeing an underlying theme or image you're going for, just a set of tropes that sound cool without alot of substance to tie them together. It's not bad for the villain of a single campaign, but it's not something I'd put in a book for players to use repeatedly for multiple scenarios.<br /> <br /> With the Bloody Chalice and Deep Ones, we do research into existing concepts while talking over what the most interesting and insightful twists and bombshells we can place into them are. We don't just bang them out over a short period. The Deep Ones document is taking so long because it legitimately takes time to craft a versatile scenario that is sensible, original, and intriguing.<br /> <br /> When we get into the Old Gods (and we will, because you're right that we need to), they'll be something with much more thought than the villain of a single campaign. But first, give us time to elaborate on the Deep Ones, the Nightmares, the Usurpers, and the Reptilian Conspiracies...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T22:40:50-07:00","id":998623,"title":"","content":"I've been working on stuff in the background. Since you're fleshing out antagonists and setting, I figured I'd put some elbow grease into mechanics.<br /> <br /> I made a second pass of Ablutions and my first pass of Purviews.<br /> <br /> You can read what I've come up with <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17xSWyoBgfa9ZULDXczUTn6DLEF2rJ4z-RgSRIiEfeUU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">in this google document</a>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Don't mind my terminology: I was trying out some different words for the power types but you can trade them out with a simple find&gt;replace.<br /> <br /> Instead of &quot;Purviews&quot;, I used &quot;Sovereignties&quot;. Purviews makes me think of Scion; perhaps I am alone in that perception.<br /> <br /> Instead of &quot;Impositions&quot;, I used Mandates. It's such a good word and tied so well to Chinese dragons; it seemed a shame to discard it. The verb is still &quot;proclaim&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;Breath&quot; is &quot;Eupnea&quot; in the document. It is a medical term for &quot;A restful breath&quot; so I felt it was appropriate.<br /> <br /> &quot;Finder&quot; is &quot;Delver&quot; and &quot;Trickster&quot; is &quot;Grifter&quot;... call it a holdout from third phase. I think those terms suit the methods better but that's up to your editor.<br /> <br /> <br /> A few points to keep in mind:<ul><li>I've eliminated Resistant wounds (the ones marked with the registered trademark symbol) in exchange for giving the orobori a LOT more Health.<br /> .<ul><li>The Health bar is divided into three sections: Divine dots (from ablutions), Corporeal dots (from human traits), and Heart dots (Always 5).<br /> .<br /> Divine dots are the sum total of what is possible for a true form dragon. Players can safely mark and leave these dots due to a mechanic I've introduced.<br /> .<br /> Corporeal dots are protected by Divine dots AND Ablutions; there's a lot of Health keeping an oroboros alive. That said, jade directly damages the Corporeal meter, and this is the one that triggers the (effective) death state when it is filled.<br /> .<br /> The Heart meter is a backwash basin for overflow damage: overflow doesn't begin until the Heart meter pushes wounds away. That said, it's not safe to fill this meter much: at full lethal it starts trying to reject the Oroboros for a new owner and at full agg it is destroyed. Both these conditions trigger fossilization, which erases one health dot each day until death occurs (starting immediately), the Heart is reclaimed and consumed again or--if it was destroyed--a new Heart is obtained.<br /> .<br /> .</li> <li>Ablutions now serve as miniature Health meters. Any damage a dragon sustains blasts away her human 'flesh suit' to reveal divine traits: the character benefits from an ablution when it has damage under its dot. This also means disbanding and healing are the same action: the more severe the injury to manifest the ablution the longer it takes to hide when the fight is over.<br /> .</li> <li>Breath has been given a boost to how much health it can replenish. It removes three bashing wounds, two lethal wounds, or one aggravated wound. This is to compensate for how much health an oroboros actually has to heal to look human again.<br /> Because of the high demand for Breath/Eupnea, I HIGHLY recommend reincorporating the Asset system IN ADDITION to the current gorging mechanic. I was going to write about it in this document but decided that's content for chapter two. Still, here are my recommendations:<br /> .<br /> Eating something also restores Breath/Eupnea. The amount restored is based on the size of the food consumed (one to one), PLUS Resolve if the food was a living thing (Even if it's been cooked: eating a steak would give 3 Breath/Eupnea: 1 size + 2 Resolve from the cow), PLUS Potency if the food was supernatural (Eating a werewolf would usually give about 10 Breath/Eupnea: 6 size, 2 Resolve, 2 Primal Urge).<br /> .<br /> Eating something inedible adds its flammability to the Breath/Eupnea garnered: one meal should translate to one point of fuel so dividing calories by 250 for the fuel should tell you roughly how much additional Breath/Eupnea it grants.<br /> .<br /> Assets store a fixed amount of Breath/Eupnea based on their rating. They can even be merits. An Asset must be a tangible noun (Person/Place/Thing, NOT an idea). Spending a scene with an Asset replenishes its Breath/Eupnea. Food can partially replenish an Asset, but the most efficient way to do so is spending time with it.<br /> .<br /> .</li> </ul></li> <li>Degree of Divinity is gone. Ablutions are strong enough as is. Besides, with the new narrative the character doesn't really become more divine; they just hide it under a flesh suit like Edgar the Bug from Men in Black.<br /> .</li> <li>True Form now refers to having all ablutions manifest (and thus being vulnerable to damage against the health meter) and provides no additional benefit. Again, ablutions are strong enough.<br /> .</li> <li>I wrote ten Sovereignties with five Mandates each. They all are roughly independent, but it's okay to introduce Mandates which overlap--provided they overlap with Mandates of OTHER sovereignties.<br /> .<ul><li>A Sovereignty proclamation has INDEFINITE duration, and is only erased by losing all of its Sovereignty's Authority<br /> .</li> <li>A new proclamation overwrites an old one: only one proclamation is allowed per Sovereignty at a time. This is to keep the bookkeeping complexity of indefinite powers down.<br /> .</li> <li>The biggest component of this new setup is that proclamations can use multiple powers as a single command. Read the example proclamations to see how this is intended to be used.<br /> .</li> <li>Dice pools were significantly simplified: each Sovereignty only rolls its rating and Heartstring to activate.<br /> .</li> <li>I eliminated emotion-manipulating powers. While they seem interesting on the surface, it is better to encourage players to invoke emotions by manipulating the environment around a victim, rather than trigger emotions directly. This is why there are only ten sovereignties instead of your original sixteen.<br /> .</li> <li>Mechanic overlap is a big problem here, particularly because the mechanics need to be able to scale. Conditions might be a good way to get around this when making more Sovereignties/purviews. Alternatively, it might not be bad to let Mandates from separate Sovereignties achieve the same effect: it'd allow a combination of proclamations to break the hard 5-point limit these powers possess.</li> </ul></li> </ul>Okay. That's what I've got for you. I'm'a go draw more pictures now. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":610,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","user":"CJC","date":". 11-05-2016, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T05:45:03-07:00","id":998713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=998589#post998589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was kind of scattered with cliche, and I'm not really seeing an underlying theme or image you're going for, just a set of tropes that sound cool without alot of substance to tie them together. It's not bad for the villain of a single campaign, but it's not something I'd put in a book for players to use repeatedly for multiple scenarios.<br /> <br /> With the Bloody Chalice and Deep Ones, we do research into existing concepts while talking over what the most interesting and insightful twists and bombshells we can place into them are. We don't just bang them out over a short period. The Deep Ones document is taking so long because it legitimately takes time to craft a versatile scenario that is sensible, original, and intriguing.<br /> <br /> When we get into the Old Gods (and we will, because you're right that we need to), they'll be something with much more thought than the villain of a single campaign. But first, give us time to elaborate on the Deep Ones, the Nightmares, the Usurpers, and the Reptilian Conspiracies...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCan I have some advice on how to make their backstory less clich\u00e9?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-05-2016, 08:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T14:04:07-07:00","id":998883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=998713#post998713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bCan I have some advice on how to make their backstory less clich\u00e9?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, let's take a look at what you've got.<br /> <br /> <b>We'll start with the aesthetic.</b><br /> Your recruiters have taken on the appearance of the door-to-door salesman (or missionary... or in your case both). In such a profession the pleasant, well-kept visage is a means of delaying the slam of a door. After all, if they were shabby the person answering the door might assume they were pan-handling derelicts or--worse--criminals.<br /> You're playing this concept straight, but it sounds like you want to play up the creep-out factor with it. So let's play with it.<br /> <br /> You could defy this idea by making them actually appear shabby. Maybe people do mistake them for criminals, but the charm of their pitch overpowers the gut reaction of fear (which is why Sunstone is so successful).<br /> <br /> Alternatively, they could keep the clean-cut look by opening their pitch by posing as security contractors and then explain that real security comes from the acquisition of power: &quot;We'll teach you how to stand your ground&quot;.<br /> <br /> You could emphasize their instability by having them wear a particularly out-of-place article of clothing despite their &quot;suit and tie&quot; facade. Something pops to mind immediately: perhaps they wear ties made out of aluminum foil. They could even make this a conversation piece:<br /> &quot;Yeah, I used to be a tin-foil hat, but then Sunstone really showed me the way to go. I wear this tie to remind me where I was and keep me tuned to a bright future... instead of aliens *laughs*.&quot;<br /> <br /> You could turn into the skid by making them VERY creepy. For instance, maybe the recruiters always come in threes, and always stand in a triangle. They move and walk in this formation, blink in unison, and even perform the same gestures (if you hurt one of them, all three flinch). This is because they've actually be Drowned by a Deep One and are really one amorphous monstrosity: they've managed to scrape together some form of illusion to hide their hideous mass, but the magick is finnicky and requires multiple illusory bodies to hide the whole body.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>On to motives.</b><br /> First, I want to know more about this religion of yours that was the original body of the cult before Cottonwood took over. What was their goal in worship? What fears were they trying to allay or what changes were they trying to make to the world? Why was their faith so threatening that an Orobori den destroyed them? People turn to religion when they are suffering, and they choose what to worship based on how that suffering might be relieved or given purpose. Something about these gods gave the monks a reason to worship them: that reason could be a lie but we need to know what the lie might be before we can see the weight of the truth underneath it. Given the old gods are dreaming horrors, I doubt they pitched their goals straight.<br /> <br /> The concept of the twin gods bothers me primarily because one has a concept which is open to social interpretation (pleasure has the context to be a positive thing) while the other does not (nightmares are universally bad). I'd recommend making them BOTH gods of death and dreams: the first steals good dreams (with the cult believes are taken from the wicked and given to the devout) while the second eats bad dreams (thereby protecting the cult from the harm they can cause). Though the old gods both represent death, they give promise of consciousness eternal in the sea of dreams, floating blissfully on a gentle current at the eye of the storm, with non-believers dragged down into the swirling chaos. The cult also believes the twin gods will grant them the comfort of death in sleep: they have heard from their leader Cottonwood that the devout always die while dreaming and thus assume that death will be painless (spoiler alert: it's not).<br /> <br /> Now, what is the cult's goal on the corporeal plane? Clearly they seek to increase their number. Perhaps they are trying to collect minds under a single idea so that--once adrift in the Dreamtide--they can combine their strengths to build some sort of civilization on the other side of the Ora. Cottonwood may be promising this city will be a utopia but instead be planning to use it as a place to launch attacks against other Orobori, whom he despises. Keep in mind cults are scary when the goals sold to the bottom of the pyramid are little more than power machinations of the peak.<br /> What does Cottonwood personally seek to gain by fishing in the dreams of these two old gods? Is it oblivion for oblivion's sake? Does he hope to somehow steal their power? Maybe he (foolishly) believes he can execute them while they sleep and then fill the void of power which forms (not realizing that the oceanic plate at the bottom of the Dreamtide is comprised of the intertwined bodies of the old gods, and beneath it waits a boiling mantle of terrible energy which if released would obliterate the entire Dreamtide and sleep as the world understands it).<br /> <br /> <br /> I know that's a lot to chew on. Still, hopefully it gives you some ideas.<br /> Take what you need and make a write-up for your antagonist. Then put it into a team pitch for Raccoon.<br /> <br /> Stick with it, you're on the right track! ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T14:34:36-07:00","id":998890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/ma