to the Old Gods. Perhaps they could be a former dragon cult who worshipped a master that abused them horribly and after getting rid of them decided to worship the old gods thinking they would be better masters. Finally, do you mind Bill Cottonwood being a former televangelist who got his heart after surviving the attack on the monastery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-05-2016, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:15:10-07:00","id":998902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=998890#post998890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI like the ideas you came up with. If you don't mind I might use some of these. Also, I could describe the other members of the cult like counselors, who are basically the teachers of the cult's doctrine. Security, perhaps they could be paramilitary-like and I could describe the corporate side too. Also, I will try to think of a reason why the monks turned to the Old Gods. Perhaps they could be a former dragon cult who worshipped a master abused them horribly and after getting rid of them decided to worship the old gods thinking they would be better masters. Finally, do you mind Bill Cottonwood being a former televangelist who got his heart after surviving the attack on the monastery?</div> </div> </div> </div>I only meant security as a means of getting in the door. When you work as a door-to-door salesman you've got about 20 seconds to make a worthwhile pitch before you get shooed away. Offering to assess the security system of a property is a good way to get invited inside, and has actually been employed by criminals to determine if a property is worth burglarizing and what might be the best means of doing so.<br /> <br /> Cottonwood's history before taking possession of the cult doesn't bother me. The means through which he became an oroboros does, though.<br /> You say he acquired a Heart during the scuffle with the orobori Den. This is rough, though, for several reasons. First, killing a dragon is HARD, especially if you're not prepared. I'd be more inclined to believe one of the monks succeeded and Cottonwood stole the Heart. Second, many orobori do not carry their Hearts on their person. Cottonwood would be forced to track down their residence and then rip it apart to find the Heart. While it isn't impossible that a dragon had Heart in chest during the raid, considering the threat the monks posed it seems highly unlikely. Given your scenario he'd have to make a conscious decision to become an oroboros, so he'd need a really good reason to go down that rabbit hole. Perhaps seeing the power of the orobori firsthand filled him with greed and he intentionally sought a Heart so that he could grasp that power and have his revenge.<br /> Be careful, you're walking on unsteady ground with the &quot;Man goes to country, takes to their religion, and is immediately better at it than the lifelong practitioners&quot; storyline. Remember that Cottonwood is looking to profit at the expense of others: he took the surface traditions because they sound good and are easily marketable but his goals are not the same as the monks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Please feel free to use some or all of the ideas I've pitched: I came up with them to enhance your concept. Personally, what I'd use:<br /> &gt;Recruiters<br /> &gt;&gt;Tin Foil Ties.<br /> &gt;&gt;Offer to sell security.<br /> &gt;&gt;Convince the prospective new cultist that the only way to really SLEEP at night is to have power.<br /> &gt;&gt;Make a promise to give that power in exchange for a &quot;small&quot; favor.<br /> <br /> &gt;Monks<br /> &gt;&gt;Learned of those two particular old gods when their leader shared a nightmare with them during meditation.<br /> &gt;&gt;Believed the old gods were gods of dreams, with the promise one would bring them good dreams from the wicked and the other would take away their bad dreams.<br /> &gt;&gt;Believed that though the gods were gods of death, they would grant them a peaceful demise during sleep.<br /> &gt;&gt;Sought to awaken the dreaming gods so that their work could be done for the whole world (not understanding the consequences of this action)<br /> &gt;&gt;Were destroyed by an Orobori den who learned of that previous goal.<br /> <br /> &gt;Cottonwood<br /> &gt;&gt;Went to Nepal to do research for a new self-help book.<br /> &gt;&gt;Liked the promises the monks gave him about the old gods; joined to learn their secrets and sell them.<br /> &gt;&gt;Survived the Orobori attack through subterfuge. Craving the power, sought out a Heart and set out for his revenge.<br /> &gt;&gt;Recruits others by misusing the monk doctrine with promises of restful sleep. Builds a pyramid scheme of power intent on siphoning eldritch energy from the twin old gods, convincing the cultists they must share the doctrines so that all humanity can benefit from their rest.<br /> &gt;&gt;Seeks to build a fortification WITHIN the Dreamtide from whence he may launch attacks--his goal is to become the sole oroboros on Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:42:10-07:00","id":998917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=998902#post998902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I only meant security as a means of getting in the door. When you work as a door-to-door salesman you've got about 20 seconds to make a worthwhile pitch before you get shooed away. Offering to assess the security system of a property is a good way to get invited inside, and has actually been employed by criminals to determine if a property is worth burglarizing and what might be the best means of doing so.<br /> <br /> Cottonwood's history before taking possession of the cult doesn't bother me. The means through which he became an oroboros does, though.<br /> You say he acquired a Heart during the scuffle with the orobori Den. This is rough, though, for several reasons. First, killing a dragon is HARD, especially if you're not prepared. I'd be more inclined to believe one of the monks succeeded and Cottonwood stole the Heart. Second, many orobori do not carry their Hearts on their person. Cottonwood would be forced to track down their residence and then rip it apart to find the Heart. While it isn't impossible that a dragon had Heart in chest during the raid, considering the threat the monks posed it seems highly unlikely. Given your scenario he'd have to make a conscious decision to become an oroboros, so he'd need a really good reason to go down that rabbit hole. Perhaps seeing the power of the orobori firsthand filled him with greed and he intentionally sought a Heart so that he could grasp that power and have his revenge.<br /> Be careful, you're walking on unsteady ground with the &quot;Man goes to country, takes to their religion, and is immediately better at it than the lifelong practitioners&quot; storyline. Remember that Cottonwood is looking to profit at the expense of others: he took the surface traditions because they sound good and are easily marketable but his goals are not the same as the monks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Please feel free to use some or all of the ideas I've pitched: I came up with them to enhance your concept. Personally, what I'd use:<br /> &gt;Recruiters<br /> &gt;&gt;Tin Foil Ties.<br /> &gt;&gt;Offer to sell security.<br /> &gt;&gt;Convince the prospective new cultist that the only way to really SLEEP at night is to have power.<br /> &gt;&gt;Make a promise to give that power in exchange for a &quot;small&quot; favor.<br /> <br /> &gt;Monks<br /> &gt;&gt;Learned of those two particular old gods when their leader shared a nightmare with them during meditation.<br /> &gt;&gt;Believed the old gods were gods of dreams, with the promise one would bring them good dreams from the wicked and the other would take away their bad dreams.<br /> &gt;&gt;Believed that though the gods were gods of death, they would grant them a peaceful demise during sleep.<br /> &gt;&gt;Sought to awaken the dreaming gods so that their work could be done for the whole world (not understanding the consequences of this action)<br /> &gt;&gt;Were destroyed by an Orobori den who learned of that previous goal.<br /> <br /> &gt;Cottonwood<br /> &gt;&gt;Went to Nepal to do research for a new self-help book.<br /> &gt;&gt;Liked the promises the monks gave him about the old gods; joined to learn their secrets and sell them.<br /> &gt;&gt;Survived the Orobori attack through subterfuge. Craving the power, sought out a Heart and set out for his revenge.<br /> &gt;&gt;Recruits others by misusing the monk doctrine with promises of restful sleep. Builds a pyramid scheme of power intent on siphoning eldritch energy from the twin old gods, convincing the cultists they must share the doctrines so that all humanity can benefit from their rest.<br /> &gt;&gt;Seeks to build a fortification WITHIN the Dreamtide from whence he may launch attacks--his goal is to become the sole oroboros on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI like the outline for the monks, recruiters and Cottonwood himself. Also, I was thinking of making Cottonwood before his change a con-man who was pretending to be a televangelist to syphon money out of unsuspecting victims. By security, I meant a branch of the cult that protects VIPS and the cult's international assets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-06-2016, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:03:52-08:00","id":999281,"title":"","content":"CJC, you have great ideas and are certainly experienced, but you realize we've written about 50 pages of research, math, brainstorming, refining, and internal coordination since our last release, right? A chunk of what you've addressed here isn't even on the table anymore. We went through your post and talked about some of the stuff, and I guess we can refer back to the document when we're finalizing some of those things, but there's so much work you're not aware of going on. This is why I keep asking you to join the Skype group... :\\<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=998623#post998623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you're fleshing out antagonists and setting</div> </div> </div> </div>We're building the drafts of the chapters for the final book, actually. The antagonist documents are rough-drafts of sections of the antagonist chapter. Chapter 2, which has the finalized Method/Philosophy rules, is coming out as soon as we buckle down and finish it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17xSWyoBgfa9ZULDXczUTn6DLEF2rJ4z-RgSRIiEfeUU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">in this google document</a> </div> </div> </div>Stuff like this takes a whole meeting to go through, and we're barely pushing progress as is, so one of us will look at it, but we're not going to sit down with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Purviews makes me think of Scion </div> </div> </div>That is the intention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead of &quot;Impositions&quot;, I used Mandates. </div> </div> </div>We're kicking around a few terms with this one...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Breath&quot; is &quot;Eupnea&quot; </div> </div> </div>&quot;Breath&quot; works though. &quot;Eupnea&quot; doesn't sound like a word that fits in with the rest of the book...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Finder&quot; is &quot;Delver&quot; and &quot;Trickster&quot; is &quot;Grifter&quot;... call it a holdout from third phase. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Finder&quot; could be changed, but it needs to reflect their approach.<br /> &quot;Trickster&quot; is a common term from mythology, and it'd be a hard thing to change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any damage a dragon sustains blasts away her human 'flesh suit' to reveal divine traits: the character benefits from an ablution when it has damage under its dot. </div> </div> </div>This WOULD be a good idea for what we put down for fire damage, except that most ablutions are specific body parts, so we have to treat it based on WHERE it's done, not which dot it's to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Breath has been given a boost to how much health it can replenish. </div> </div> </div>This is one of your changes which, to implement all of them, would require an overhaul to the entire mathematical structure of a nearly-complete game. I'd rather just finish than start from square one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Degree of Divinity is gone. </div> </div> </div>We've looked at about 10 different ways to alter this mechanic already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True Form now refers to having all ablutions manifest </div> </div> </div>That's what it always meant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wrote ten Sovereignties with five Mandates each. </div> </div> </div>We'll have to see how they look next to our (as of yet, incomplete) notes on what to do with this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I eliminated emotion-manipulating powers. </div> </div> </div>This was unanimously voted against by the team. None of us want to remove them, as far as I know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 11-06-2016, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:18:43-08:00","id":999291,"title":"","content":"I will try to post the first draft of my antagonist soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T12:00:34-08:00","id":999359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=999281#post999281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're building the drafts of the chapters for the final book, actually. The antagonist documents are rough-drafts of sections of the antagonist chapter. Chapter 2, which has the finalized Method/Philosophy rules, is coming out as soon as we buckle down and finish it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not transparently apparent in your updates to the community nor is it mentioned in your first post. Conflicting suggests occur when you do not have a transparent development process.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=999281#post999281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what it always meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope! True Form from second edition (which was your primary draw) increased all attributes by 1.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=999281#post999281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This WOULD be a good idea for what we put down for fire damage, except that most ablutions are specific body parts, so we have to treat it based on WHERE it's done, not which dot it's to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a heads up: abstracting Health is as helpful to a system like Chronicles of Darkness as the abstraction of currency is. If you get bogged down in where damage is inflicted the game will require too much bookkeeping on the character sheet. Ablutions are already tedious to track.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=999281#post999281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff like this takes a whole meeting to go through, and we're barely pushing progress as is, so one of us will look at it, but we're not going to sit down with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, don't bother. I had a question bothering me and your response answers it concisely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc","name":"CJC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar610_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T12:08:22-08:00","id":999365,"title":"","content":"Hey CJ, can I pm you some fiction involving the interaction between a Sunstone Recruiter and a random person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T11:09:00-08:00","id":1000345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CJC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=999359#post999359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not transparently apparent in your updates to the community nor is it mentioned in your first post. Conflicting suggests occur when you do not have a transparent development process.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I need to update that. On the flip side, it'd be a real time-sink to keep a solid record of everything that we're doing at all times. I know it makes it harder for people outside the project to figure out what's going on, but I have to choose what to spend time on, and there's really not alot of it within the team, so stuff like that is pushed aside. People who want to get involved can join the team.<br /> <br /> I am a firm believer, however, that we can get more content made, better and faster, if we work as a close-knit team which discusses new ideas and carefully reviews the material as we write, rather than a single person or two trying to compile hundreds of disjointed forum posts. Also, because that method's already been used, I feel it has diminishing returns. That's why I'm doing it this way. Anyone can join in if they want to, but I'd rather juggle a pile of crafted notes and details than try to crowdsource a whole book...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T01:18:46-08:00","id":1008854,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Status Update from the latest meeting...</b></span></span><br /> We are currently pushing to finish and release a document with the new Purview setup in a week or two, complete with mechanics and a list of 14 purviews. This is because it's been pointed out that the Purviews are required for character creation, and the last release was nigh unworkable. The document will contain the following...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>General Mechanics</b><br /> Purviews have been pegged to being similar to Werewolf Gifts, and more potent versions whatever the equivalent spell in Mage 2E is. (the term &quot;Mini Arcana&quot; has been used) Impositions are basically small, specific miracles, which are extremely useful in their specific situations. Purviews are also written from a generally virtuous angle, but one that can easily be abused, even Hippocratic. The exception is Apathy, which is written from a generally malevolent (actually, more apathetic) angle, but can be used for good if carefully applied.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Each Purview confers 5 Impositions, a power to sense a specific thing, an amplifying condition, and a drawback for having them.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Apathy is the exception, with 8 Impositions: one to counter each Philosophy and an aura of what is basically Disquiet.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">All impositions can now be used once the first dot is purchased, and can be trained for 1 experience point.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Dice Pools for an Imposition no longer have attributes, and use the following math. We'd been kicking this around for a while, and CJC's latest suggestion-dump sealed it.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Untrained = Purview + Heartstring</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Trained += Skill</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Amplified += 1 to 3</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Impositions take 1 turn of concentration to invoke, cost 1 breath (unless the roll is an exceptional success), and the number used is limited only by Breath and time.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Impositions generally only target 1 thing at a time, and generally last 1 day. A point of willpower can be spent each day to extend this, and a dot can be used to make them indefinite.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Certain conditions work as Amplifiers, which add to the rolls, and sometimes have other effects.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Example 1: Hippocratic's range is &quot;within 10 feet and in sight&quot;, while the amplifier is &quot;laying on hands&quot;. Brushing against is +1, putting a hand on them through clothing is +2, and putting the bare hand on bare flesh is +3.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Example 2: Oath's amplifier is a written contract: a clear contract with the target's signature can be used to enforce the oath, adding a +2 to rolls, +3 if signed in the target's blood. On top of that, as long as this physical contract exists, the Oroboros does not need to spend willpower for the Oath to be in effect longer.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Each Purview has it's own drawback, which prevents the Oroboros from working against what they now embody.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">For example, Polygraph gives a penalty to lying for every point the Oroboros has. (or something like that, we're still doing math)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Apathy has the most potent drawbacks, which we're still working on.</span></span></li> </ul></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Each philosophy has 3 Purviews, one signature, 2 shared with at least one other. This will likely increase to 4-per by the time Chapter 3 is released.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Purview List by Philosophy</b><br /> These have all been re-written, and will have full entries in the doc.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Ash</b> - Ruin, Assembly, Agriculture (AKA Wood)</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Blood</b> - Oath, Justice, Polygraph</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Sweat</b> - Industry, Property, Agriculture</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Bone</b> - Hippocratic, Assembly, Agriculture</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Tears</b> - Passion, Assembly, Trance</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Tome</b> - Knowledge, Polygraph, Trance</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Coin</b> - Currency, Justice, Property</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Void</b> - Apathy</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">We plan to put Metal and Husbandry back in, among other things, eventually, but we don't want to take the time on that yet, with how long we've been taking with the Ablution and Purview stuff.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hCA8HofWsxc\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Finally, we leave you with this meeting's music...</b></span></a></span></span><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hCA8HofWsxc\" data-code=\"hCA8HofWsxc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/hCA8HofWsxc/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 02-23-2017, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T12:33:36-07:00","id":1108877,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">U dont know what's really happening.<br /> This is what's really happening.<br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/41/Red_Dress_Programmes_by_Neil_Hague.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Wake up sheeple.</span></span></b></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T13:13:12-07:00","id":1108901,"title":"","content":"IT LIVES!<br /> <br /> Kind of weirdly, but IT LIVES!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T15:03:37-07:00","id":1108960,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we've just been quietly trucking away over Skype and Google Drive. Nova brought up that David Icke makes him think of the Dominion last time I saw him, so we were talking about him in the meeting yesterday. I figured I should make a post after seeing that this thread had fallen to the second page. Aside from that... Expect some sort of release real soon, either for the Purviews or Deep Ones, or maybe a Chapter... We have about 80% of the first 5 chapters drafted at this point...<br /> <br /> I'm putting Mister Feral in charge of the next update post, because I think he's more popular than me, so we'll see when he gets to that...<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Just to be clear, <b>we can still take on new members at this point</b>, but we're getting to the point where we'll be working on the final book soon, so it's better to join now than later if anyone is on the fence. Any new blood helps, even if it's just someone who wants to talk about ideas...<br /> <br /> AJ, that includes you, if you want to come back to join us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 06-28-2017, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T16:11:36-07:00","id":1109002,"title":"","content":"How the Reimagining works<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/-c2V8qIvGgQ?t=35s\" data-code=\"-c2V8qIvGgQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-c2V8qIvGgQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> People... People try to say it's not... That it ain't like it is... but it do. It do be like it do, not like what aint be do done dum dum...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T21:17:51-07:00","id":1110459,"title":"","content":"So... Is Shock like... Dead? I haven't been able to contact him in a few months...<br /> <br /> Anyone have his number or anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-02-2017, 01:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T21:41:07-07:00","id":1111151,"title":"","content":"I am alive.<br /> <br /> Just had to deal with two suicides (one distant, one semi-close) on the same side of the family along with a unplanned move over to a new place.<br /> <br /> So things have been a bit... rattled over the last few months. I apologize if I have fallen off the radar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T01:29:43-07:00","id":1111189,"title":"","content":"Wow, that's terrible and I'm sorry to hear that. It's fine if you need to take time to yourself, you're under no obligation to keep in contact with me, I was just a little concerned that Skype and the Forum said you hadn't been on in a few months...<br /> <br /> If you want to talk, you know my contact info... :\\","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T15:12:54-07:00","id":1112369,"title":"","content":"Wasn't expecting this to come back. Also, I would like to apologize for my unprofessional behavior when I pitched my idea. I think my writing skills have improved since the last time I was here and I would like to post a new idea here, effectively scrapping the cult idea for a idea I think is somewhat better. And, if you want me too, I will fill out a application.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T16:10:06-07:00","id":1112396,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Updates from most recent meetings</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Hello everyone! Sorry it has been so long since a substantive update. We have had some difficulties, but mostly our work has gone without substantive updates. To keep things consistent, work on any one section needs to be in line with the others, so as we make progress on any given section we get closer to finalizing the book as a whole. That being the case, we have taken some important steps.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Previews coming soon</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Within the next month or so, we plan to have a first draft of a chapter for you to see, from the first section dedicated to player knowledge</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Over the next few months we plan on slow releases of the first 5 chapters, which will total the information that players need to play the game</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">As to the rest</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">We are finalizing the antagonists which we have been hinting at for a while, and very confident that they will be welcome additions to the World of Darkness.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Conspiracies among the draconic factions are also getting nice. Among their features are special bonuses that characters will receive for membership</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Ablutions are nearly finalized, and the purview lists are coming along as well. These are the last few stumbling blocks as far as mechanics go. From there, we need to tighten up and complete the writing.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">We appreciate your patience everyone, and we want to reward it. We all have day jobs, but it is extremely rewarding to see how this is coming together. We hope that when the time does come you will help us share this project and give us your thoughts, to make it everything that it can be.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Finally, we leave you with this meeting's music...</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=urglg3WimHA\" data-code=\"urglg3WimHA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/urglg3WimHA/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T16:10:50-07:00","id":1112397,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#800000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">[Accidentally double posted. Deleted second version]</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T00:00:06-07:00","id":1112532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1112369#post1112369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't expecting this to come back.</div> </div> </div> </div>We never left, it's just that no one was keeping up with updating the thread: we've been busy both inside and outside of the project.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I would like to apologize for my unprofessional behavior when I pitched my idea. </div> </div> </div>No need to apologize: It's absolutely fine, and I don't mean to discourage people from throwing down a couple ideas here. As long as they don't make several-page writeups which take an hour to parse through, I try to understand them and bring them up in meetings. Hell, even CJC's 20 page version of chapter 3 wasn't that bad, it was just really inconvenient to try and actually merge those ideas in.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I wasn't even bothered by the way you wrote it, or even annoyed by anything you did, I just didn't see how it actually fit within what we were writing: the Old Gods are written as this obscure boogeyman which isn't really active. After some thought, a cult trying to wake them up would be a perfectly valid thing to write into the book, but not as a major force in the world. I wasn't entirely sure you understood how things fit together though, and it didn't seem like you were really interested in figuring that out, though, to be very fair, I don't think the information we've released on that stuff, or even in the notes we haven't released, is thick enough to really talk about them.<br /> <br /> There also wasn't alot that was really unique about smiling people in suits. Now, if you had them doing some sort of Thetan-Reading-like thing as part of a massive dream-sorcery ritual and infiltrating the government, and had them throwing down symbolism of waking some ancient divinities sleeping within volcanoes deep beneath the sea to overthrow some sort of interdimensional tyrants like Xenu (yeah, Scientology references abound, but they'd get whittled into vagueness by the time it was fully developed), that sort of thing could be really interesting, and would certainly fit in with the material inspired by Crowley's ultranatural beings, David Icke's interdimensional reptilians, and other weird conspiracy theories about massive conspiracies running the government.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think my writing skills have improved since the last time I was here </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm definitely seeing a marked improvement. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would like to post a new idea here, effectively scrapping the cult idea for a idea I think is somewhat better. </div> </div> </div>Go ahead, we're probably going to have an Old God cult as a minor threat at some point in there, and we're pretty open for new material as long as it doesn't mess with existing concepts...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, if you want me too, I will fill out a application. </div> </div> </div>Go ahead: everyone who wants to be a major part of writing this should just fill out an application. I only have that process in place to make sure you can write with some restraint, so I don't have to worry about you accidentally messing up some formatting in a document, and I only bother keeping a specific team because I don't want to manage a chunk of the forum posting disconnected and contradictory (though often very interesting) ideas at me while I struggle to fit them all into a single book alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T07:37:19-07:00","id":1112668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1112532#post1112532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We never left, it's just that no one was keeping up with updating the thread: we've been busy both inside and outside of the project.<br /> <br /> <br /> No need to apologize: It's absolutely fine, and I don't mean to discourage people from throwing down a couple ideas here. As long as they don't make several-page writeups which take an hour to parse through, I try to understand them and bring them up in meetings. Hell, even CJC's 20 page version of chapter 3 wasn't that bad, it was just really inconvenient to try and actually merge those ideas in.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I wasn't even bothered by the way you wrote it, or even annoyed by anything you did, I just didn't see how it actually fit within what we were writing: the Old Gods are written as this obscure boogeyman which isn't really active. After some thought, a cult trying to wake them up would be a perfectly valid thing to write into the book, but not as a major force in the world. I wasn't entirely sure you understood how things fit together though, and it didn't seem like you were really interested in figuring that out, though, to be very fair, I don't think the information we've released on that stuff, or even in the notes we haven't released, is thick enough to really talk about them.<br /> <br /> There also wasn't alot that was really unique about smiling people in suits. Now, if you had them doing some sort of Thetan-Reading-like thing as part of a massive dream-sorcery ritual and infiltrating the government, and had them throwing down symbolism of waking some ancient divinities sleeping within volcanoes deep beneath the sea to overthrow some sort of interdimensional tyrants like Xenu (yeah, Scientology references abound, but they'd get whittled into vagueness by the time it was fully developed), that sort of thing could be really interesting, and would certainly fit in with the material inspired by Crowley's ultranatural beings, David Icke's interdimensional reptilians, and other weird conspiracy theories about massive conspiracies running the government.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm definitely seeing a marked improvement. :3<br /> <br /> <br /> Go ahead, we're probably going to have an Old God cult as a minor threat at some point in there, and we're pretty open for new material as long as it doesn't mess with existing concepts...<br /> <br /> <br /> Go ahead: everyone who wants to be a major part of writing this should just fill out an application. I only have that process in place to make sure you can write with some restraint, so I don't have to worry about you accidentally messing up some formatting in a document, and I only bother keeping a specific team because I don't want to manage a chunk of the forum posting disconnected and contradictory (though often very interesting) ideas at me while I struggle to fit them all into a single book alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks man. My basic concept so far is a pharmacutical company called Crescent. They have recently developed a drug that was meant to cure insomnia but ended up with a odd side-affect in certain people. This side affect was that it plunged the person's subconscious into the Dreamtide. The company soon figures out that this mysterious new plane can access people's dreams. So, kinda like Freddy Kruger, the company starts to send agents into the dreams of executives of rival companies and tries to drive them incurably insane through horrific nightmares. Meanwhile, their scientists are trying to study the Dreamtide and figure out how it could possibly exist while trying to develop more potent versions of the medication to widen the amount of agents they could have in the Dreamtide. The company is unaware that the Dreamtide is populated by creatures that won't exactly be welcoming of them. Could this work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 07-07-2017, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T16:42:02-07:00","id":1112986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1112668#post1112668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks man. My basic concept so far is a pharmacutical company called Crescent. They have recently developed a drug that was meant to cure insomnia but ended up with a odd side-affect in certain people. This side affect was that it plunged the person's subconscious into the Dreamtide. The company soon figures out that this mysterious new plane can access people's dreams. So, kinda like Freddy Kruger, the company starts to send agents into the dreams of executives of rival companies and tries to drive them incurably insane through horrific nightmares. Meanwhile, their scientists are trying to study the Dreamtide and figure out how it could possibly exist while trying to develop more potent versions of the medication to widen the amount of agents they could have in the Dreamtide. The company is unaware that the Dreamtide is populated by creatures that won't exactly be welcoming of them. Could this work?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of a drug which causes people i screw with the dreamtide would work well with the Dream Sorcery stuff, same with the idea of something like Cherion Group meddling with the dreamtide. The idea reminds me a little of Freddy vs Jason. I can picture the Naga and the Deep Ones getting pissed when they find out too...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-07-2017, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T17:52:05-07:00","id":1113010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1112986#post1112986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea of a drug which causes people i screw with the dreamtide would work well with the Dream Sorcery stuff, same with the idea of something like Cherion Group meddling with the dreamtide. The idea reminds me a little of Freddy vs Jason. I can picture the Naga and the Deep Ones getting pissed when they find out too...</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what the Deep Ones are but what exactly are the Naga? I am wondering how the Knights and the Ororboroi would react to them. Also, i might write up the company's backstory soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T18:54:00-07:00","id":1113044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1113010#post1113010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know what the Deep Ones are but what exactly are the Naga? I am wondering how the Knights and the Ororboroi would react to them. Also, i might write up the company's backstory soon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Er yeah, they're a Reptilian Conspiracy-our z-splats, cabals of culturally themed Oroboroi that pool their power for ideological reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T19:30:12-07:00","id":1113058,"title":"","content":"Here, let me finish their entry in Chapter 2 and I'll post it...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T19:31:56-07:00","id":1113060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1113058#post1113058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here, let me finish their entry in Chapter 2 and I'll post it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks buddy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T20:08:49-07:00","id":1113071,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b><b><span style=\"color:#980000\">Reptilian Conspiracies -</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#980000\">Structures of Power</span></b></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">If an Oroboros defines their approach by their Method, and their belief by their philosophy, how do they define their interaction with the world at large? Often, Oroboroi who have come into their own will end up joining Reptilian Conspiracies, large networks of Oroboroi which work to influence the world on a global scale. Of these, five are truly major players on the world stage. In chronological order of their formation, they are:</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><b><span style=\"color:#980000\">The Dominion</span></b></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The oldest conspiracy in history, the Dominion traces its structure back to the Dragons themselves. Their goal is simple: to impose order upon humanity as the Dragons once did. The Dominion is known for being cold, calculating, and ruthless in its goal to control the world governments, and its leaders often see all other ends as futile: a world without the Dominion is a world in chaos. Individual Dominionists range from bright eyed young drakes looking to make a positive impact in the world, to corrupt power-mongers looking to lord over humanity with an iron talon... </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><b><span style=\"color:#980000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The Collapsers</span></span></b></b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ever since the final days of the Dominion, the Collapsers have been a thorn in the side of anyone who wants to control large groups of people. Despite not having the structure for any real historical records, they claim to trace their ideological roots back to the first Oroboroi who caused the collapse. The Collapsers are a network of libertines, minarchists, and outright anarchists who form cells of rebellion, and work tirelessly prevent hegemonies like the Dominion from forming again, no matter who\u2019s in charge. In the eyes of a Collapser, it is better to struggle in chaos than to live under the tyranny of another\u2019s will...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><b><span style=\"color:#980000\">The Naga</span></b></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Founded by an oroboros named Kadru in the chaos after the collapse, the Naga are as mystical and mysterious as they are ancient. The exact goals and workings of their leadership are shrouded in mystery, but their stated goal is to return the harmony between the Dreamtide and the Waking which was lost as the Dominion fell apart. They believe that, if they can bring peace to the World of Darkness, that they can end the cycle of violence which plagues it on all levels. How they go about this is a matter of debate however, as the machinations are often complex and magical, and sometimes involve violence without much explanation other than \u201cit was what the cycle needed.\u201d Naga leaders tend to be mystics, sorcerers, and spiritualists, but will welcome any being who wishes to bring peace to the cycle, and even count non-Oroboroi among their ranks...</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><b><span style=\"color:#980000\">The Order of St George</span></b></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Order of St. George is unique in many ways. For one, the most famous deed of their titular founder, a Roman Legionary of the pre-catholic era, who became an Oroboroi after slaying a mad plaguebearing dragon at the behest of his remorseful peer. This founding act has echoed throughout their history; the Order is a conspiracy of draconic dragonslayers, dedicated to protecting the world from the excesses of their kin, in particular Religious institutions who would be perverted into mockeries by literal Serpents of Eden. While they are the least numerous conspiracy, they more than make up for their low numbers in both zeal and their connections to the human world; the ideal Oroboroi of St. George is a general who leads from the front, eager to suffer and die for the sake of her men and her cause, accepting any personal loss to see that justice is done. Their membership ranges from young warriors filled with idealistic fervor to guilt-ridden ancients who have seen and done too much to do anything but atone. They will save the world, or die trying-and there is few more unpredictable things than a would-be hero with godlike powers...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><b><span style=\"color:#980000\">The Delvers</span></b></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">It\u2019s hard to say when the group now known as the Delvers first formed, as they have records of groups meeting to discuss science and philosophy dating back to ancient Greece, and a structure dating back to record-keepers in the fall of the Roman Empire, but the group didn\u2019t rise to prominence until the mass-discovery of the ancient records of the Dragons during the Renaissance. Soon after that though, the Delver\u2019s discoveries lead them to become a player on par with the other 4 conspiracies, and today they are an occult information network which spans the globe. The Delvers have been known to consort with many otherworldly beings, including Fae, Mages, Spirits, and <i>especially</i> the Deep Ones, and believe that only through knowledge can they achieve their many goals. They have a sort of hierarchy system, in which new initiates must prove themselves to be taught the secrets which the higher members know, and considering who their leaders are talking to...</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-07-2017, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T22:18:18-07:00","id":1113113,"title":"","content":"That is a pretty interesting chapter Raccon. I can most defiantly see the Naga and Dominion being pissed with Crescent I wonder how the Knights of the Bloody Chalice would view them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T05:55:57-07:00","id":1113201,"title":"","content":"I see a few possible responses from the Knights. They could ignore Crescent, which after all is not directly related to their hunt in any substantial way. They could view Crescent as a threat to its limited control over dream sorcery. They may see a potential ally with resources to help them in their hunt, which could be genuine or via manipulation. Either not allowing Crescent to know they exist but learning their secrets from within to make it easier to locate targets or providing them with false information about the nature of dreams so that they can use Crescent to gain a foothold while using the company's resources to expand their own abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T14:14:07-07:00","id":1113369,"title":"","content":"Keeping in mind, only the Barons would really be worried about that. I think individual Knights would tend to not know about broad conspiracy stuff, because they are loners in isolation mostly concerned with their own affairs, and the Old Gods are an obscure threat...<br /> <br /> You guys keep talking about the Old Gods here, and I should point out, they aren't even mentioned untill chapter 5, and even then it's written as a rumour which may just be the Delvers lying to scare others away from Pandemonium. They're not on everyone's mind, and we've talked about the Dominion and/or Collapsers outright denying their existence...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-08-2017, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T14:20:12-07:00","id":1113373,"title":"","content":"Those are pretty good assumptions Feral. Crescent's agents often appear in the Dreamtide wearing suits and ties and are nicknamed The Suits by both Oroboroi and their victims. Their appearances have lead to them being referred to as urban legends where if you do a certain act before bed, they appear and give horrific nightmares and haunt you for the rest of your life. Crescent's scientists either go into the Dreamtide with the Suits or study whatever the Suits bring back from that plane. Now, I got to determine what the hell is in the medication that plunges people into the Dreamtide in the first place.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 07-08-2017, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T14:49:57-07:00","id":1113392,"title":"","content":"Some sort of sleeping pill that gives you vivid dreams and loosens your supernatural blocks so you can dreamwalk, I'd guess... That sort of detail isn't important.<br /> <br /> When developing a new group, or any sort of content for one of these, you need to have multiple things in mind that you think over.<br /> <br /> On top of anything else, you need to be thinking of it from a meta perspective: how is the Storyteller going to use this? What power level and kind of threat should you make these guys? Do they have a special mechanic? Do they have a special plot meaning? Why would the players find this group interesting to interact with? World building isn't just a creative outlet for the writer. It's a tool for the Storyteller, which gives them things to flesh out the game world with and use on the player without having to develop a setting from scratch. Just to be clear, these guys don't sound like they'd make a good universal villain to me.<br /> <br /> Before you write about their activities, you have to figure out their motivations in detail, then move to their resources and internal structure/culture. Those are the most important details, because everything else about their operations is going to be supported by that.<br /> <br /> What EXACTLY are they interested in and why? What do they think they will find and what lengths are they willing to go through for it? What underlying motivations do they have and why do they have these? Why would a real person be part of this group? Give them some logical explanations so you have some ideas to base their actions on before you start writing the other stuff, then think of what fits.<br /> <br /> Finally, you need to also think about how they fit into the rest of the book. Pretty much everything in there so far connects with everything else. We have a set of underlying references to things like Nietsche and David Icke that give the book a consistent theme and concept. How does this fit?<br /> <br /> Start with that, not a series of tropes and disconnected ideas. That's how you write a solid part of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T22:01:32-07:00","id":1114053,"title":"","content":"So gathered my thoughts and retooled a skeleton framework on turning the philosophies into &quot;motivational&quot; archetypes.<br /> <br /> The four that I have worked on are Sweat, Ash, Bone, and Blood. They exist as the follow:<br /> <br /> Sweat - Now known as the Unconquered. They have the short term goals known as Breakthroughs with their long term goal called the Magnum Opus.<br /> <br /> Bone - Now known as Avatars. They have the short term goals known as Revelations with their long term goal called The Trial.<br /> <br /> Ash - Now known as the Catalysts. They have two categories of short term goals: Those being crucibles and forges. They have the long term goal known as Synthesis (Synthesis is not earned until both Crucibles and Forges have been completed)<br /> <br /> Blood - Now known as the Immutable (Working title, feel free to suggest another). They have the short term goal of Pledges (working title.) with the long term goal being Final Testament (working title).<br /> <br /> Completion of short term goals give you a point of breath per dot of furnace.<br /> <br /> Completion of long term goals fills your breath track and gives you a dot of furnace free of charge (Because you already spent entire chronicle to get it)<br /> <br /> &quot;But what do dragons do?&quot; answer.<br /> <br /> Unconquered: To bring my desires forth. To make the covert vulgar. To the imagined into the real.<br /> Catalysts: To destroy a corrupt system and replace it with a better one.<br /> Immutable: To live the truth in all things.<br /> Bone: to be the God we are born to be.<br /> <br /> Passive abilities gained upon joining. No point of breath needed to activate. They can only be activated once every 30 days. Possibility OP. Do I care? No. Reason? They're fucking dragons. Let's get started.<br /> <br /> Catalysts: Auto successes on one roll equal to furnace when damaging a person, place, or thing, that is the subject of his Crucible and/or attempting to renew a person place or thing the target of his Forge.<br /> <br /> Avatars: Remove damage (Any) on a one to one basis on any supernatural being within line of sight per dot of furnace or complete wipe the damage track clean of mortals with in her line of sight up her dots in furnace. (example: three mortals get turn apart by angry tribbles and suffer Agg. Dragon has three dots of furnace, activates ability, they are good as new).<br /> <br /> Unconquered: Gain extra willpower dots equal to furnace. They function as normal and the will power dots can be spent per usual. Will power dots committed in this fashion return at the end of 30 days. No exp needed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The following is a work in progress:<br /> Immutable: each active Pledge gives the dragon two extra attributes. They may have as many pledges up to their dots in furnace. Pledges completed count as short term goals.<br /> <br /> Draconic pledges akin to the Adamantine Arrow Oaths (AA book. Page 62-66). Meaning they work off the spirit of the oath rather than the letter and as such, focuses on metaphorical intent rather than literal action. For one of the Immutable to state that they will be with someone in their darkest hour does not mean hiding out in their closet, disabling their light and locking them inside for an hour as a Changeling pledge may fulfill but rather sending physical, emotional, and/or financial support when they are most in need.<br /> <br /> Also such pledges can not be forced. Such coercion when the soul is not with the words fails to activate the ability. Both parties must pledge of their own free will with the full intent of fulfilling the pledge.<br /> <br /> Any attempt to ensnare the Immutable through unwilling and unwitting pacts or pledges through supernatural abilities fail outright. Old hearts beat within them and will not be conquered so easily.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 07-10-2017, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T14:49:00-07:00","id":1114287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1114053#post1114053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any attempt to ensnare the Immutable through unwilling and unwitting pacts or pledges through supernatural abilities fail outright. Old hearts beat within them and will not be conquered so easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe make it a Clash of Wills? Dragons may be ancient, but Mages, Demons and Changelings are all pretty good at deal-related fuckery at high levels. You're bringing an ancient serpent-god into conflict with either a gnostic wonder-worker of godlike potential, a super-liar with root access to reality, or a being warped to the edge of humanity by the metaphysical force of fate and narrative itself. It's hard to say who exactly would win in such a face-off. Or, <i>fate</i>-off? <sup>I'll see myself out.</sup>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T18:50:23-07:00","id":1114355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1114287#post1114287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe make it a Clash of Wills? Dragons may be ancient, but Mages, Demons and Changelings are all pretty good at deal-related fuckery at high levels. You're bringing an ancient serpent-god into conflict with either a gnostic wonder-worker of godlike potential, a super-liar with root access to reality, or a being warped to the edge of humanity by the metaphysical force of fate and narrative itself. It's hard to say who exactly would win in such a face-off. Or, <i>fate</i>-off? <sup>I'll see myself out.</sup></div> </div> </div> </div>That was my first thought when dealing with stated ability. Problem is that it runs into two issues.<br /> <br /> The first is theme.<br /> <br /> The Immutable as a archetype gather power from power of their bonds and the truth of their lives. While other archetypes play with the idea of truth to power, The Immutable is the one that hammers home the ideal of it the most. They embody concepts (and more importantly, meaning) that can be socially distorted, circumvented, covered, and even suspended for a time but like gravity, will continue to exist, undamaged and unmoved. When the universe comes crashing down and reveals to them their insignificance, they respond with their existence. When it asks &quot;What is Truth?&quot;, they respond with their lives of fire and meaning.<br /> <br /> Now granted, this maybe overkill to how the Blood was portrayed but meh.<br /> <br /> idle thought: The way things are looking, this might as well be Dragon: The Existential Crisis<br /> <br /> Now this is all fine and dandy but what does this mean?<br /> <br /> It means the Immutable strengths are not in offensive power but rather their ability to remain truthful (and honorable) in a world that laughs at the concept and while they're pledges are somewhat weaker to the other archetypes (extra willpower, free healing, auto successes), they gain innate ability have all promises in relation to them become Pledges and thus are judged on spirit of the law vs the letter (which is powerful in it's own niche, useless in others)<br /> <br /> Drawback being they can't enter any other type. Changeling boons do nothing, Demon (Descent and Inferno) pacts fail to find purchase, etc to a dragon other than a Pledge being enacted. Also Draconic pledges focus on intent than action. If either party has intent to sabotage the other while the pledge is being enacted, it fails.<br /> <br /> This is mostly due to two reasons:<br /> <br /> The first highlighting the ideal of the dragon being the avatar of unyielding truth and raw meaning and thus someone who doesn't have their heart in the words that they are saying isn't someone worth trucking with.<br /> <br /> the second is the meta concept of that Pledges completed for the Immutable are their ladder for exp and this provides a comfort to the player that he/she is not going to screwed immediately on the other party not being genuine on a archetype that bases it's power on being genuine.<br /> <br /> Lastly, an appropriate drawback the dragon when he/she fails a Pledge. Was toying with the idea of removing the number of attributes being erased for the timespan of the Pledge or 30 days (whichever is longer) with the complete wipe of her breath track. A dragon who has one pledge gets +2 attributes, breaking it removes -2 for 30 days and loses all the current breath she has. Not big of an issue for a Immutable at low level but when a Immutable who starts to fail pledge after pledge, they can easily end up on death's door.<br /> <br /> But if we want to weakened this power still, we can still have the Dragon enter into Pacts/Changeling Pledges/etc but any promise with them in it is judged by Intent rather the Letter which is still quite powerful.<br /> <br /> Again, this is just a few thoughts and not the final thoughts on the matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 07-11-2017, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T19:21:11-07:00","id":1114363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1114053#post1114053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SOMETHING ABOUT WORKING ON REDOING THE PHILOSOPHIES FROM SCRATCH</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh god, please no... Releasing that chapter is literally one of the next three things on my TODO list, and it's almost done... (the other two are these dev-hell <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1o8khkgxWiuaRbLcw0AXr8MV1GlQ2ZEQQoB2BX2hs61k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Purview</span></a> and <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-mjT33mm_ht38d0nvw49YOpjF2G4eDx5YxcKWV-3V_Y/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Deep One</span></a> writeups...) We'll look at what you've written in our next meeting, which will be to finalize the Philosophy list, but I should be clear: we are literally in the process of readying <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_UPcMgovOnJ3WSs_3aAEDP_7ZlfIAbCsgDbKF0rHlig/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Chapter 2</span></a> for proofreading and release, so if you want to throw us ideas your time is better spent on smaller things or on the World Building of the Storyteller's guide which we are still a little ways from...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1114355#post1114355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">idle thought: The way things are looking, this might as well be Dragon: The Existential Crisis</div> </div> </div> </div>...Yeah, that's about a third of the mid and late game...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1114355#post1114355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling boons do nothing, Demon (Descent and Inferno) pacts fail to find purchase, etc to a dragon other than a Pledge being enacted. Also Draconic pledges focus on intent than action. If either party has intent to sabotage the other while the pledge is being enacted, it fails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... What if I added some component to the philosophies where they could actively subvert or alter the use of other powers based on their philosophies...?<br /> <br /> Like, what if Blood had the power to FORCE supernatural deals like that to be held to intent instead of letter? What if Sweat could give bonuses to their others? We were toying with the idea of how we could give the Philosophies more potency, but all we've added so far was giving them an innate sense of things, and the ability to add their Heartstring to certain social traits, so we could use something that becomes potent with non-dragon magic...<br /> <br /> Edit: this is hilarious: the first person to click that Deep One link I hid in there is listed as &quot;Anonymous Kraken&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-10-2017, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T20:46:41-07:00","id":1114390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RockstarRaccoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1114363#post1114363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh god, please no... Releasing that chapter is literally one of the next two things on my TODO list, and it's almost done...<br /> <br /> Edit: just to be clear, we'll look at what you've written, but we are literally in the process of readying <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_UPcMgovOnJ3WSs_3aAEDP_7ZlfIAbCsgDbKF0rHlig/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Chapter 2</a> for proofreading and release, so your time is better spent elsewhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>Speak of the devil and he will appear. When I was last with the project, I was tasked with trying to find how the philosophies in terms of what the direction the game was going (and namely how Dragons obtain Breath). A series of life events happened and the project fell off the radar until someone tried to get ahold of me.<br /> <br /> Now seeing that original goal through (As late as it is), I present a system that ties innately with Beats and Aspirations that in turn ties nicely with theme of building one's Legend as well as a way to obtain Breath (if it isn't the main way to do so) with a few perks that can be expanded upon later.<br /> <br /> Now granted this so late in the process that it most likely will not be included but can exist as a hack to flesh out later as there is always a new edition.<br /> <br /> As for time spent elsewhere, I'll look the current state and collect my notes. I have time available in the upcoming weekend to discuss if you want.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-10T21:05:52-07:00","id":1114398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1114390#post1114390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speak of the devil and he will appear.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=E0Ozyshpmno\" target=\"_blank\">Yep, that's me</a>. &gt;:|<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I was last with the project, I was tasked with trying to find how the philosophies in terms of what the direction the game was going (and namely how Dragons obtain Breath). </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I'd forgotten about that...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> until someone tried to get ahold of me. </div> </div> </div>Me again. :|<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I present a system that ties innately with Beats and Aspirations that in turn ties nicely with theme of building one's Legend as well as a way to obtain Breath (if it isn't the main way to do so) with a few perks that can be expanded upon later. Now granted this so late in the process that it most likely will not be included but can exist as a hack to flesh out later as there is always a new edition. </div> </div> </div>It's appreciated, and I'll look for a way to use some of that, but yeah, it's a bit late to fold stuff like that in... Remember, this project has a lot of focus on, not simply crowdsourcing as the previous ones did, but trying to distill the previous material down into a well-reconciled set of internally-consistent rules... And sure, I'm sure in a few years someone else will pick this up for another rewrite: I'm already seeing a couple missed opportunities and things that could've been done better with our version that it's now too late to fix... I just don't want to be designing this thing for another year: there's always going to be new ideas that can be added, but eventually you have to get it done with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have time available in the upcoming weekend to discuss if you want. </div> </div> </div>Alright! You're still in the Skype group, so we'll have a meeting this weekend. :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T03:15:20-07:00","id":1114500,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><b>Team Application</b></span></span><br /> <br /> Suppose I'd be interested in being a <b>playtester</b>, but I'm not entirely sure what would go into making one of the Orobori. From what I've been reading of it so far it seems to be something along the lines of, you slew a dragon, and had the brilliant idea of consuming it's supernatural power source (in this case, it's heart) and you became the thing you slew, kind of. Which means to me that most characters would likely be either Hunters or Heroes, as those are the most likely groups of mortals to deal with the supernatural in the first place. There's no being born into being an Orobori, if I am recalling correctly (some of this is based off the original book). Character concepts are something I usually work on for a good while (I've spent weeks working on Ophelia, my shadowrun latent drake) because I generally prefer to do things right. Usually it helps if I know the GM that's running the game and the type of game that they want to run (Because, seriously, you can run pretty much any kind of splat in wildly different ways). I know you likely have way too many playtesters, so I doubt this really is what you are looking for, but eh. I do like heavy roleplay focused games, less focused on say.. combat. If I wanted to play a high-fantasy combat simulator I'd be playing D&amp;D, where turning into a dragon is only one of the many things you can do at high levels. But no, I like my gritty, semi-realistic world where fantastic things happen and you have to roleplay how your character handles and interacts with them.<br /> <br /> As for the why would I be interested, I've always been intrigued by dragons. Just a quirk of mine. I've read or watched many of the modern fiction, mythology, etc. Not all of it, of course, but a decent amount I've gone out of my way to read for myself. Though I will say that Dragon and the George was a book I kind of got bored of really quickly unfortunately as the protagonist didn't feel that... draconic. His dragon form seems to have gotten forgotten the second he remembered he could into the human form, and then it hardly ever showed up from then on. Really disappointed me.<br /> <br /> I've worked on my own side-project before, a Drake Rework for Shadowrun. Sadly the Catalyst forums went down so I've never felt the need to finish proofing it with nowhere to post it. Though I did go and do a fuck load of research on drakes for that rework document. I doubt it's anything quite on the scale of this project, but who knows, I may be able to contribute in some small way. Even if it's just being a slightly above-average roleplayer.<br /> <br /> So I suppose if you want to have me on the team, send me a PM with the contact details. Otherwise, I'll just patiently wait and see if this project gets finalized and maybe hope into a game after it's development elapses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 07-11-2017, 06:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T08:46:21-07:00","id":1114607,"title":"","content":"Yoouuu are writing long paragraphs that make me not want to read until I'm more awake than I am now... And that makes me hesitant to put you on something right away.... But we're talking about you in the Skype and we know what to do with you, (gonna make you proofread) and it seems like a promising application.<br /> <br /> This is probably <b>ACCEPTED</b>. PM me you Skype name and I'll get back to you when I get to my computer...<br /> <br /> Edit: actually, we don't really have anyone clambering to playtest this. Mostly it's been tested through raw math and simulations... It's a thing I'd rather have had more people to help with earlier, like art...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-11-2017, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T10:06:23-07:00","id":1114654,"title":"","content":"Ok, gonna look over this in more detail.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1114500#post1114500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've been reading of it so far it seems to be something along the lines of, you slew a dragon, and had the brilliant idea of consuming it's supernatural power source (in this case, it's heart) and you became the thing you slew, kind of. Which means to me that most characters would likely be either Hunters or Heroes, as those are the most likely groups of mortals to deal with the supernatural in the first place. There's no being born into being an Orobori, if I am recalling correctly</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily Hunters or Heroes. We have a Usurper template in the works of someone who is being called by the heart and attempting to Usurp it, and only one of then methods outright requires an active act of killing. Inheritors are straight up given their hearts. The most important thing about becoming an Oroboros is that <i>you chose that path</i>: moreso than any other supernatural creature, the Oroboroi cannot deny that this was something they did for themselves, as being a Usurper is a major undertaking in ones life and the hearts 1) call out to people who want them and 2) do not take people who don't want them. That was something we stressed for the darker mood of this game. The only group to not choose that path is Pilot Lights, and they are rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (some of this is based off the original book) </div> </div> </div>Most of this is based off of Second Edition and the other Embers books, just reinterpreted and revised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Character concepts are something I usually work on for a good while (I've spent weeks working on Ophelia, my shadowrun latent drake) because I generally prefer to do things right. Usually it helps if I know the GM that's running the game and the type of game that they want to run (Because, seriously, you can run pretty much any kind of splat in wildly different ways). </div> </div> </div>In this case, we need data on how people interpret and use this material without our input.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know you likely have way too many playtesters, so I doubt this really is what you are looking for </div> </div> </div>We don't have enough playtesters... or artists for that matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do like heavy roleplay focused games, less focused on say.. combat. If I wanted to play a high-fantasy combat simulator I'd be playing D&amp;D, where turning into a dragon is only one of the many things you can do at high levels. But no, I like my gritty, semi-realistic world where fantastic things happen and you have to roleplay how your character handles and interacts with them. </div> </div> </div>...That's what this game is about, actually, so you're here...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the why would I be interested, I've always been intrigued by dragons. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Dragons are good. :V<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dragon and the George was a book I kind of got bored of really quickly unfortunately as the protagonist didn't feel that... draconic. His dragon form seems to have gotten forgotten the second he remembered he could into the human form, and then it hardly ever showed up from then on. </div> </div> </div>It's more about the magic he can do, and more specifically the power he can wield, and the Dragon thing is a metaphor for that. The stories are about someone who is thrust into power and how they use their power. This new version of Dragon is primarily about that, how you utilize immense amounts of power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've worked on my own side-project before, a Drake Rework for Shadowrun. Sadly the Catalyst forums went down so I've never felt the need to finish proofing it with nowhere to post it. </div> </div> </div>You could just post it on another forum then....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I did go and do a fuck load of research on drakes for that rework document. I doubt it's anything quite on the scale of this project, but who knows, I may be able to contribute in some small way. Even if it's just being a slightly above-average roleplayer. </div> </div> </div>That's good to hear, you won't be confused by the references to mythology. So tell me, what do you know about the Paleolithic era, Richard Dawkins, Frederich Nietzsche, and David Icke?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I suppose if you want to have me on the team, send me a PM with the contact details. </div> </div> </div>....You can't just send me your Skype name in a PM? :P<br /> <br /> Send me your Skype name, we'll try and get together tonight or tomorrow and I'll onboard you with all the necessary reading and document access, introduce you to the team, and show you what we need you to work on...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T07:26:45-07:00","id":1118539,"title":"","content":"So... A couple things have come up that we might use some community feedback on...<br /> <br /> Philosophies - so, we have 7 instea of 5, abd while I think they're all pretty much unique while still being broad enough to cover all the bases, I'm wondering if anyone is uncomfortable with there being 7 instead of 5. We could boil it back down to the original 5, but I worry that won't be enough to have everything you want...<br /> <br /> As for differentiation, I was wanting to make sure they all had something more than a Purview (Edict) list to make the choice more meaningful. So far, we came up with giving them all the ability to sense when their philosophy is being upheld or violated and the ability to add their Heartstring to social rolls which directly reflect the philosophy's core tenants. Anyone have any feedback on that? Is is too much? Is there something else we should do?<br /> <br /> Another issue that's come up is the (dreaded) Breath garnering system, where you get breath by eating. There was a discussion as to if making them have to eat for nourishment before garnering Breath was a good nerf, or was too complicated to keep track of. Keeping in mind that you only start to really pay attention to this in extreme cases like starvation or using a large amount of Breath for something, do people think that the system described in the Transitional Rulebook is too complicated?<br /> <br /> Other than that... Still hoping to release something soon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T07:32:44-07:00","id":1118542,"title":"","content":"Do the Seven Philosophies include Void? I forgot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T07:36:24-07:00","id":1118543,"title":"","content":"It's an 8th, but most books have a bad-guy Y along with the other 5. Embers has always had like, 12, with 2 true hearts, 5 normal ones, and the 5 evils. The 7 normal ones we have written down are...<br /> Ash - Destruction<br /> Blood - Virtue<br /> Bone - Stability<br /> Coin - Materialism<br /> Sweat - Creation<br /> Tears - Emotion<br /> Tome - Knowledge<br /> <br /> There's also one for Undecided and Void... They're in the Transitional Rulebook. It's a concept that hasn't really changed in the past year...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 07-20-2017, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T11:43:01-07:00","id":1119046,"title":"","content":"Then I would suggest starting to flesh them out and remove the ones we feel are either redundant or with too little to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T11:12:00-08:00","id":1274742,"title":"","content":"OwO what's this? <br /> <br /> So, uh, I used to be Gepetto887 many years (and more than a few email addresses) ago, and... Wow. I still remember how this first started to take root over an exchange of PMs between Shock and myself, before one of us (Shock, I think) made the initial thread and the ball got rolling. It's astounding to see that the project kept going strong for so long, and has developed so far. <br /> <br /> I'm honestly having trouble finding the right words to use here. This is bringing back a lot of memories. <br /> <br /> Thank you to everyone who found this project worth continuing, and especially to Shock for carrying on after I dropped the ball and vanished all those years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24885-callmesalticidae","name":"Callmesalticidae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T15:30:02-08:00","id":1281586,"title":"","content":"<b>TEAM APPLICATION</b><br /> <br /> Position: Playtester<br /> <br /> While I'm applying as a Playtester, I'm also quite capable of writing decently-well-worded paragraphs and stories. My main concern isn't my skill, but my availability. That said, if it becomes necessary, or I have some free time, I can write stuff for the book. I'll go ahead and fulfill both requirements below.<br /> <br /> <b>WORK SAMPLES</b><br /> <br /> Character Concept: Gabriel the Refined.<br /> Roughly thirty years ago, in the year of 1992, a tall, thin man with shoulder-length silver hair(quite obviously dyed) sits alone in his bedroom, surrounded by paintings. He hasn't managed much in his life. Despite his parents pushing him through college, a degree in Art History hasn't done much for him in the workplace. He refuses any job his parents offer to help him land, believing ordinary jobs to be beneath him. Besides, they would be shackles upon his very soul, for they would keep him away from his truest calling.<br /> <br /> Gabriel's one true skill lies in his craft. He is a painter, and his art reflects the beauty and majesty of what he believes to be the most elegant form ever devised by mankind - the Dragons. The shimmering scales, their inner magic, the nigh infinite variety of their wings! Nothing else was more worthy of his brush, and nothing else filled up more of his room, and it was this skill that ultimately won him his Heart.<br /> <br /> Displaying his art in a local festival earned him the attention of a particular Orobori, well aged and looking to die. He asked Gabriel about his designs, and the fervor with which he proselytized their inherent beauty was enough for the old dragon to know he'd appreciate the gift he was to be given.<br /> <br /> Now equipped with the mystical powers of the Dragons, (and a bit of an inheritance from his Heart's previous holder), he's managed to accrue quite a following. While he wouldn't dream of parting with his own works(for he sees them as a part of his very soul), he leaves his work on display for all to see, and is regularly commissioned to teach classes, and to draw more works of his own. From his fans, those who manage to impress him are secreted away to his private villa, where they may bask in the light of his True Form, a large, snake-like silver dragon, and learn at the feet of the master.<br /> <br /> <br /> Writing Sample: &quot;She's not really that different from one of us.&quot;<br /> &quot;What do you mean 'not different'? She's literally a Wyrm. That's about as Wyrm-tainted as you can get.&quot;<br /> &quot;She doesn't smell like a Wyrm. She smells more like a fae.&quot;<br /> &quot;It's still unnatural.<br /> <br /> The muffled voices at the edge of Melissa's perception carried her to awareness. She tried to force her eyes open, but it felt like weights had been tied to her eyelashes, making the effort difficult. <i>Was I drugged?</i> She wanted nothing more than to go back to sleep, but she was sitting on a wooden floor, in a room with three people she didn't recognize - two men, and one woman. She tried to stand, only to feel the tension of the ropes that bound her. Her Heart beat powerfully in her chest, and she could feel that the energy she had spent fighting those strange wolf-monsters returning to her. Part of her was grateful she hadn't yet cut out the powerful muscle, so she still had some fire in her that might help her escape. Most of her wished the thing was safe at home rather than here.<br /> <br /> The woman, a small thing with firey-red hair that hung to her shoulders, bounced her way over to where Melissa lay, knealing down beside her. &quot;Well goodie! You're awake! We got some questions for ya, missy. I'd pick your answers carefully.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Qualifications: </b>Well, I'm a professional game designer to start. I work for ODAM Publishing, and I actually just finished revamping their core rulebook for a 2nd Edition. Unfortunately, very little of my work for them is public yet, aside from a few specific playtesting documents that themselves require a Non-Disclosure Agreement before I can share them. Even then, I would only want to do that for the purpose OF playtesting. My point though, is I have experience in this field, having designed a game before, that specifically dealt with Dreams and reality-warping nonsense.<br /> <br /> I've also been writing since like, high school. Mostly forum roleplays, but I've also got a college degree with an emphasis on English so...yeah. That's a thing.<br /> <br /> My roleplaying-game knowledge covers a good breadth of subjects, from Exalted, to Star Wars, to Pathfinder, to Maid RPG, and that's proven to be a great boon in my field.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Why I Want to Join: </b><br /> <br /> As previously mentioned, I've been playing roleplaying games for years, and managed to recently wrangle myself a job as a professional game dev. I also wound up dragging in a friend of mine, due to her exceptional writerly abilities, and editorial prowess. Trouble is, all of her previous experience with tabletop games have been rather horrid, mostly owing to lengthy character creation processes, and a poor set of players. She doesn't like lengthy maths, or generally feeling stupid for not knowing things. Given that game design is her JOB now, which she doesn't intend on quitting, this lack of experience with gaming is a bit of an issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> As one of her closest friends, who understands what she does and doesn't like, the responsibility of trying to introduce her to our hobby in a safe enviornment falls to me. I didn't want to start her off with Pathfinder or D&amp;D or anything like that - she's much more interested in narrative than combat or gaming crunchiness. She does need some room to learn these things though. I needed a system, so I settled on Chronicles of Darkness, which tends to have a roughly even split between narrative elements and gamey-strategy-things, and the stats rarely go above 10.<br /> <br /> Which ultimately led me to you guys. My friend LOVES dragons. (I mean, I do to, but this isn't about me.) And that's one of the most important elements of playing these games - being excited about the plot, the world, and the characters. This was an excellent way to do this. I told her a bit about the lore, and she loved it(especially True Hearts.) Even if the system has a few holes in it by nature of being an in-development fan game, I'm a skilled enough GM to patch over them as I go.<br /> <br /> Which brings me here. I'm in the process of reading all of the currently released Dragon: The Embers material old and new, and I intend on running a game for her once I know all there is to know, both old and new. I figured that, as long as I'm doing so, I might as well try to hand feedback over to you guys. I'm a pretty big fan of what you guys have accomplished, and I want to see it shine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25003-witchling","user":"Witchling","date":".  Real writers revise. So my Creative Writing teacher told me. 01-22-2019, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25003-witchling","name":"Witchling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T10:52:56-07:00","id":1374939,"title":"","content":"<b>Potential Update</b><br /> So like, obviously stuff fell apart here at some point. I had a move, a job change, etc, and this just kinda fell by the wayside for so long...<br /> <br /> We were really happy with what we had, but we just didn't get to the point of putting it in the format we wanted before things got dropped. We've been talking about reviving this though, and I'd really like for y'all to see what we have here, so... Hopefully there will be an update soon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T13:50:56-07:00","id":1375143,"title":"","content":"I'm still there should this be revived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T19:22:29-07:00","id":1375208,"title":"","content":"I'm here too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key"