stagnation and madness, whereas Dragon si more about ambition and powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Good to know. Consider me signed. Now i'm wondering just how will The Oroboroi interact with the Wicked tribe. Will Leviathans be seen as some pitch-dark mirror to themselves? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T08:33:24-07:00","id":1462655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1462627#post1462627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah! Good to know. Consider me signed. Now i'm wondering just how will The Oroboroi interact with the Wicked tribe. Will Leviathans be seen as some pitch-dark mirror to themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure, it's been a while since I've checked the Crossover section of the available docs (or that could just be my memory going on the fritz again).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T18:57:48-07:00","id":1464447,"title":"","content":"Is it me, or does Dragon have a bit in common with Beast? I think the former has a more interesting premise to be sure...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T23:06:24-07:00","id":1464462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1464447#post1464447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me, or does Dragon have a bit in common with Beast? I think the former has a more interesting premise to be sure...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, Beast is more street level, and abt being a living nightmare creature. Dragon is abt being a creature off literal power, and how you use it. It's also much larger in scale, kinda like an RTS(I think).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T07:51:36-07:00","id":1464513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1464447#post1464447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me, or does Dragon have a bit in common with Beast? I think the former has a more interesting premise to be sure...</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in a superficial sense. Dragon has more in common with Mummy: the Curse, if anything.<br /> <br /> Also, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1437975-similarities-between-beast-and-fan-game-lines\">you already discussed this and got answers.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-19-2021, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T15:51:42-07:00","id":1464928,"title":"","content":"Right...except both are beings litteraly born from dreams, have themes of finding purpose, and have mechanics based on feeding. In fact the Reimagining mechanics of Dragon feel alot better than the Kinship mechanics of Beasts, in that for the former it's unintentional on the Dragon's part a sign of how tied they are to humanity's perception of their myths and doesn't come off as blatant crossover hooks like the latter, along with being a pretty massive loophole in regards towards feeding, which sorta weakens the Beast's main concept of monsters needing to feed...which was cribbed from vampire irregardless. In a way I kinda wish we could combine the two: monsters litterly born from myths that hold less meaning in the modern world and are struggling with their relevance. Needing to cause fear is just one way of trying to maintain their myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T21:33:44-07:00","id":1464963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1464928#post1464928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right...except both are beings litteraly born from dreams, have themes of finding purpose, and have mechanics based on feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Dreams&quot; in Beast are the interior of the soul, working with potent psychic real estate bridging the gap between universal ideas from the world itself and the resonant archetypes of culture in the collective human unconscious. I cannot make the same claim about Dragon, because its engagement with dreams and culture is\u2026 extremely vague.<br /> <br /> Beast does not have a theme of finding purpose. Beast has establishing place as its main common long-term project to lean into if you want more than the basic mechanical loop of feeding your Hunger while other story beats are going on. I can only take your word for it that Dragon has this theme, because when I last checked the Drive folders the book was a long way from coherently assembled and what I remember of previous editions did little to impress upon me what Dragons do.<br /> <br /> &quot;Having mechanics based on feeding&quot; is extremely not a useful comparison for exactly the reason that Family Dinner is a thing: <i>lots of monsters have stuff they feel driven to do</i> in this franchise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact the Reimagining mechanics of Dragon feel alot better than the Kinship mechanics of Beasts, </div> </div> </div>Your preference is not an argument. You're valid to have it, but it's not a persuasive statement in itself. It is important that you understand that if you have any intention of making a good-faith comparison between Beast and Dragon, and it <i>really doesn't look like you have that intention</i> when the rest of your post reads the way it does.<br /> <br /> The comparable aspect of Beast to the Reimagining isn't Kinship, it's Anathema and to a lesser extent Destabilization, because the type of dream-creature the Begotten are is not fundamentally a human invention and leaning into the parts of them that are is something that takes effort and/or resources, which suits a type of monster specifically made by naturalizing something from outside human culture into the stuff of legends and nightmares. Psychic interference with your metaphysical state is an imposition from outside actors and/or a consequence of overreaching rather than part of your everyday existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in that for the former it's unintentional on the Dragon's part a sign of how tied they are to humanity's perception of their myths and doesn't come off as blatant crossover hooks like the latter, along with being a pretty massive loophole in regards towards feeding, which sorta weakens the Beast's main concept of monsters needing to feed </div> </div> </div>&quot;Monsters need to feed, so your main alternative to feeding is to accompany another monster while they feed&quot; is not a loophole when <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1422382-legend-embellishment-and-the-siege-of-the-bright-dream-assorted-brainstorming?p=1443087#post1443087\">the thing that you are comes from the part of the universal soul where everything is part of a bigger umbrella category</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...which was cribbed from vampire irregardless. </div> </div> </div>Werewolves eat people, changelings pull the sentiment out of people, the Bound eat ghosts, mages chase the dragon of understanding esoteric phenomena in dangerous ways, mummies steal and destroy relics/eat people/pull inspiration out of the world, Prometheans rip the experience out of each other, deviants scourge people who gave them half a reason to, and &quot;feeding&quot; in Beast can run the gamut from cannibalism to grand larceny to petty assertion of dominance. Vampires do not have a monopoly on feeding mechanics and the feeding mechanics of Vampire resemble the feeding mechanics of Beast basically not at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Mummy comparison, meanwhile\u2026<br /> <br /> Dragons have removed their internal organs to live forever, use powerful god-magic, draw upon the imagery of a type of monster variously known for dwelling in dangerous places full of treasure, and owe their modern state to a deal with cosmic devils that means a lot of people want to kill them and take their stuff. It's by no means perfect, but it's got more legs to stand on as a comparison than it probably should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T03:38:59-07:00","id":1464991,"title":"","content":"Yeah, please let's keep the Beast-bashing away from here. This isn't what this thread is about. And I agree with Satchel that the comparison between Reimagining and Kinship is a weird one, given they are two completely different things that have nothing to do mechanic-wise (Kinship are beneficial abilities used by Beasts to interact with other supernatural beings; the Reimagining is a <i>weakness</i> representing how Dragons can lose control over their form)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T12:13:47-07:00","id":1465023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darinas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1464991#post1464991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, please let's keep the Beast-bashing away from here. This isn't what this thread is about. And I agree with Satchel that the comparison between Reimagining and Kinship is a weird one, given they are two completely different things that have nothing to do mechanic-wise (Kinship are beneficial abilities used by Beasts to interact with other supernatural beings; the Reimagining is a <i>weakness</i> representing how Dragons can lose control over their form)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T14:01:22-07:00","id":1465041,"title":"","content":"No problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11745-darinas","name":"Darinas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11745_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"486"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T03:53:41-08:00","id":1470209,"title":"","content":"I remembered that Dragon has a diverse set of inspirations. And I also found some similarities between it and American gods. <br /> Is that intentional? cuz if so then I'm impressed, if not then even more so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T04:29:27-08:00","id":1472955,"title":"","content":"Hi everyone! Sooooo... a while back I had someone ask me to make an interactive version of character sheet for what I now know is a play testing version of Dragon The Embers (of which the play testing version of the pdf is listed on my site). Not really realizing it was a play testing version I decided to rebuild the sheet from scratch. It took me a bit to get the project started, but I finally have that sheet finished and you can download it here:<br /> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/MiscNWOD/DragonTheEmbers_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/p...nteractive.pdf</a><br /> <br /> I ran across this thread now and realized that not only is there is another version of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/20836-dragon-the-embers-third-stage-development\">Dragon The Embers</a>, there is actually a reboot! I am super behind on this I guess...lol. Sorry about that...<br /> <br /> So, do you think I should try to work on a character sheet for this version of the game? Is the border and fonts I used for the for sheet I just made acceptable, or should something else be used? Any suggestions? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/610-cjc\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar610_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"610\" data-vbnamecard=\"610\">CJC</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10120_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10120\" data-vbnamecard=\"10120\">RockstarRaccoon</a> do y'all have any thoughts?<br /> <br /> If I need to work on a character sheet, I might need some help with the layout or knowing what would be needed, so if a kind soul wants to send me an email sometime with some info, it'd be much appreciated. Oh, should you need it, my email is: mrgonejediknight (@) gmail<br /> <br /> Anyway, sorry for being so late to the party...but hopefully I can help, even if it's in a small way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":24,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","user":"Mr Gone","date":". 01-22-2022, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T20:52:20-08:00","id":1473137,"title":"","content":"I'd like that, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T04:10:14-08:00","id":1473157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1473137#post1473137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like that, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'll have to see what I can do then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T14:17:56-07:00","id":1493533,"title":"","content":"*From the depths of the earth, rise again to power!*<br /> <br /> Team Application<br /> <br /> Position: Writer/Playtester<br /> <br /> Just a general note - I'm applying here and now because I was invited to a CoD crossover game that is being run by a friend of mine. The game is already populated with a few fangame characters, and upon examining the skeleton of the Dragons fangames, I was fascinated by the concepts, philosophy, and lore, especially for the ReKindled stuff. I intend to create a character with the Rekindled rules, filling in with Embers content wherever necessary, and taking a critical look at how the character plays and interacts with e.g. vampires, geniuses, and a few other CoD creatures that have not yet been revealed to me.<br /> <br /> Sample/Concept: Gunnar Cavalius is a Dragon. Well, more specifically, a being called an Oroboroi - the distinction seemed moot to him not long ago, but now, after his life has changed so drastically, he is acutely aware of what being an Oroboroi really means. The vitality in his being, the fire in his spirit, the sheer power at his fingertips - none of it truly his own, yet all of it available at his beck and call for every waking moment - would make him, or it would break him.<br /> <br /> Just a few months ago, now feeling like both yesterday and a lifetime away, Gunnar was given this power by his robber-baron CEO godmother. A firebrand who built an empire on pillars of her charming charisma, shrewd business dealings, and vicious, cutthroat ambition, she had grown weary of her historic exploits over the last few decades, until Gunnar arrived in her life. The only child of an overwhelmed personal assistant, Gunnar gave her an unexpected burst of perspective, and a strange new sense of empathy, doting on him like a grandmother would - until she disappeared and left him everything.<br /> <br /> Gunnar thinks back on that day often now, the image of the nine-chambered heart in her impossibly smooth hands, her words of encouragement, which had followed words that initially convinced Gunnar that her mind had taken all the damage of aging, though her body took none. He was almost catatonic from the revelation, until he took the gift that was offered to him, taking on a great and powerful legacy as well. One that even now, he does not understand.<br /> <br /> What he does understand, however, is how someone might grow weary in his Godmother's position. The legacy of her business was not something he wished to continue, the behemoth she had built was for him a golden prison - he may have been the leader in name, but the beast made its own decisions, took its own orders, followed its own directions, made up by committee and council and focus group. So Gunnar left it. Now, with the memory of his Gammaw almost alive in his own mind, he sets off to a new city, escaping the expectations heaped upon him in his previous life to try and create his own empire, and thus truly make use of the power that Gammaw gave him. <br /> <br /> Gunnar Cavalius is an Inheritor Dragon of the Coin philosophy. In being groomed since birth to be the replacement for his CEO godmother, he was denied the chance to be whatsoever normal. Despite that, he is fiercely loyal, though perhaps patronizingly so, to anyone that he likes. He is astonishingly arrogant, and ignorant of his intellectual shortcomings, but somehow his arrogance is infectious rather than destructive, often inspiring the humans around him to great accomplishments. Currently working in middle management, he uses this arrogance along with his draconic charisma to secure recognition and resources for himself and his team. In his personal life, he has recently stumbled upon a larger supernatural community filled with fantastic creatures of lore - will his new power allow him to claim hold in this chaotic realm, or will it drive him to madness?<br /> <br /> Qualifications: Not much! A general talent for writing and baseline knowledge of tropes, but I'm also very new to CoD/WoD content specifically. Some may consider that a boon, since fresh eyes can sometimes lend alternate perspectives, but I'll let you be the judge of that. <br /> <br /> Intent: Like I mention above, I primarily just want to run this character in my friend's supernatural kitchen sink campaign. But because of the current nature of rekindled, in order to do so, I will likely need to improvise and fill in a bit where current public work is not complete. Having the team to talk to would undoubtedly help with that, and I'm absolutely willing to both share the practical data from play as well as contribute to writing up abilities and other sections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27596-radscience","name":"RadScience","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T18:22:20-07:00","id":1509809,"title":"","content":"OI, everything going good with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T18:24:17-07:00","id":1509810,"title":"","content":"Also the <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><u><b><a href=\"http://s6.postimg.org/bfsoay0e9/Sheet_Prototype.png\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Prototype Oroboros Sheet: Image Version</span></a></b></u> - </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">doesn't work</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T18:33:08-07:00","id":1509811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot?p=1509809#post1509809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OI, everything going good with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit of idle research of going back not even five pages would tell you Rockstar hasn't touched this since 2020, and even less research would point that no one has touched this thread for about 7 months, and a little more tells you the most significant update was over a year ago. I think the context clues speak for themselves.<br /> <br /> Relatedly, do you just have a deep aversion to listening to the mods when they tell you stop necromancing old threads?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-26-2023, 09:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","r